nt Events, WebRTC\n      - **Batch**: File transfer, scheduled data exchange\n      **Security Considerations**:\n      - Transport security (TLS 1.2/1.3, certificate pinning)\n      - API authentication (API keys, OAuth, mTLS)\n      - Data encryption in transit and at rest\n      - Rate limiting and throttling\n      **Integration Standards**:\n      - API design guidelines (REST, OpenAPI, AsyncAPI)\n      - Data format standards (JSON, Protocol Buffers, Avro)\n      - Error handling and response formats\n      - Idempotency and retry handling\n  conpla:\n    prefix: CONPLA\n    subsection-types:\n      copl-item-lst:\n        max-count: 1\n    description: 12.6.2. Contingency Plans.\n  conres:\n    prefix: CONRES\n    subsection-types:\n      corep1:\n        max-count: 1\n      coreof:\n        max-count: 1\n      coreop:\n        max-count: 1\n    description: Connectivity resilience requirements.\n  coorco:\n    prefix: COORCO\n    format: coorco-form\n    description: Coupling guidance.\n  coorde:\n    prefix: COORDE\n    format: coorde-form\n    description: Dependency management rules.\n  coordo:\n    prefix: COORDO\n    format: coordo-form\n    description: Domain boundaries.\n  coorla:\n    prefix: COORLA\n    format: coorla-form\n    description: Layering rules.\n  copaas:\n    prefix: COPAAS\n    format: copaas-form\n    description: Asynchronous communication details.\n  copaob:\n    prefix: COPAOB\n    format: copaob-form\n    description: Observability settings.\n  copare:\n    prefix: COPARE\n    format: copare-form\n    description: Reliability controls.\n  copasy:\n    prefix: COPASY\n    format: copasy-form\n    description: Synchronous communication details.\n  coqume:\n    prefix: COQUME\n    subsection-types:\n      cqmc:\n        max-count: 1\n      coqumeco:\n        max-count: 1\n      cqmd:\n        max-count: 1\n      cqmsa:\n        max-count: 1\n      cqmt:\n        max-count: 1\n    description: Code quality metrics and thresholds.\n  