efix: SCREVE\n    format: screve-form\n    description: Vertical scaling configuration.\n  secere:\n    prefix: SECERE\n    subsection-types:\n      scri:\n        max-count: 1\n      scrs:\n        max-count: 1\n      secerein:\n        max-count: 1\n      scrm:\n        max-count: 1\n    description: Security certification and compliance framework needs.\n  sedeli:\n    prefix: SEDELI\n    subsection-types:\n      sdld:\n        max-count: 1\n      sdlt:\n        max-count: 1\n      sdlr:\n        max-count: 1\n    description: Security development lifecycle.\n  selein:\n    prefix: SELEIN\n    subsection-types:\n      slip:\n        max-count: 1\n      sliq:\n        max-count: 1\n      slim:\n        max-count: 1\n    description: Service Level Indicators.\n  seosre:\n    prefix: SEOSRE\n    subsection-types:\n      sorh:\n        max-count: 1\n      sors:\n        max-count: 1\n      sorm:\n        max-count: 1\n      sorl:\n        max-count: 1\n    description: Operating system requirements.\n  sestre:\n    prefix: SESTRE\n    subsection-types:\n      ssrd:\n        max-count: 1\n      ssrfs:\n        max-count: 1\n      ssrb:\n        max-count: 1\n      ssrp:\n        max-count: 1\n    description: Storage requirements.\n  seteau:\n    prefix: SETEAU\n    subsection-types:\n      stad:\n        max-count: 1\n      stai:\n        max-count: 1\n      staf:\n        max-count: 1\n      stas:\n        max-count: 1\n      stag:\n        max-count: 1\n    description: "Automated security testing integration (SAST, DAST, IAST)."\n  slenop:\n    prefix: SLENOP\n    format: slenop-form\n    description: Alerting and ownership rules.\n  slenta:\n    prefix: SLENTA\n    format: slenta-form\n    description: Objective target and budget definition.\n  slmore:\n    prefix: SLMORE\n    subsection-types:\n      slmoremo:\n        max-count: 1\n      smreb:\n        max-count: 1\n      slmorecu:\n        max-count: 1\n      slmorere:\n        max-count: 1\n    description: SLA monitoring.\n  smaglb:\n    prefix: SMAGLB\n    format: smaglb-form\n    description: Load balancing and termination rules.\n  stcose:\n    prefix: STCOSE\n    subsection-types:\n      itstco-itst-lst:\n        max-count: 1\n      inprco-indu-lst:\n        max-count: 1\n      intspe-inte-lst:\n        max-count: 1\n      rce-regu-lst:\n        max-count: 1\n      sestco-secu-lst:\n        max-count: 1\n      accstd-acce-lst:\n        max-count: 1\n      qlstd-qual-lst:\n        max-count: 1\n      dostse:\n        max-count: 1\n      costse:\n        max-count: 1\n      cerese:\n        max-count: 1\n      covese:\n        max-count: 1\n    description: |\n      Specify compliance requirements with IT standards, industry protocols,\n      regulatory frameworks, and certification requirements. Standards compliance\n      is often mandatory for enterprise and regulated industries.\n      **IT Standards**:\n      - **ISO/IEC**: 27001 (InfoSec), 9001 (Quality), 22301 (Business Continuity),\n        25010 (Software Quality), 12207 (Lifecycle)\n      - **IEEE**: 830 (Requirements), 1471 (Architecture), 29148 (Requirements)\n      - **NIST**: Cybersecurity Framework, SP 800-53 controls\n      **Industry Protocols**:\n      - **API**: REST, GraphQL, gRPC, OpenAPI/Swagger specifications\n      - **Data**: JSON, XML, Protocol Buffers, Avro schemas\n      - **Security**: OAuth 2.0, OIDC, SAML, JWT, mTLS\n      - **Messaging**: AMQP, MQTT, WebSocket, Server-Sent Events\n      **Regulatory Compliance**:\n      - **Privacy**: GDPR, CCPA, PIPEDA, LGPD, HIPAA\n      - **Financial**: PCI-DSS, SOX, Basel III\n      - **Industry**: FedRAMP, HITRUST, PSD2, MiFID II\n      **Certification Requirements**:\n      - SOC 2 Type I/II\n      - ISO 27001 certification\n      - Industry-specific certifications\n      - Third-party security assessments\n  syarsp:\n    prefix: SYARSP\n    description: System architecture (new in Phase A).\n  sycoma:\n    prefix: SYCOMA\n    subsection-types:\n      scmd:\n        max-count: 1\n      scme:\n        max-count: 1\n      scmg:\n        max-count: 1\n      scset-sett-lst:\n        max-count: 1\n    description: Configuration management.\n  sydito:\n    prefix: SYDITO\n    subsection-types:\n      sdtt:\n        max-count: 1\n      sdtl:\n        max-count: 1\n      sdtss:\n        max-count: 1\n    description: System diagnostic tools.\n  teengo:\n    prefix: TEENGO\n    format: teengo-form\n    description: Architecture governance context.\n  teenne:\n    prefix: TEENNE\n    subsection-types:\n      teenne-devo-lst:\n        max-count: 1\n      teenne-obse-lst:\n        max-count: 1\n    description: Network and infrastructure standards.\n  teenst:\n    prefix: TEENST\n    format: teenst-form\n    description: Platform standards and preferred technologies.\n  testor:\n    prefix: TESTOR\n    format: testor-form\n    description: Additional test types and organization.\n  testpa:\n    prefix: TESTPA\n    format: testpa-form\n    description: Preferred testing patterns.\n  testqu:\n    prefix: TESTQU\n    format: testqu-form\n    description: Quality requirements for tests.\n  testto:\n    prefix: TESTTO\n    format: testto-form\n    description: Testing tools and CI integration.\n  tlreco:\n    prefix: TLRECO\n    format: tlreco-form\n    description: Compliance and HSTS settings.\n  tlrete:\n    prefix: TLRETE\n    format: tlrete-form\n    description: Termination and internal encryption.\n  trareq:\n    prefix: TRAREQ\n    subsection-types:\n      trareq-tran:\n        max-count: 1\n      trrert:\n        max-count: 1\n      trrefo:\n        max-count: 1\n      trreva:\n        max-count: 1\n      trrete:\n        max-count: 1\n    description: Translation handling requirements (whole).\n  trcaac:\n    prefix: TRCAAC\n    format: trcaac-form\n    description: Break-glass and diagnostic access controls.\n  trcaco:\n    prefix: TRCACO\n    format: trcaco-form\n    description: Incident communication and retrospective support.\n  trcaru:\n    prefix: TRCARU\n    format: trcaru-form\n    description: Runbook and remediation support.\n  trrefo:\n    prefix: TRREFO\n    format: trrefo-form\n    description: Locale-specific formatting rules.\n  trrert:\n    prefix: TRRERT\n    format: trrert-form\n    description: RTL and bidirectional support.\n  trrete:\n    prefix: TRRETE\n    format: trrete-form\n    description: Technical text and font support.\n  trreva:\n    prefix: TRREVA\n    format: trreva-form\n    description: Pluralization and variants.\n  usgrpr:\n    prefix: USGRPR\n    subsection-types:\n      ugpf:\n        max-count: 1\n      ugps:\n        max-count: 1\n      ugpt:\n        max-count: 1\n    description: User growth projections.\n  usprto:\n    prefix: USPRTO\n    subsection-types:\n      uptl:\n        max-count: 1\n      uptrm:\n        max-count: 1\n      uptdi:\n        max-count: 1\n    description: User provisioning and management tools.\n  usrset:\n    prefix: USRSET\n    subsection-types:\n      usset-sett-lst:\n        max-count: 1\n    description: Server-persisted settings that follow the user across devices (CE-UP).\n  vecoco:\n    prefix: VECOCO\n    subsection-types:\n      vccr:\n        max-count: 1\n      vccb:\n        max-count: 1\n      vccc:\n        max-count: 1\n      vccm:\n        max-count: 1\n    description: Version control configuration.\n  vireco:\n    prefix: VIRECO\n    format: vireco-form\n    description: Container requirements.\n  vireku:\n    prefix: VIREKU\n    format: vireku-form\n    description: Kubernetes requirements.\n  virene:\n    prefix: VIRENE\n    format: virene-form\n    description: Networking requirements.\n  virevm:\n    prefix: VIREVM\n    format: virevm-form\n    description: VM requirements.\n  vumapo:\n    prefix: VUMAPO\n    subsection-types:\n      vmpc:\n        max-count: 1\n      vmpp:\n        max-count: 1\n      vmpr:\n        max-count: 1\n    description: Vulnerability management.\n  apmus:\n    prefix: APMUS\n    format: apmus-form\n    description: User and synthetic monitoring settings.\n  bjmjt:\n    prefix: BJMJT\n    description: "Describe the shape of the scheduled workload in a short paragraph: what the batch surface of this system is mostly made of, and why it exists. This is orientation, not the job inventory — every job is declared individually in Scheduled Jobs (SCJOB). Do not list jobs here; a list in two places is a list that can disagree with itself."\n  bmsfu:\n    prefix: BMSFU\n    format: bmsfu-form\n    description: Feature adoption and engagement metrics.\n  btcbs:\n    prefix: BTCBS\n    format: btcbs-form\n    description: Build system settings.\n  btccf:\n    prefix: BTCCF\n    format: btccf-form\n    description: Configuration and plugins.\n  btcvr:\n    prefix: BTCVR\n    format: btcvr-form\n    description: Version requirements.\n  btreq:\n    prefix: BTREQ\n    subsection-types:\n      pllng:\n        max-count: 1\n      as:\n        max-count: 1\n      dpas:\n        max-count: 1\n    description: |\n      Define the foundational technical requirements that govern all system\n      development. These decisions have far-reaching implications and should\n      be made early with careful stakeholder alignment.\n      **Subsections**:\n      - **Platform and Language**: Runtime environments, programming languages,\n        frameworks, build toolchain, deployment targets\n      - **Architecture Style**: Monolith, microservices, serverless, or hybrid;\n        component organization; communication patterns; scalability approach\n      - **Design Patterns and Standards**: Required patterns, coding standards,\n        industry compliance (ISO, OWASP, IEEE), quality metrics\n      **Decision Criteria**:\n      - Business requirements alignment (performance, availability, cost)\n      - Team capabilities and hiring market\n      - Ecosystem maturity and vendor support\n      - Long-term maintainability and evolution\n      - Regulatory and compliance requirements\n      **Reference Frameworks**: TOGAF, C4 Model, ISO/IEC 25010 (quality model),\n      OWASP guidelines, IEEE 1471 architectural description.\n  ccprb:\n    prefix: CCPRB\n    format: ccprb-form\n    description: Build stage settings.\n  ccprd:\n    prefix: CCPRD\n    format: ccprd-form\n    description: Deployment stage settings.\n  ccprn:\n    prefix: CCPRN\n    format: ccprn-form\n    description: Notification and escalation settings.\n  ccprq:\n    prefix: CCPRQ\n    format: ccprq-form\n    description: Quality gate settings.\n  cmpdp:\n    prefix: CMPDP\n    format: cmpdp-form\n    description: Deployment.\n  cmpmt:\n    prefix: CMPMT\n    format: cmpmt-form\n    description: Maturity and community.\n  cmppf:\n    prefix: CMPPF\n    format: cmppf-form\n    description: Security and performance.\n  cmpsp:\n    prefix: CMPSP\n    format: cmpsp-form\n    description: Support.\n  cmpvd:\n    prefix: CMPVD\n    format: cmpvd-form\n    description: Vendor information.\n  cmstr:\n    prefix: CMSTR\n    subsection-types:\n      csvnd:\n        max-count: 1\n      csgov:\n        max-count: 1\n      csprt:\n        max-count: 1\n      cspol:\n        max-count: 1\n      cspln:\n        max-count: 1\n      rguse-reus-lst:\n        max-count: 1\n      evcri:\n        max-count: 1\n    description: 12.1. Component Strategy.\n  cqmsa:\n    prefix: CQMSA\n    format: cqmsa-form\n    description: Static analysis thresholds.\n  cserd:\n    prefix: CSERD\n    format: cserd-form\n    description: Rule description.\n  csgov:\n    prefix: CSGOV\n    format: csgov-form\n    description: Governance and evaluation process.\n  cspln:\n    prefix: CSPLN\n    format: cspln-form\n    description: Budget and pilot planning.\n  cspol:\n    prefix: CSPOL\n    format: cspol-form\n    description: Policy and baseline requirements.\n  csprt:\n    prefix: CSPRT\n    format: csprt-form\n    description: Portfolio management settings.\n  csrcp:\n    prefix: CSRCP\n    format: csrcp-form\n    description: Code protection controls.\n  csvnd:\n    prefix: CSVND\n    format: csvnd-form\n    description: Vendor preferences and exceptions.\n  dcevc:\n    prefix: DCEVC\n    format: dcevc-form\n    description: Version control requirements.\n  dfcdt:\n    prefix: DFCDT\n    format: dfcdt-form\n    description: Date and time formatting.\n  dochd:\n    prefix: DOCHD\n    description: Standard TomSpecs document header.\n  dorer:\n    prefix: DORER\n    format: dorer-form\n    description: Hardware and display requirements.\n  dores:\n    prefix: DORES\n    format: dores-form\n    description: Support prioritization.\n  doret:\n    prefix: DORET\n    format: doret-form\n    description: Testing and known issues.\n  dpaps:\n    prefix: DPAPS\n    subsection-types:\n      prreco:\n        max-count: 1\n      darere:\n        max-count: 1\n      comare:\n        max-count: 1\n      dsrm:\n        max-count: 1\n      piap:\n        max-count: 1\n      dpar:\n        max-count: 1\n      daprcl:\n        max-count: 1\n    description: |\n      Specify data protection and privacy requirements including regulatory\n      compliance, data residency, consent management, and data subject rights.\n      Privacy compliance is mandatory in most jurisdictions.\n      **Privacy Regulations**:\n      - **GDPR** (EU): Consent, data minimization, right to erasure, DPO\n      - **CCPA/CPRA** (California): Consumer rights, opt-out, data sales\n      - **LGPD** (Brazil): Similar to GDPR, data protection officer\n      - **PIPEDA** (Canada): Consent and purpose limitation\n      - **Industry-specific**: HIPAA (health), FERPA (education), GLBA (finance)\n      **Data Residency**:\n      - Geographic data storage requirements\n      - Cross-border data transfer mechanisms\n      - Data localization requirements\n      - Cloud region selection considerations\n      - Data transfer impact assessments\n      **Consent Management**:\n      - Consent collection user experience\n      - Granular consent options\n      - Consent withdrawal mechanism\n      - Consent record keeping\n      - Cookie consent management\n      **Data Subject Rights**:\n      - **Right to Access**: Export user data in portable format\n      - **Right to Rectification**: Update incorrect data\n      - **Right to Erasure**: Delete all user data (right to be forgotten)\n      - **Right to Portability**: Transfer data to another provider\n      - **Right to Object**: Opt-out of processing\n      **Privacy by Design**:\n      - Data minimization\n      - Purpose limitation\n      - Privacy impact assessments (PIA/DPIA)\n      - Privacy-preserving technologies\n  dparh:\n    prefix: DPARH\n    format: dparh-form\n    description: Data-handling details.\n  dparm:\n    prefix: DPARM\n    format: dparm-form\n    description: Agreement-management details.\n  dpars:\n    prefix: DPARS\n    format: dpars-form\n    description: Security and audit details.\n  dpart:\n    prefix: DPART\n    format: dpart-form\n    description: International-transfer details.\n  dsrma:\n    prefix: DSRMA\n    format: dsrma-form\n    description: Access and rectification handling.\n  dsrme:\n    prefix: DSRME\n    format: dsrme-form\n    description: Erasure handling.\n  dsrmo:\n    prefix: DSRMO\n    format: dsrmo-form\n    description: Operational workflow and tracking.\n  dsrmp:\n    prefix: DSRMP\n    format: dsrmp-form\n    description: Portability handling.\n  dsrmr:\n    prefix: DSRMR\n    format: dsrmr-form\n    description: Restriction and objection handling.\n  dsrsc:\n    prefix: DSRSC\n    format: dsrsc-form\n    description: Supply-chain security rules.\n  dtebo:\n    prefix: DTEBO\n    format: dtebo-form\n    description: Build output configuration.\n  dtiac:\n    prefix: DTIAC\n    format: dtiac-form\n    description: Infrastructure-as-code strategy.\n  ehsuc:\n    prefix: EHSUC\n    format: ehsuc-form\n    description: User-facing communication rules.\n  escei:\n    prefix: ESCEI\n    format: escei-form\n    description: Integration details.\n  escer:\n    prefix: ESCER\n    format: escer-form\n    description: Setup requirements.\n  esces:\n    prefix: ESCES\n    format: esces-form\n    description: Authentication and access.\n  escet:\n    prefix: ESCET\n    format: escet-form\n    description: Testing and notes.\n  evceg:\n    prefix: EVCEG\n    format: evceg-form\n    description: Scoring guidelines and scope.\n  evcep:\n    prefix: EVCEP\n    format: evcep-form\n    description: Evaluation process.\n  evces:\n    prefix: EVCES\n    format: evces-form\n    description: Scoring settings.\n  evcri:\n    prefix: EVCRI\n    subsection-types:\n      evcen-item-lst:\n        max-count: 1\n    description: 12.1.2. Evaluation Criteria.\n  fwrcp:\n    prefix: FWRCP\n    format: fwrcp-form\n    description: Compatibility.\n  fwrid:\n    prefix: FWRID\n    format: fwrid-form\n    description: Identity details.\n  fwrjt:\n    prefix: FWRJT\n    format: fwrjt-form\n    description: Justification.\n  fwrsc:\n    prefix: FWRSC\n    format: fwrsc-form\n    description: Scope and plugins.\n  fwrsp:\n    prefix: FWRSP\n    format: fwrsp-form\n    description: Support status.\n  fwrvr:\n    prefix: FWRVR\n    format: fwrvr-form\n    description: Version requirements.\n  hardr:\n    prefix: HARDR\n    format: hardr-form\n    description: Disaster recovery alignment.\n  harlb:\n    prefix: HARLB\n    format: harlb-form\n    description: Load balancing behavior.\n  hcads:\n    prefix: HCADS\n    subsection-types:\n      hechen:\n        max-count: 1\n      apdi:\n        max-count: 1\n      loagre:\n        max-count: 1\n      trca:\n        max-count: 1\n      dehemo:\n        max-count: 1\n    description: |\n      Specify health check, diagnostics, and troubleshooting requirements.\n      Health checks enable rapid problem detection and automated remediation.\n      **Health Check Types**:\n      - **Liveness**: Is the process alive? (restart if not)\n      - **Readiness**: Is the service ready for traffic? (remove from LB if not)\n      - **Startup**: Is the service still starting? (give more time)\n      - **Deep Health**: Are all dependencies healthy?\n      **Health Check Endpoints**:\n      - Standard endpoints (/health, /ready, /live)\n      - Response format (JSON with details)\n      - Performance requirements (fast, non-blocking)\n      - Authentication considerations\n      **Diagnostics Capabilities**:\n      - Real-time log access\n      - Distributed tracing\n      - Request/response capture (debug mode)\n      - Performance profiling\n      - Memory and CPU analysis\n      **Troubleshooting Tools**:\n      - Log search and filtering\n      - Trace correlation\n      - Error aggregation and analysis\n      - Dependency graph visualization\n      - Runbook integration\n      **Self-Healing**:\n      - Automatic restart on failure\n      - Circuit breaker activation\n      - Traffic rerouting\n      - Resource scaling\n      - Alerting and escalation\n  imrpi:\n    prefix: IMRPI\n    format: imrpi-form\n    description: Post-incident expectations.\n  imrwr:\n    prefix: IMRWR\n    format: imrwr-form\n    description: War room setup.\n  inris:\n    prefix: INRIS\n    format: inris-form\n    description: Inter-service communication controls.\n  ipcei:\n    prefix: IPCEI\n    format: ipcei-form\n    description: Implementation details.\n  ipces:\n    prefix: IPCES\n    format: ipces-form\n    description: Compliance scope and features.\n  ipcet:\n    prefix: IPCET\n    format: ipcet-form\n    description: Testing details.\n  irppi:\n    prefix: IRPPI\n    format: irppi-form\n    description: Post-incident activities.\n  iscee:\n    prefix: ISCEE\n    format: iscee-form\n    description: Evidence and notes.\n  isceo:\n    prefix: ISCEO\n    format: isceo-form\n    description: Ownership and support.\n  iscer:\n    prefix: ISCER\n    format: iscer-form\n    description: Control requirements.\n  isces