system settings.\n  btccf:\n    prefix: BTCCF\n    format: btccf-form\n    description: Configuration and plugins.\n  btcvr:\n    prefix: BTCVR\n    format: btcvr-form\n    description: Version requirements.\n  btreq:\n    prefix: BTREQ\n    subsection-types:\n      pllng:\n        max-count: 1\n      as:\n        max-count: 1\n      dpas:\n        max-count: 1\n    description: |\n      Define the foundational technical requirements that govern all system\n      development. These decisions have far-reaching implications and should\n      be made early with careful stakeholder alignment.\n      **Subsections**:\n      - **Platform and Language**: Runtime environments, programming languages,\n        frameworks, build toolchain, deployment targets\n      - **Architecture Style**: Monolith, microservices, serverless, or hybrid;\n        component organization; communication patterns; scalability approach\n      - **Design Patterns and Standards**: Required patterns, coding standards,\n        industry compliance (ISO, OWASP, IEEE), quality metrics\n      **Decision Criteria**:\n      - Business requirements alignment (performance, availability, cost)\n      - Team capabilities and hiring market\n      - Ecosystem maturity and vendor support\n      - Long-term maintainability and evolution\n      - Regulatory and compliance requirements\n      **Reference Frameworks**: TOGAF, C4 Model, ISO/IEC 25010 (quality model),\n      OWASP guidelines, IEEE 1471 architectural description.\n  ccprb:\n    prefix: CCPRB\n    format: ccprb-form\n    description: Build stage settings.\n  ccprd:\n    prefix: CCPRD\n    format: ccprd-form\n    description: Deployment stage settings.\n  ccprn:\n    prefix: CCPRN\n    format: ccprn-form\n    description: Notification and escalation settings.\n  ccprq:\n    prefix: CCPRQ\n    format: ccprq-form\n    description: Quality gate settings.\n  cqmsa:\n    prefix: CQMSA\n    format: cqmsa-form\n    description: Static analysis thresholds.\n  cserd:\n    prefix: CSERD\n    format: cserd-form\n    description: Rule description.\n  csrcp:\n    prefix: CSRCP\n    format: csrcp-form\n    description: Code protection controls.\n  datcl:\n    prefix: DATCL\n    subsection-types:\n      datcl-over:\n        max-count: 1\n      dclse-item-lst:\n        max-count: 1\n    description: 7.1.3. Data Classification.\n  datmd:\n    prefix: DATMD\n    subsection-types:\n      daent-enti-lst:\n        max-count: 1\n        min-count: 1\n      enrel:\n        max-count: 1\n      datcl:\n        max-count: 1\n      dadi:\n        max-count: 1\n      vaco:\n        max-count: 1\n      inco:\n        max-count: 1\n    description: Data model — CE-DB persistence + CE-VA server-side rules.\n  dcevc:\n    prefix: DCEVC\n    format: dcevc-form\n    description: Version control requirements.\n  dfcdt:\n    prefix: DFCDT\n    format: dfcdt-form\n    description: Date and time formatting.\n  dochd:\n    prefix: DOCHD\n    description: Standard TomSpecs document header.\n  domen:\n    prefix: DOMEN\n    subsection-types:\n      dmene-enum-lst:\n        max-count: 1\n    description: "Domain enum registry — the closed value sets, shared by client & server."\n  dorer:\n    prefix: DORER\n    format: dorer-form\n    description: Hardware and display requirements.\n  dores:\n    prefix: DORES\n    format: dores-form\n    description: Support prioritization.\n  doret:\n    prefix: DORET\n    format: doret-form\n    description: Testing and known issues.\n  dpaps:\n    prefix: DPAPS\n    subsection-types:\n      prreco:\n        max-count: 1\n      darere:\n        max-count: 1\n      comare:\n        max-count: 1\n      dsrm:\n        max-count: 1\n      piap:\n        max-count: 1\n      dpar:\n        max-count: 1\n      daprcl:\n        max-count: 1\n    description: |\n      Specify data protection and privacy requirements including regulatory\n      compliance, data residency, consent management, and data subject rights.\n      Privacy compliance is mandatory in most jurisdictions.\n      **Privacy Regulations**:\n      - **GDPR** (EU): Consent, data minimization, right to erasure, DPO\n      - **CCPA/CPRA** (California): Consumer rights, opt-out, data sales\n      - **LGPD** (Brazil): Similar to GDPR, data protection officer\n      - **PIPEDA** (Canada): Consent and purpose limitation\n      - **Industry-specific**: HIPAA (health), FERPA (education), GLBA (finance)\n      **Data Residency**:\n      - Geographic data storage requirements\n      - Cross-border data transfer mechanisms\n      - Data localization requirements\n      - Cloud region selection considerations\n      - Data transfer impact assessments\n      **Consent Management**:\n      - Consent collection user experience\n      - Granular consent options\n      - Consent withdrawal mechanism\n      - Consent record keeping\n      - Cookie consent management\n      **Data Subject Rights**:\n      - **Right to Access**: Export user data in portable format\n      - **Right to Rectification**: Update incorrect data\n      - **Right to Erasure**: Delete all user data (right to be forgotten)\n      - **Right to Portability**: Transfer data to another provider\n      - **Right to Object**: Opt-out of processing\n      **Privacy by Design**:\n      - Data minimization\n      - Purpose limitation\n      - Privacy impact assessments (PIA/DPIA)\n      - Privacy-preserving technologies\n  dparh:\n    prefix: DPARH\n    format: dparh-form\n    description: Data-handling details.\n  dparm:\n    prefix: DPARM\n    format: dparm-form\n    description: Agreement-management details.\n  dpars:\n    prefix: DPARS\n    format: dpars-form\n    description: Security and audit details.\n  dpart:\n    prefix: DPART\n    format: dpart-form\n    description: International-transfer details.\n  dsrma:\n    prefix: DSRMA\n    format: dsrma-form\n    description: Access and rectification handling.\n  dsrme:\n    prefix: DSRME\n    format: dsrme-form\n    description: Erasure handling.\n  dsrmo:\n    prefix: DSRMO\n    format: dsrmo-form\n    description: Operational workflow and tracking.\n  dsrmp:\n    prefix: DSRMP\n    format: dsrmp-form\n    description: Portability handling.\n  dsrmr:\n    prefix: DSRMR\n    format: dsrmr-form\n    description: Restriction and objection handling.\n  dsrsc:\n    prefix: DSRSC\n    format: dsrsc-form\n    description: Supply-chain security rules.\n  dtebo:\n    prefix: DTEBO\n    format: dtebo-form\n    description: Build output configuration.\n  dtiac:\n    prefix: DTIAC\n    format: dtiac-form\n    description: Infrastructure-as-code strategy.\n  efmef:\n    prefix: EFMEF\n    format: efmef-form\n    description: Ordering and formatting settings.\n  efmei:\n    prefix: EFMEI\n    format: efmei-form\n    description: Inclusion and defaults.\n  efmel:\n    prefix: EFMEL\n    format: efmel-form\n    description: Fixed-width and quoting rules.\n  efmet:\n    prefix: EFMET\n    format: efmet-form\n    description: Transformation rules.\n  ehsuc:\n    prefix: EHSUC\n    format: ehsuc-form\n    description: User-facing communication rules.\n  enrel:\n    prefix: ENREL\n    subsection-types:\n      enrle-item-lst:\n        max-count: 1\n    description: 7.1.2. Entity Relationships.\n  ercrg:\n    prefix: ERCRG\n    subsection-types:\n      ercen-code-lst:\n        max-count: 1\n    description: Error code registry — CE-ER shared error-code vocabulary.\n  escei:\n    prefix: ESCEI\n    format: escei-form\n    description: Integration details.\n  escer:\n    prefix: ESCER\n    format: escer-form\n    description: Setup requirements.\n  esces:\n    prefix: ESCES\n    format: esces-form\n    description: Authentication and access.\n  escet:\n    prefix: ESCET\n    format: escet-form\n    description: Testing and notes.\n  fwrcp:\n    prefix: FWRCP\n    format: fwrcp-form\n    description: Compatibility.\n  fwrid:\n    prefix: FWRID\n    format: fwrid-form\n    description: Identity details.\n  fwrjt:\n    prefix: FWRJT\n    format: fwrjt-form\n    description: Justification.\n  fwrsc:\n    prefix: FWRSC\n    format: fwrsc-form\n    description: Scope and plugins.\n  fwrsp:\n    prefix: FWRSP\n    format: fwrsp-form\n    description: Support status.\n  fwrvr:\n    prefix: FWRVR\n    format: fwrvr-form\n    description: Version requirements.\n  hardr:\n    prefix: HARDR\n    format: hardr-form\n    description: Disaster recovery alignment.\n  harlb:\n    prefix: HARLB\n    format: harlb-form\n    description: Load balancing behavior.\n  hcads:\n    prefix: HCADS\n    subsection-types:\n      hechen:\n        max-count: 1\n      apdi:\n        max-count: 1\n      loagre:\n        max-count: 1\n      trca:\n        max-count: 1\n      dehemo:\n        max-count: 1\n    description: |\n      Specify health check, diagnostics, and troubleshooting requirements.\n      Health checks enable rapid problem detection and automated remediation.\n      **Health Check Types**:\n      - **Liveness**: Is the process alive? (restart if not)\n      - **Readiness**: Is the service ready for traffic? (remove from LB if not)\n      - **Startup**: Is the service still starting? (give more time)\n      - **Deep Health**: Are all dependencies healthy?\n      **Health Check Endpoints**:\n      - Standard endpoints (/health, /ready, /live)\n      - Response format (JSON with details)\n      - Performance requirements (fast, non-blocking)\n      - Authentication considerations\n      **Diagnostics Capabilities**:\n      - Real-time log access\n      - Distributed tracing\n      - Request/response capture (debug mode)\n      - Performance profiling\n      - Memory and CPU analysis\n      **Troubleshooting Tools**:\n      - Log search and filtering\n      - Trace correlation\n      - Error aggregation and analysis\n      - Dependency graph visualization\n      - Runbook integration\n      **Self-Healing**:\n      - Automatic restart on failure\n      - Circuit breaker activation\n      - Traffic rerouting\n      - Resource scaling\n      - Alerting and escalation\n  iameg:\n    prefix: IAMEG\n    format: iameg-form\n    description: "Validation, classification, and purpose."\n  iames:\n    prefix: IAMES\n    format: iames-form\n    description: Synchronization and conflict handling.\n  iamet:\n    prefix: IAMET\n    format: iamet-form\n    description: Transformation and defaulting behavior.\n  idaut:\n    prefix: IDAUT\n    subsection-types:\n      ident:\n        max-count: 1\n      authen:\n        max-count: 1\n    description: 9.1.2. Identification and Authentication.\n  ident:\n    prefix: IDENT\n    subsection-types:\n      idtsr-iden-lst:\n        max-count: 1\n      idvepo:\n        max-count: 1\n      idtpv-iden-lst:\n        max-count: 1\n      ssop:\n        max-count: 1\n      serepo:\n        max-count: 1\n      idtam-attr-lst:\n        max-count: 1\n    description: 9.2.1. Identification.\n  imrpi:\n    prefix: IMRPI\n    format: imrpi-form\n    description: Post-incident expectations.\n  imrwr:\n    prefix: IMRWR\n    format: imrwr-form\n    description: War room setup.\n  inris:\n    prefix: INRIS\n    format: inris-form\n    description: Inter-service communication controls.\n  ipcei:\n    prefix: IPCEI\n    format: ipcei-form\n    description: Implementation details.\n  ipces:\n    prefix: IPCES\n    format: ipces-form\n    description: Compliance scope and features.\n  ipcet:\n    prefix: IPCET\n    format: ipcet-form\n    description: Testing details.\n  irppi:\n    prefix: IRPPI\n    format: irppi-form\n    description: Post-incident activities.\n  iscee:\n    prefix: ISCEE\n    format: iscee-form\n    description: Evidence and notes.\n  isceo:\n    prefix: ISCEO\n    format: isceo-form\n    description: Ownership and support.\n  iscer:\n    prefix: ISCER\n    format: iscer-form\n    description: Control requirements.\n  isces:\n    prefix: ISCES\n    format: isces-form\n    description: Applicability and priority.\n  iscet:\n    prefix: ISCET\n    format: iscet-form\n    description: Compliance timeline.\n  keabp:\n    prefix: KEABP\n    description: Key Escrow and Backup Policy.\n  keagn:\n    prefix: KEAGN\n    format: keagn-form\n    description: Key generation settings.\n  keagv:\n    prefix: KEAGV\n    format: keagv-form\n    description: Constraint semantics and business meaning.\n  kearf:\n    prefix: KEARF\n    format: kearf-form\n    description: Foreign-key reference and cascade behavior.\n  lfseb:\n    prefix: LFSEB\n    format: lfseb-form\n    description: "State what happens when the step succeeds and when it fails. Fill in Conditional Trigger only where the step is conditional; a step with no trigger always runs, and a step that states one runs only when it holds — which is also what makes the step skippable."\n  lfsep:\n    prefix: LFSEP\n    format: lfsep-form\n    description: Protocol-level and descriptive details.\n  lfsev:\n    prefix: LFSEV\n    format: lfsev-form\n    description: Inputs and validation behavior.\n  lprpt:\n    prefix: LPRPT\n    format: lprpt-form\n    description: Performance target metrics.\n  lprrl:\n    prefix: LPRRL\n    format: lprrl-form\n    description: Request volume assumptions.\n  mcrea:\n    prefix: MCREA\n    format: mcrea-form\n    description: Allowed authenticators and phishing-resistance rules.\n  mcreo:\n    prefix: MCREO\n    format: mcreo-form\n    description: "Fallback, timeouts, and rationale."\n  mcret:\n    prefix: MCRET\n    format: mcret-form\n    description: Enrollment and remembered-device timing.\n  mdrec:\n    prefix: MDREC\n    format: mdrec-form\n    description: Capability requirements.\n  mdred:\n    prefix: MDRED\n    format: mdred-form\n    description: Device coverage.\n  mdreh:\n    prefix: MDREH\n    format: mdreh-form\n    description: Hardware expectations.\n  mdres:\n    prefix: MDRES\n    format: mdres-form\n    description: Support prioritization.\n  msgkr:\n    prefix: MSGKR\n    subsection-types:\n      msgke-mkey-lst:\n        max-count: 1\n    description: "Message key registry — CE-TX author-copy-once keys, shared."\n  muigd:\n    prefix: MUIGD\n    format: muigd-form\n    description: Graceful-degradation strategy.\n  mvsrm:\n    prefix: MVSRM\n    format: mvsrm-form\n    description: Release management process.\n  nlbra:\n    prefix: NLBRA\n    format: nlbra-form\n    description: Availability settings.\n  nlbrr:\n    prefix: NLBRR\n    format: nlbrr-form\n    description: Routing strategy.\n  nlbrt:\n    prefix: NLBRT\n    format: nlbrt-form\n    description: TLS settings.\n  nspim:\n    prefix: NSPIM\n    format: nspim-form\n    description: IP management controls.\n  ocscc:\n    prefix: OCSCC\n    format: ocscc-form\n    description: Override and coverage handling.\n  ocsco:\n    prefix: OCSCO\n    format: ocsco-form\n    description: Compensation and tooling support.\n  piapa:\n    prefix: PIAPA\n    format: piapa-form\n    description: Assessment process inputs.\n  piapm:\n    prefix: PIAPM\n    format: piapm-form\n    description: Mitigation measures.\n  piapr:\n    prefix: PIAPR\n    format: piapr-form\n    description: Review and approval workflow.\n  plgjt:\n    prefix: PLGJT\n    format: plgjt-form\n    description: Justification and notes.\n  plgqu:\n    prefix: PLGQU\n    format: plgqu-form\n    description: Quality settings.\n  plgsk:\n    prefix: PLGSK\n    format: plgsk-form\n    description: SDK configuration.\n  plgus:\n    prefix: PLGUS\n    format: plgus-form\n    description: Usage context.\n  plgvr:\n    prefix: PLGVR\n    format: plgvr-form\n    description: Version requirements.\n  pllng:\n    prefix: PLLNG\n    subsection-types:\n      tgplt-targ-lst:\n        max-count: 1\n      plgen-prog-lst:\n        max-count: 1\n      frreen-fram-lst:\n        max-count: 1\n      btcen-buil-lst:\n        max-count: 1\n      deptar-depl-lst:\n        max-count: 1\n      dema:\n        max-count: 1\n      ruen:\n        max-count: 1\n    description: |\n      Specify all platform targets, programming languages, frameworks, build\n      tools, and deployment configurations. These choices define the technical\n      foundation and constrain future development options.\n      **Coverage Areas**:\n      - **Target Platforms**: OS (Linux, Windows, macOS), runtimes (Node.js,\n        JVM, .NET), containers (Docker, Kubernetes), cloud platforms (AWS,\n        Azure, GCP), mobile (iOS, Android), embedded systems\n      - **Programming Languages**: Primary and secondary languages, version\n        requirements, SDK specifications, type safety requirements\n      - **Frameworks**: UI frameworks (Flutter, React, Angular), backend\n        frameworks (Spring, Django, Express), testing frameworks, ORM/database\n      - **Build Toolchain**: Build systems, code generators, bundlers, package\n        managers, CI/CD integration, artifact repositories\n      - **Deployment Targets**: Production environments, staging, development,\n        edge deployment, app stores, container registries\n      **Decision Factors**:\n      - Performance requirements and benchmarks\n      - Team expertise and learning curve\n      - Ecosystem maturity and community support\n      - License compatibility (MIT, Apache, GPL implications)\n      - Long-term support and vendor viability\n      - Cross-platform requirements and code sharing\n  psaai:\n    prefix: PSAAI\n    subsection-types:\n      prstov:\n        max-count: 1\n      acov:\n        max-count: 1\n      inca:\n        max-count: 1\n      kesc:\n        max-count: 1\n      acredi:\n        max-count: 1\n      etets-endt-lst:\n        max-count: 1\n      uscatr:\n        max-count: 1\n    description: "Process steps & actor interactions — CE-SU server-use + CE-SC client-side"\n  rfeib:\n    prefix: RFEIB\n    format: rfeib-form\n    description: "Boolean-kind filter options — a promoted `@OneOf` case (csra4)."\n  rfeid:\n    prefix: RFEID\n    format: rfeid-form\n    description: "Tem