erability requirements.\n  inrm:\n    prefix: INRM\n    format: inrm-form\n    description: Monitoring and notes.\n  inrr:\n    prefix: INRR\n    format: inrr-form\n    description: Routing and service discovery.\n  inrs:\n    prefix: INRS\n    format: inrs-form\n    description: Segmentation and isolation.\n  inse:\n    prefix: INSE\n    format: inse-form\n    description: Security and authorization.\n  intr:\n    prefix: INTR\n    format: intr-form\n    description: Related elements and traceability.\n  irde:\n    prefix: IRDE\n    format: irde-form\n    description: Data-exchange definitions.\n  irec:\n    prefix: IREC\n    format: irec-form\n    description: Extension and workspace configuration.\n  irei:\n    prefix: IREI\n    format: irei-form\n    description: "Debugger, linting, and formatting integration."\n  ires:\n    prefix: IRES\n    format: ires-form\n    description: Shared team standardization settings.\n  irpc:\n    prefix: IRPC\n    format: irpc-form\n    description: Communication requirements.\n  irpp:\n    prefix: IRPP\n    format: irpp-form\n    description: Response process.\n  isec:\n    prefix: ISEC\n    format: isec-form\n    description: Requirement applicability.\n  ised:\n    prefix: ISED\n    format: ised-form\n    description: Definition storage and validation.\n  isel:\n    prefix: ISEL\n    format: isel-form\n    description: Synchronization and provisioning details.\n  isem:\n    prefix: ISEM\n    format: isem-form\n    description: Attribute mapping details.\n  iseo:\n    prefix: ISEO\n    format: iseo-form\n    description: Operational behavior.\n  iser:\n    prefix: ISER\n    format: iser-form\n    description: Reference metadata.\n  ises:\n    prefix: ISES\n    format: ises-form\n    description: Scope details.\n  iset:\n    prefix: ISET\n    format: iset-form\n    description: Tooling and notes.\n  isev:\n    prefix: ISEV\n    format: isev-form\n    description: Verification settings.\n  isha:\n    prefix: ISHA\n    format: isha-form\n    description: Access hardening.\n  ishc:\n    prefix: ISHC\n    format: ishc-form\n    description: Container security.\n  ishn:\n    prefix: ISHN\n    format: ishn-form\n    description: Network hardening.\n  isss:\n    prefix: ISSS\n    subsection-types:\n      sse-stan-lst:\n        max-count: 1\n      apsere:\n        max-count: 1\n      inseha:\n        max-count: 1\n      sedeli:\n        max-count: 1\n      vumapo:\n        max-count: 1\n      inrepl:\n        max-count: 1\n    description: |\n      Specify IT security standards including application security, infrastructure\n      security, vulnerability management, and security development practices.\n      Following established standards reduces security risk systematically.\n      **Application Security (OWASP)**:\n      - OWASP Top 10 mitigation (injection, XSS, CSRF, etc.)\n      - OWASP ASVS (Application Security Verification Standard)\n      - Secure coding guidelines by language\n      - Input validation and output encoding\n      - Authentication and session management\n      **Infrastructure Security**:\n      - Server hardening (CIS Benchmarks)\n      - Network security (firewall rules, segmentation)\n      - Cloud security configuration (AWS/Azure/GCP best practices)\n      - Container security (image scanning, runtime protection)\n      - Endpoint security (device management, AV/EDR)\n      **Security Development Lifecycle**:\n      - Threat modeling during design\n      - Security requirements in user stories\n      - Security code review process\n      - Security testing (SAST, DAST, IAST)\n      - Secure deployment practices\n      **Vulnerability Management**:\n      - Vulnerability scanning frequency\n      - CVE monitoring and response time\n      - Patch management procedures\n      - Risk-based prioritization\n      - Vulnerability disclosure process\n      **Incident Response**:\n      - Incident detection mechanisms\n      - Response playbooks\n      - Communication templates\n      - Recovery procedures\n      - Postmortem process\n  ivpd:\n    prefix: IVPD\n    format: ivpd-form\n    description: Required proofing artifacts.\n  ivpf:\n    prefix: IVPF\n    format: ivpf-form\n    description: Failure handling rules.\n  ivpl:\n    prefix: IVPL\n    format: ivpl-form\n    description: Reverification and retention settings.\n  ivpm:\n    prefix: IVPM\n    format: ivpm-form\n    description: Contact and provider verification.\n  ivpw:\n    prefix: IVPW\n    format: ivpw-form\n    description: Workflow and approval settings.\n  kcrp:\n    prefix: KCRP\n    description: Key Compromise and Recovery Policy.\n  kema:\n    prefix: KEMA\n    subsection-types:\n      kegepo:\n        max-count: 1\n      kestpo:\n        max-count: 1\n      keropo:\n        max-count: 1\n      keabp:\n        max-count: 1\n      kcrp:\n        max-count: 1\n    description: 9.5.3. Key Management.\n  kesc:\n    prefix: KESC\n    subsection-types:\n      scov:\n        max-count: 1\n      scnry-scen-lst:\n        max-count: 1\n        min-count: 1\n    description: 6.2.3. Key Scenarios — contains 1+× Scenario.\n  lams:\n    prefix: LAMS\n    subsection-types:\n      sle-soft-lst:\n        max-count: 1\n      lacoru:\n        max-count: 1\n      bce-boun-lst:\n        max-count: 1\n      paor:\n        max-count: 1\n      modent-modu-lst:\n        max-count: 1\n      shlien-shar-lst:\n        max-count: 1\n      deinst:\n        max-count: 1\n      crcuco:\n        max-count: 1\n      ftrmod-feat-lst:\n        max-count: 1\n      movest:\n        max-count: 1\n    description: |\n      Define software layering approach, module organization, and dependency\n      management rules. Clear boundaries prevent spaghetti architecture and\n      enable independent development and testing.\n      **Common Layering Approaches**:\n      - **Clean Architecture**: Entities → Use Cases → Interface Adapters →\n        Frameworks & Drivers (dependencies point inward)\n      - **Hexagonal (Ports & Adapters)**: Domain core with ports (interfaces)\n        and adapters (implementations)\n      - **Onion Architecture**: Domain Model → Domain Services → Application\n        Services → Infrastructure\n      - **Traditional N-Tier**: Presentation → Business Logic → Data Access\n      **Module Organization**:\n      - **By Feature/Domain**: Vertical slices containing all layers for a feature\n      - **By Layer**: Horizontal separation (all controllers, all repositories)\n      - **Bounded Contexts (DDD)**: Independent modules with clear context maps\n      - **Package-by-Component**: Self-contained components with public APIs\n      **Dependency Rules**:\n      - Define allowed and forbidden dependencies between layers/modules\n      - Enforce with architecture tests (ArchUnit, deptry, import linters)\n      - Use interfaces/abstractions for cross-cutting concerns\n      - Keep domain logic independent of frameworks\n      **Best Practices**: SOLID, DRY, KISS, YAGNI, Dependency Inversion.\n  lara:\n    prefix: LARA\n    format: lara-form\n    description: Search and analysis capabilities.\n  larc:\n    prefix: LARC\n    format: larc-form\n    description: Dynamic configuration and collection settings.\n  larr:\n    prefix: LARR\n    format: larr-form\n    description: Retention and archival settings.\n  lcec:\n    prefix: LCEC\n    format: lcec-form\n    description: Constraints and limitations.\n  lcei:\n    prefix: LCEI\n    format: lcei-form\n    description: Integration approach.\n  lcem:\n    prefix: LCEM\n    format: lcem-form\n    description: Migration planning.\n  lcer:\n    prefix: LCER\n    format: lcer-form\n    description: Risk management.\n  lcrf:\n    prefix: LCRF\n    format: lcrf-form\n    description: Cross-layer event and exception flow.\n  lcrg:\n    prefix: LCRG\n    format: lcrg-form\n    description: Boundary enforcement and validation rules.\n  lcri:\n    prefix: LCRI\n    format: lcri-form\n    description: Interface requirements between layers.\n  ldsd:\n    prefix: LDSD\n    format: ldsd-form\n    description: Dependencies and local services.\n  ldsr:\n    prefix: LDSR\n    format: ldsr-form\n    description: Running configuration.\n  ldst:\n    prefix: LDST\n    format: ldst-form\n    description: Test setup.\n  ldsw:\n    prefix: LDSW\n    format: ldsw-form\n    description: Setup workflow.\n  lmra:\n    prefix: LMRA\n    format: lmra-form\n    description: Search and analysis.\n  lmrc:\n    prefix: LMRC\n    format: lmrc-form\n    description: Collection method.\n  lmrs:\n    prefix: LMRS\n    format: lmrs-form\n    description: Storage settings.\n  lprp:\n    prefix: LPRP\n    format: lprp-form\n    description: Temporal and seasonal patterns.\n  maas:\n    prefix: MAAS\n    subsection-types:\n      moin:\n        max-count: 1\n      mecore:\n        max-count: 1\n      appemo:\n        max-count: 1\n      lomare:\n        max-count: 1\n      alre:\n        max-count: 1\n      aledef-aler-lst:\n        max-count: 1\n      dare:\n        max-count: 1\n      oncapr:\n        max-count: 1\n      inmare:\n        max-count: 1\n      slmore:\n        max-count: 1\n    description: |\n      Specify monitoring, alerting, logging, and observability requirements.\n      Effective monitoring enables rapid issue detection and resolution.\n      **Three Pillars of Observability**:\n      - **Metrics**: Quantitative measurements (latency, throughput, errors)\n      - **Logs**: Discrete events with context\n      - **Traces**: Request flow across services\n      **Monitoring Infrastructure**:\n      - Metrics: Prometheus, Datadog, CloudWatch, New Relic\n      - Logging: ELK Stack, Splunk, CloudWatch Logs, Loki\n      - Tracing: Jaeger, Zipkin, AWS X-Ray, Honeycomb\n      - APM: Datadog APM, New Relic APM, Dynatrace\n      **Key Metrics**:\n      - **SLIs (Service Level Indicators)**: Latency, availability, error rate\n      - **SLOs (Service Level Objectives)**: Targets for SLIs\n      - **Error Budgets**: Acceptable error margin\n      - **Golden Signals**: Latency, traffic, errors, saturation\n      **Alerting Requirements**:\n      - Alert severity levels and response times\n      - Notification channels (PagerDuty, Slack, email)\n      - Alert routing and escalation\n      - Alert fatigue prevention\n      **Dashboards and Visualization**:\n      - Operational dashboards for on-call\n      - Business metrics dashboards\n      - Real-time vs. historical views\n      - SLO tracking dashboards\n      **Incident Management**:\n      - On-call rotation and coverage\n      - Incident response procedures\n      - Postmortem process\n      - Runbook integration\n  mcec:\n    prefix: MCEC\n    format: mcec-form\n    description: Platform capabilities.\n  mced:\n    prefix: MCED\n    format: mced-form\n    description: Supported devices.\n  mceh:\n    prefix: MCEH\n    format: mceh-form\n    description: Hardware requirements.\n  mcma:\n    prefix: MCMA\n    format: mcma-form\n    description: Logging and audit trail expectations.\n  mcmd:\n    prefix: MCMD\n    format: mcmd-form\n    description: Required assessments and rollback planning.\n  mcmg:\n    prefix: MCMG\n    format: mcmg-form\n    description: CAB cadence and documentation prerequisites.\n  mcmt:\n    prefix: MCMT\n    format: mcmt-form\n    description: Testing and sign-off requirements.\n  mcra:\n    prefix: MCRA\n    format: mcra-form\n    description: Application metrics.\n  mcrb:\n    prefix: MCRB\n    format: mcrb-form\n    description: Business metrics.\n  mcrc:\n    prefix: MCRC\n    format: mcrc-form\n    description: Container and cluster metrics.\n  mfsc:\n    prefix: MFSC\n    format: mfsc-form\n    description: Field conventions.\n  mfsr:\n    prefix: MFSR\n    format: mfsr-form\n    description: Pagination and error envelopes.\n  mfss:\n    prefix: MFSS\n    format: mfss-form\n    description: Schema standards.\n  mfst:\n    prefix: MFST\n    format: mfst-form\n    description: Comp