Redis | Database | InMemory | None — server-side token store (for opaque tokens)"\n      - fieldname: tokenRevocationEnabled\n        description: "Yes | No — whether token revocation endpoint is available"\n      - fieldname: tokenRevocationPropagation\n        description: "Immediate | EventualConsistency | Polling — how revocation propagates"\n      - fieldname: tokenIntrospectionEnabled\n        description: "Yes | No — whether RFC 7662 token introspection endpoint is available"\n      - fieldname: audienceRestriction\n        description: "Yes | No — whether tokens are audience-restricted to specific services"\n      - fieldname: scopePolicy\n        description: Minimum scope principle — how token scopes are assigned and validated\n  scp-form:\n    fields:\n      - fieldname: sessionMechanism\n        description: "ServerSideCookie | JwtBearer | OpaqueToken — primary session mechanism"\n      - fieldname: sessionIdGeneration\n        description: "CryptoRandom | UUID | HMAC — method for session identifier generation"\n      - fieldname: sessionIdEntropy\n        description: "Minimum entropy for session identifiers (e.g., 128-bit, 256-bit)"\n      - fieldname: sessionBindingMethod\n        description: "Cookie | Header | TokenBound — how sessions are bound to requests"\n      - fieldname: httpOnlyCookies\n        description: "Yes | No — whether session cookies use HttpOnly flag"\n      - fieldname: secureCookies\n        description: "Yes | No — whether session cookies use Secure flag (HTTPS only)"\n      - fieldname: sameSitePolicy\n        description: "Strict | Lax | None — SameSite cookie attribute policy"\n      - fieldname: cookieDomain\n        description: Domain scope for session cookies (exact domain or parent domain)\n      - fieldname: deviceBinding\n        description: "None | Fingerprint | CertificateBound | DPoP — session-to-device binding"\n      - fieldname: sessionDataStorage\n        description: "ServerSide | ClientSide | Hybrid — where full session data is stored"\n      - fieldname: sessionReplicationStrategy\n        description: "StickySession | Distributed | Stateless — strategy for multi-node deployments"\n      - fieldname: csrfProtection\n        description: "SynchronizerToken | DoubleSubmit | SameSite | None — CSRF mitigation method"\n      - fieldname: postLoginRedirectValidation\n        description: "Allowlist | SameOrigin | None — validation of post-login redirect targets"\n  rhp-form:\n    fields:\n      - fieldname: oauthRedirectUriPolicy\n        description: "ExactMatch | WildcardSubdomain | DynamicRegistration — redirect URI validation"\n      - fieldname: allowedRedirectDomains\n        description: Comma-separated list of allowed redirect domains\n      - fieldname: callbackUrlValidation\n        description: "StrictMatch | PathPrefix | OriginOnly — how callback URLs are validated"\n      - fieldname: stateParameterRequired\n        description: "Yes | No — whether OAuth state parameter is required for CSRF protection"\n      - fieldname: pkceRequired\n        description: "Yes | No — whether PKCE (Proof Key for Code Exchange) is mandatory"\n      - fieldname: pkceMethod\n        description: "S256 | Plain — PKCE code challenge method (S256 recommended)"\n      - fieldname: deepLinkHandling\n        description: "UniversalLinks | AppLinks | CustomScheme — mobile deep link strategy"\n      - fieldname: errorRedirectBehavior\n        description: "RedirectWithError | ErrorPage | OriginalPage — behavior on auth errors"\n      - fieldname: postLogoutRedirectUri\n        description: Where users are redirected after logout\n      - fieldname: singleLogoutRedirectChain\n        description: "Yes | No — whether SLO propagates logouts across all connected services"\n      - fieldname: corsPolicy\n        description: AllowedOrigins for authentication endpoints (exact list or pattern)\n      - fieldname: iframeEmbeddingPolicy\n        description: "Deny | SameOrigin | AllowSpecific — X-Frame-Options / CSP frame-ancestors"\n  aeh-form:\n    fields:\n      - fieldname: invalidCredentialResponse\n        description: "GenericError | SpecificError — response to invalid credentials (generic preferred)"\n      - fieldname: accountLockoutThreshold\n        description: "Number of failed attempts before lockout (e.g., 5, 10, configurable)"\n      - fieldname: lockoutDuration\n        description: "Duration of lockout (e.g., 15min, 30min, progressive, permanent)"\n      - fieldname: lockoutEscalation\n        description: "Fixed | Progressive | Exponential — whether lockout duration increases"\n      - fieldname: bruteForceProtection\n        description: "RateLimiting | CAPTCHA | IPBlock | AccountLock — brute-force mitigation"\n      - fieldname: credentialStuffingProtection\n        description: "BreachDatabase | DeviceFingerprint | BehaviorAnalysis | None"\n      - fieldname: userNotificationOnFailure\n        description: "Yes | No — whether users are notified of failed login attempts"\n      - fieldname: adminAlertThreshold\n        description: "Number of failures before admin alert (e.g., 10, 50, per-minute rate)"\n      - fieldname: failedLoginAuditLogging\n        description: "Yes | No — whether failed login attempts are logged for audit"\n      - fieldname: suspiciousActivityResponse\n        description: "RequireMFA | TemporaryBlock | CAPTCHA | ManualReview — response to anomalies"\n      - fieldname: gracefulDegradation\n        description: "Behavior when authentication service is partially unavailable (queue, fallback, deny)"\n  suap-form:\n    fields:\n      - fieldname: stepUpEnabled\n        description: "Yes | No — whether step-up authentication is implemented"\n      - fieldname: stepUpTriggers\n        description: "HighRiskOperation | SensitiveDataAccess | AdminAction | PaymentApproval | SettingsChange"\n      - fieldname: stepUpTargetAal\n        description: "AAL2 | AAL3 — target assurance level for step-up authentication"\n      - fieldname: stepUpTimeout\n        description: "Duration the elevated session lasts (e.g., 5min, 15min, transaction-scoped)"\n      - fieldname: riskBasedAuthEnabled\n        description: "Yes | No — whether risk signals influence authentication requirements"\n      - fieldname: riskSignals\n        description: "GeoLocation | IPReputation | DeviceFingerprint | BehaviorPattern | TimeOfDay"\n      - fieldname: riskScoringMethod\n        description: "RuleBased | MachineLearning | Hybrid — how risk scores are computed"\n      - fieldname: lowRiskAction\n        description: "AllowSilently | NormalAuth — response to low-risk signals"\n      - fieldname: mediumRiskAction\n        description: "RequireMFA | AdditionalVerification — response to medium-risk signals"\n      - fieldname: highRiskAction\n        description: "Block | RequirePhishingResistant | ManualReview — response to high-risk signals"\n      - fieldname: adaptiveAuthProvider\n        description: "Built-in | Third-party service name — provider of adaptive authentication"\n      - fieldname: continuousAuthEnabled\n        description: "Yes | No — whether session is continuously monitored for risk changes"\n  lfsev-form:\n    fields:\n      - fieldname: inputRequired\n        description: "Username | Password | OTP | BiometricSample | ConsentApproval | None"\n      - fieldname: validationAction\n        description: "CredentialVerification | TokenValidation | RiskAssessment | MfaVerification | None"\n      - fieldname: timeoutSeconds\n        description: "Maximum time allowed for this step (e.g., 300, 600)"\n  lfseb-form:\n    fields:\n      - fieldname: successOutcome\n        description: "NextStep | TokenIssued | SessionCreated | RedirectToApp — outcome on success"\n      - fieldname: failureOutcome\n        description: "RetryWithError | Lockout | RedirectToError | AbortFlow — outcome on failure"\n      - fieldname: conditionalTrigger\n        description: "The condition under which this step runs, if it is not unconditional (e.g. MFA required, new device). Leave empty for a step that always runs; a step that states a trigger is by that fact the one that can be skipped."\n  lfsep-form:\n    fields:\n      - fieldname: protocolMessage\n        description: "OAuth2 AuthZ Request | Token Request | SAML AuthnRequest | OIDC Userinfo — protocol-level message"\n      - fieldname: description\n        description: Detailed description of what happens in this step\n  prp-form:\n    fields:\n      - fieldname: minimumLengthSingleFactor\n        description: "Minimum password length when used as single factor (NIST: 15 characters)"\n      - fieldname: minimumLengthMultiFactor\n        description: "Minimum password length when used as part of MFA (NIST: 8 characters)"\n      - fieldname: maximumLength\n        description: "Maximum allowed password length (NIST: at least 64 characters)"\n      - fieldname: allowedCharacterSets\n        description: "ASCII | Unicode | ASCIIPlusSpace — character sets accepted in passwords"\n      - fieldname: compositionRulesEnforced\n        description: "Yes | No — whether mixed-case/digit/symbol rules are enforced (NIST: No)"\n      - fieldname: passphraseSupported\n        description: "Yes | No — whether multi-word passphrases with spaces are supported"\n      - fieldname: unicodeNormalization\n        description: "NFC | NFD | None — Unicode normalization form applied before hashing"\n      - fieldname: passwordBlocklistEnabled\n        description: "Yes | No — whether passwords are compared against a blocklist"\n      - fieldname: blocklistSources\n        description: "BreachCorpus | DictionaryWords | ContextSpecific | HaveIBeenPwned — sources for blocklist"\n      - fieldname: passwordStrengthMeter\n        description: "Yes | No — whether a real-time strength indicator is displayed during creation"\n      - fieldname: passwordHintsAllowed\n        description: "Yes | No — whether password hints are stored (NIST: No)"\n      - fieldname: securityQuestionsAllowed\n        description: "Yes | No — whether KBA/security questions are used (NIST: No)"\n      - fieldname: showPasswordOption\n        description: "Yes | No — whether users can toggle password visibility during entry"\n      - fieldname: passwordManagerSupport\n        description: "Yes | No — whether autofill and paste are supported for password entry"\n      - fieldname: truncationPolicy\n        description: "None | Trim — whether leading/trailing whitespace is trimmed (NIST: verify entire password)"\n      - fieldname: typoTolerancePolicy\n        description: "None | CaseFirstChar | TrimWhitespace — whether minor typo corrections are attempted"\n  psp-form:\n    fields:\n      - fieldname: hashingAlgorithm\n        description: "Argon2id | bcrypt | scrypt | PBKDF2 — password hashing algorithm"\n      - fieldname: hashingCostFactor\n        description: "Work factor/iteration count for the hashing algorithm (e.g., bcrypt cost 12)"\n      - fieldname: costFactorReviewSchedule\n        description: "Annual | Biannual | OnHardwareUpgrade — when cost factor is re-evaluated"\n      - fieldname: saltLength\n        description: "Minimum salt length in bits (NIST: at least 32 bits)"\n      - fieldname: saltGeneration\n        description: "CryptoRandom | CSPRNG — method for generating salt values"\n      - fieldname: pepperEnabled\n        description: "Yes | No — whether a server-side secret key (pepper) is used for additional hashing"\n      - fieldname: pepperStorage\n        description: "HSM | TEE | EncryptedConfig | SecretManager — where the pepper key is stored"\n      - fieldname: hashVersioning\n        description: "Yes | No — whether the hash algorithm and cost factor are stored per password for migration"\n      - fieldname: transmissionEncryption\n        description: "TLS1.3 | TLS1.2 — encryption for password transmission"\n      - fieldname: clientSideHashing\n        description: "Yes | No — whether passwords are pre-hashed on the client before transmission"\n      - fieldname: memoryHardFunction\n        description: "Yes | No — whether the hashing function is memory-hard to resist GPU attacks"\n      - fieldname: outputLength\n        description: Hash output length in bits (should match underlying scheme output length)\n  plp-form:\n    fields:\n      - fieldname: periodicRotationRequired\n        description: "Yes | No — whether periodic password changes are required (NIST: No)"\n      - fieldname: rotationPeriod\n        description: "If rotation is required: period in days (e.g., 90, 180, 365)"\n      - fieldname: forceChangeOnCompromise\n        description: "Yes | No — whether password change is forced on evidence of compromise"\n      - fieldname: passwordHistoryDepth\n        description: "Number of previous passwords stored to prevent reuse (e.g., 0, 5, 12, 24)"\n      - fieldname: minimumPasswordAge\n        description: "Minimum time before a password can be changed again (e.g., 0, 1d) to prevent rapid cycling"\n      - fieldname: initialPasswordPolicy\n        description: "SystemGenerated | UserChosen | TemporaryWithForceChange — policy for initial passwords"\n      - fieldname: temporaryPasswordExpiry\n        description: "Duration before a temporary/initial password expires (e.g., 24h, 72h)"\n      - fieldname: passwordExpiryWarning\n        description: "Number of days before expiry that users are warned (e.g., 14, 30)"\n      - fieldname: passwordChangeNotification\n        description: "Yes | No — whether users are notified when their password is changed"\n      - fieldname: passwordChangeRequiresCurrent\n        description: "Yes | No — whether current password must be verified before setting a new one"\n      - fieldname: administratorResetPolicy\n        description: "TemporaryPassword | ResetLink | MfaVerification — how admins reset user passwords"\n      - fieldname: passwordInactivityDisable\n        description: "Duration of inactivity before account is disabled (e.g., 90d, 180d, Never)"\n  alp-form:\n    fields:\n      - fieldname: lockoutThreshold\n        description: "Number of consecutive failed attempts before lockout (NIST max: 100, typical: 5-10)"\n      - fieldname: lockoutDuration\n        description: "Duration of lockout (e.g., 15min, 30min, UntilAdminUnlock, Progressive)"\n      - fieldname: lockoutEscalation\n        description: "Fixed | Progressive | Exponential — whether lockout duration increases"\n      - fieldname: rateLimitingMethod\n        description: "Delay | CAPTCHA | Lockout | IPBlock | Combination — rate-limiting strategy"\n      - fieldname: delayProgression\n        description: "Delay schedule for progressive throttling (e.g., 30s after 3rd, 1min after 5th)"\n      - fieldname: captchaTriggerThreshold\n        description: Number of failed attempts before CAPTCHA is required\n      - fieldname: ipBasedRateLimiting\n        description: "Yes | No — whether rate limiting also applies per IP address"\n      - fieldname: distributedAttackProtection\n        description: "Yes | No — whether protection against credential stuffing across IPs is implemented"\n      - fieldname: unlockMechanism\n        description: "TimeBasedAutoUnlock | AdminUnlock | SelfServiceWithMFA | EmailVerification"\n      - fieldname: failedAttemptResetOnSuccess\n        description: "Yes | No — whether the failed attempt counter resets after successful login"\n      - fieldname: lockoutNotification\n        description: "User | Admin | Both | None — who is notified when lockout occurs"\n      - fieldname: permanentLockoutEnabled\n        description: "Yes | No — whether accounts are permanently locked after extreme abuse"\n      - fieldname: permanentLockoutThreshold\n        description: "Number of lockout cycles before permanent lock (e.g., 5, 10)"\n  crp-form:\n    fields:\n      - fieldname: passwordResetMethod\n        description: "EmailLink | SMSCode | SecurityQuestions | MfaVerification | AdminAssisted — how users reset passwords"\n      - fieldname: resetLinkExpiry\n        description: "Duration before a password reset link expires (e.g., 15min, 1h, 24h)"\n      - fieldname: resetLinkSingleUse\n        description: "Yes | No — whether reset links can only be used once"\n      - fieldname: resetRateLimiting\n        description: "Requests per period allowed (e.g., 3 per hour, 5 per day)"\n      - fieldname: savedRecoveryCodesEnabled\n        description: "Yes | No — whether one-time recovery codes are provided at enrollment"\n      - fieldname: recoveryCodeCount\n        description: "Number of recovery codes generated (e.g., 8, 10, 16)"\n      - fieldname: recoveryCodeFormat\n        description: "AlphaNumeric | NumericOnly | Words — format of recovery codes"\n      - fieldname: issuedRecoveryCodeChannels\n        description: "Email | SMS | PostalMail | InPerson — channels for sending issued recovery codes"\n      - fieldname: recoveryCodeExpiry\n        description: "Duration before issued recovery codes expire (NIST: 10min SMS, 24h email)"\n      - fieldname: identityReverificationRequired\n        description: "Yes | No — whether identity re-verification is required for recovery at higher AALs"\n      - fieldname: recoveryContactEnabled\n        description: "Yes | No — whether a trusted contact can initiate recovery"\n      - fieldname: multipleRecoveryAddresses\n        description: "Yes | No — whether subscribers can register multiple recovery addresses (NIST: at least 2)"\n      - fieldname: recoveryAuditLogging\n        description: "Yes | No — whether all recovery attempts are logged for audit"\n  ccdp-form:\n    fields:\n      - fieldname: breachDatabaseMonitoring\n        description: "Yes | No — whether passwords are checked against known breach databases"\n      - fieldname: breachDatabaseSource\n        description: "HaveIBeenPwned | Internal | CommercialFeed | Multiple — source of breach data"\n      - fieldname: breachCheckFrequency\n        description: "AtCreation | AtLogin | Periodic | RealTime — when breach checks are performed"\n      - fieldname: compromisedCredentialAction\n        description: "ForceChange | NotifyAndRecommend | DisableAccount — action when credential is found compromised"\n      - fieldname: credentialStuffingDetection\n        description: "Yes | No — whether automated credential stuffing attacks are detected"\n      - fieldname: stuffingDetectionMethod\n        description: "BehaviorAnalysis | IPReputation | VelocityChecks | DeviceFingerprint — detection methods"\n      - fieldname: darkWebMonitoring\n        description: "Yes | No — whether organizational credentials are monitored on dark web"\n      - fieldname: userCompromiseNotification\n        description: "Email | InApp | Push | SMS — how users are notified of credential compromise"\n      - fieldname: adminCompromiseAlerts\n        description: "Yes | No — whether administrators receive alerts for mass compromise events"\n      - fieldname: compromiseResponseSla\n        description: "Time to force credential change after detection (e.g., Immediate, 24h, 72h)"\n  sacp-form:\n    fields:\n      - fieldname: serviceAccountPasswordPolicy\n        description: "AutoGenerated | ManagedByVault | CertificateBased — how service account credentials are managed"\n      - fieldname: serviceAccountRotationPeriod\n        description: "Rotation period for service account credentials (e.g., 30d, 90d, OnDemand)"\n      - fieldname: apiKeyLifetime\n        description: "Maximum lifetime for API keys (e.g., 90d, 365d, NoExpiry)"\n      - fieldname: apiKeyRotationPolicy\n        description: "Automatic | Manual | GracePeriodOverlap — how API keys are rotated"\n      - fieldname: secretsManagementTool\n        description: "HashiCorpVault | AWSSecretsManager | AzureKeyVault | GCPSecretManager | None"\n      - fieldname: machineToMachineAuth\n        description: "OAuth2ClientCredentials | mTLS | JWTBearer | APIKey — authentication method"\n      - fieldname: serviceAccountMfaRequired\n        description: "Yes | No — whether service accounts require MFA for interactive login"\n      - fieldname: sharedCredentialProhibition\n        description: "Yes | No — whether shared/group credentials are prohibited"\n      - fieldname: credentialVaultIntegration\n        description: "Yes | No — whether application credentials are injected from a secrets vault at runtime"\n      - fieldname: hardcodedCredentialDetection\n        description: "Yes | No — whether CI/CD scans for hardcoded credentials in source code"\n  mcrea-form:\n    fields:\n      - fieldname: allowedAuthenticatorTypes\n        description: "TOTP | WebAuthn | FIDO2 | SMS | Push | Passkey — allowed second-factor types"\n      - fieldname: phishingResistanceRequired\n        description: "Yes | No | Recommended — whether phishing-resistant authenticators are required"\n  mcret-form:\n    fields:\n      - fieldname: mfaEnrollmentDeadline\n        description: "Deadline or grace period for MFA enrollment (e.g., Immediate, 30d, 90d)"\n      - fieldname: mfaGracePeriod\n        description: Period after enrollment deadline during which MFA is recommended but not enforced\n      - fieldname: rememberDeviceEnabled\n        description: "Yes | No — whether trusted device remembering can skip MFA temporarily"\n      - fieldname: rememberDeviceDuration\n        description: "Duration the device is trusted (e.g., 7d, 30d, 90d)"\n  mcreo-form:\n    fields:\n      - fieldname: fallbackMechanismIfUnavailable\n        description: "RecoveryCode | AdminAssist | Deny — fallback when primary MFA is unavailable"\n      - fieldname: reauthenticationTimeout\n        description: "Overall session timeout requiring re-authentication (NIST: AAL1=30d, AAL2=24h, AAL3=12h)"\n      - fieldname: inactivityTimeout\n        description: "Session inactivity timeout (NIST: AAL2=1h, AAL3=15min)"\n      - fieldname: description\n        description: Description of MFA requirements and rationale for this user category\n  stp-form:\n    fields:\n      - fieldname: idleTimeoutDefault\n        description: "Duration of inactivity before session expires (e.g., 15min, 30min, 1h)"\n      - fieldname: idleTimeoutHighValue\n        description: "Shorter idle timeout for sensitive operations (e.g., 2min, 5min)"\n      - fieldname: absoluteTimeout\n        description: "Maximum session duration regardless of activity (e.g., 4h, 8h, 24h)"\n      - fieldname: renewalTimeout\n        description: "Interval at which the session ID is transparently rotated (e.g., 15min, 30min)"\n      - fieldname: idleTimeoutAal1\n        description: "Idle timeout for AAL1 sessions (NIST default: 30 days)"\n      - fieldname: absoluteTimeoutAal1\n        description: "Maximum session duration for AAL1 (NIST default: 30 days)"\n      - fieldname: idleTimeoutAal2\n        description: "Idle timeout for AAL2 sessions (NIST default: 1 hour)"\n      - fieldname: absoluteTimeoutAal2\n        description: "Maximum session duration for AAL2 (NIST default: 24 hours)"\n      - fieldname: idleTimeoutAal3\n        description: "Idle timeout for AAL3 sessions (NIST default: 15 minutes)"\n      - fieldname: absoluteTimeoutAal3\n        description: "Maximum session duration for AAL3 (NIST default: 12 hours)"\n      - fieldname: timeoutEnforcement\n        description: "ServerSide | ClientSide | Both — where session timeout is enforced (server-side mandatory)"\n      - fieldname: timeoutWarningEnabled\n        description: "Yes | No — whether users receive a warning before session expiry"\n      - fieldname: timeoutWarningLeadTime\n        description: "Time before expiry to show warning (e.g., 2min, 5min)"\n      - fieldname: timeoutWarningAction\n        description: "ExtendSession | SaveDraft | RedirectToLogin — action offered to user"\n      - fieldname: sessionExtensionAllowed\n        description: "Yes | No | Limited — whether users can extend an expiring session"\n      - fieldname: maxExtensions\n        description: "Maximum number of consecutive session extensions (e.g., 3, unlimited)"\n      - fieldname: gracePeriodAfterExpiry\n        description: "Brief window after expiry for saving work (e.g., 0s, 30s, 2min)"\n  csp-form:\n    fields:\n      - fieldname: concurrentSessionsAllowed\n        description: "Yes | No | Limited — whether multiple simultaneous sessions are permitted"\n      - fieldname: maxConcurrentSessions\n        description: "Maximum number of active sessions per user (e.g., 1, 3, 5, unlimited)"\n      - fieldname: concurrentSessionScope\n        description: "PerAccount | PerDeviceType | PerApplication — scope for counting sessions"\n      - fieldname: conflictResolution\n        description: "TerminateOldest | TerminateNewest | DenyNew | AskUser — action when limit exceeded"\n      - fieldname: sessionListVisible\n        description: "Yes | No — whether users can see a list of their active sessions"\n      - fieldname: remoteTerminationEnabled\n        description: "Yes | No — whether users can terminate other sessions remotely"\n      - fieldname: sessionDeviceInfo\n        description: "IPAddress | DeviceType | Browser | Location | All — info shown per session"\n      - fieldname: concurrentLoginNotification\n        description: "None | Email | Push | InApp | All — notification when new session starts"\n      - fieldname: suspiciousConcurrentLoginAction\n        description: "Notify | RequireMFA | TerminateAll | LockAccount — action for suspicious simultaneous access"\n      - fieldname: privilegedAccountSessionLimit\n        description: "Maximum sessions for admin/privileged accounts (typically stricter, e.g., 1)"\n      - fieldname: crossDeviceSessionHandling\n        description: "Independent | Synchronized | SingleDevice — how sessions relate across devices"\n  srp-form:\n    fields:\n      - fieldname: logoutMechanism\n        description: "ServerSideInvalidation | TokenBlacklist | CookieClear | All — how sessions are terminated"\n      - fieldname: logoutButtonPlacement\n        description: "Header | Menu | Both | EveryPage — where the logout action is accessible"\n      - fieldname: logoutConfirmation\n        description: "Immediate | ConfirmDialog | None — whether logout requires confirmation"\n      - fieldname: postLogoutRedirect\n        description: "LoginPage | HomePage | GoodbyePage | CustomUrl — where users go after logout"\n      - fieldname: postLogoutCacheClear\n        description: "Yes | No — whether Clear-Site-Data header is sent on logout"\n      - fieldname: singleLogoutEnabled\n        description: "Yes | No — whether logout propagates to all connected IdPs and services"\n      - fieldname: singleLogoutProtocol\n        description: "FrontChannel | BackChannel | Both — SLO propagation method"\n      - fieldname: privilegeChangeRevocation\n        description: "Regenerate | Terminate | NoAction — session handling when user roles change"\n      - fieldname: passwordChangeRevocation\n        description: "TerminateAll | TerminateOthers | KeepCurrent — session handling after password change"\n      - fieldname: compromiseRevocation\n        description: "TerminateAll | TerminateOthers | RequireReauth — action when account compromise suspected"\n      - fieldname: adminTerminationEnabled\n        description: "Yes | No — whether administrators can terminate user sessions"\n      - fieldname: bulkRevocationEnabled\n        description: "Yes | No — whether mass session invalidation is supported (e.g., security incident)"\n      - fieldname: revocationPropagationDelay\n        description: "Immediate | EventualConsistency | MaxDelay — how quickly revocation takes effect across nodes"\n  rmp-form:\n    fields:\n      - fieldname: rememberMeEnabled\n        description: "Yes | No — whether remember-me / keep-me-signed-in is offered"\n      - fieldname: rememberMeDuration\n        description: "Duration of persistent session (e.g., 7d, 30d, 90d)"\n      - fieldname: rememberMeTokenType\n        description: "PersistentCookie | DeviceToken | RefreshToken — mechanism for persistent login"\n      - fieldname: rememberMeTokenStorage\n        description: "HttpOnlyCookie | SecureStorage | EncryptedLocalStorage — client-side storage"\n      - fieldname: rememberMeTokenRotation\n        description: "Yes | No — whether persistent tokens are rotated on each use"\n      - fieldname: rememberMeReuseDetection\n        description: "Yes | No — whether reuse of old persistent tokens triggers revocation"\n      - fieldname: rememberMeDeviceBinding\n        description: "None | Fingerprint | CertificateBound — how persistent tokens are bound to devices"\n      - fieldname: rememberMeRevocation\n        description: "ManualOnly | OnPasswordChange | OnSecurityEvent | All — when persistent tokens are revoked"\n      - fieldname: rememberMeAalReduction\n        description: "Yes | No — whether remember-me reduces effective AAL (e.g., AAL2 to AAL1)"\n      - fieldname: rememberMeRestrictedOperations\n        description: "Operations requiring full reauthentication even with active remember-me (e.g., password change, payment)"\n      - fieldname: trustedDeviceManagement\n        description: "Yes | No — whether users can manage a list of trusted/remembered devices"\n      - fieldname: maxTrustedDevices\n        description: "Maximum number of devices in the trusted device list (e.g., 5, 10)"\n      - fieldname: trustedDeviceExpiry\n        description: "Duration a device stays trusted (e.g., 30d, 90d, indefinite)"\n  ssp-form:\n    fields:\n      - fieldname: sessionFixationProtection\n        description: "RegenerateOnLogin | RegenerateOnPrivilegeChange | Both — session ID regeneration strategy"\n      - fieldname: sessionIdRegenerationTriggers\n        description: "Login | PrivilegeChange | PasswordChange | MfaStep | All — events triggering session ID renewal"\n      - fieldname: sessionBindingProperties\n        description: "None | IPAddress | UserAgent | DeviceFingerprint | TlsCertificate — properties bound to session"\n      - fieldname: bindingMismatchAction\n        description: "Terminate | RequireReauth | LogAndContinue | StepUpAuth — action on session binding violation"\n      - fieldname: sessionAnomalyDetection\n        description: "Yes | No — whether session anomalies (IP change, user-agent change) are monitored"\n      - fieldname: anomalyDetectionSignals\n        description: "IPChange | UserAgentChange | GeoLocationJump | ConcurrentAccess — signals monitored"\n      - fieldname: sessionCachePolicy\n        description: "NoStore | NoCache | Private — Cache-Control directive for pages with session data"\n      - fieldname: clearSiteDataOnLogout\n        description: "Yes | No — whether Clear-Site-Data header clears cache, cookies, storage on logout"\n      - fieldname: sessionTransportSecurity\n        description: "HttpsOnly | HstsEnabled | CertificatePinning — transport layer requirements for sessions"\n      - fieldname: sessionIdInUrlPrevention\n        description: "Yes | No — whether session IDs in URL parameters are explicitly blocked"\n      - fieldname: crossOriginSessionProtection\n        description: "SameSiteCookies | CorsRestriction | Both — cross-origin session protection mechanisms"\n      - fieldname: sessionDataMinimization\n        description: "Yes | No — whether session stores only essential data (minimize sensitive data in session)"\n  slm-form:\n    fields:\n      - fieldname: sessionCreationLogging\n        description: "Yes | No — whether session creation events are logged"\n      - fieldname: sessionDestructionLogging\n        description: "Yes | No — whether session termination events are logged"\n      - fieldname: sessionRenewalLogging\n        description: "Yes | No — whether session ID renewal events are logged"\n      - fieldname: sessionEventDetails\n        description: "Timestamp | SourceIP | UserAgent | GeoLocation | SessionAction — details captured per event"\n      - fieldname: sessionIdInLogs\n        description: "SaltedHash | Truncated | Never — how session IDs appear in logs (never in plaintext)"\n      - fieldname: sessionActivityTracking\n        description: "Yes | No — whether per-session activity (page visits, actions) is tracked"\n      - fieldname: sessionHistoryVisibleToUser\n        description: "Yes | No — whether users can view their session activity history"\n      - fieldname: failedSessionAccessLogging\n        description: "Yes | No — whether invalid/expired session access attempts are logged"\n      - fieldname: sessionMetricsCollection\n        description: "Yes | No — whether session duration, count, and patterns are collected as metrics"\n      - fieldname: sessionAuditRetention\n        description: "Duration session audit logs are retained (e.g., 90d, 1y, 7y)"\n      - fieldname: realTimeSessionAlerts\n        description: "Yes | No — whether suspicious session events trigger real-time alerts"\n      - fieldname: alertTriggers\n        description: "BruteForce | AnomalousAccess | MassLogout | SessionHijack — events triggering alerts"\n  dap-form:\n    fields:\n      - fieldname: databaseConnectionSecurity\n        description: "TlsRequired | TlsOptional | LocalSocketOnly — transport security for DB connections"\n      - fieldname: minimumTlsVersion\n        description: "TLS 1.2 | TLS 1.3 — minimum TLS version for database connections"\n      - fieldname: applicationAccountStrategy\n        description: "PerService | PerModule | SharedPool — how application-level DB accounts are organized"\n      - fieldname: applicationAccountPrivileges\n        description: "SelectUpdateDelete | ReadOnly | Custom — default permissions for application accounts"\n      - fieldname: schemaOwnershipSeparation\n        description: "Yes | No — whether schema owner accounts are separate from application accounts"\n      - fieldname: directTableAccess\n        description: "Allowed | ViewsOnly | StoredProceduresOnly — whether direct table access is permitted"\n      - fieldname: databaseCredentialStorage\n        description: "SecretsVault | EnvironmentVariable | EncryptedConfig — where DB credentials are stored"\n      - fieldname: credentialRotationPolicy\n        description: "Automatic | Manual | Interval — how DB credentials are rotated (e.g., every 90d)"\n      - fieldname: connectionPoolSecurity\n        description: "PerUser | PerService | Shared — connection pool isolation level"\n      - fieldname: privilegedAccessManagement\n        description: "JustInTime | PermanentWithApproval | BreakGlass — how DBA access is managed"\n      - fieldname: databaseFirewallRules\n        description: "AllowlistOnly | VpcInternal | SubnetRestricted — network access restrictions"\n      - fieldname: sqlInjectionPrevention\n        description: "ParameterizedQueries | OrmOnly | PreparedStatements — SQL injection mitigation strategy"\n      - fieldname: queryComplexityLimits\n        description: "Yes | No — whether query complexity or execution time limits are enforced"\n      - fieldname: databaseActivityMonitoring\n        description: "DamEnabled | NativeAudit | None — database activity monitoring tool usage"\n  rlsp-form:\n    fields:\n      - fieldname: rowLevelSecurityEnabled\n        description: "Yes | No — whether row-level security (RLS) is implemented"\n      - fieldname: rlsImplementation\n        description: "DatabaseNative | ApplicationLayer | OrmFilter | Hybrid — where RLS is enforced"\n      - fieldname: rlsFilteringStrategy\n        description: "TenantId | UserId | OrganizationId | CustomPredicate — primary filtering dimension"\n      - fieldname: rlsBypassPolicy\n        description: "NeverBypass | SuperAdminOnly | ServiceAccountOnly — who can bypass RLS"\n      - fieldname: hierarchicalVisibility\n        description: "Yes | No — whether managers see subordinate data (organizational hierarchy)"\n      - fieldname: hierarchyDepthLimit\n        description: "Unlimited | DirectReports | NLevels — how deep hierarchical visibility extends"\n      - fieldname: crossTenantAccess\n        description: "Denied | PlatformAdminOnly | ConsentBased — cross-tenant data access rules"\n      - fieldname: dataOwnerAccess\n        description: "FullAccess | ReadOnly | Delegated — access level for the data owner/creator"\n      - fieldname: sharedDataHandling\n        description: "ExplicitGrant | GroupBased | LinkSharing — how shared records are authorized"\n      - fieldname: rlsPerformanceStrategy\n        description: "IndexedFilterColumn | PartitionedByTenant | MaterializedViews — performance optimization for RLS"\n      - fieldname: rlsTestingStrategy\n        description: "AutomatedTests | PenetrationTesting | Both — how RLS enforcement is verified"\n  clsp-form:\n    fields:\n      - fieldname: columnLevelSecurityEnabled\n        description: "Yes | No — whether column-level access control is implemented"\n      - fieldname: columnAccessImplementation\n        description: "DatabaseGrants | ViewRestriction | ApplicationLayer | FieldProjection — enforcement mechanism"\n      - fieldname: sensitiveColumnClassification\n        description: "PII | Financial | Health | Confidential | Internal | Public — classification scheme for columns"\n      - fieldname: piiColumnAccess\n        description: "RestrictedByRole | MaskedByDefault | EncryptedAtRest — access policy for PII columns"\n      - fieldname: financialDataColumnAccess\n        description: "RestrictedByRole | AuditedAccess | Masked — access policy for financial data columns"\n      - fieldname: healthDataColumnAccess\n        description: "HipaaCompliant | StrictRole | Encrypted — access policy for health/medical data"\n      - fieldname: dynamicFieldVisibility\n        description: "Yes | No — whether field visibility varies dynamically based on user role or context"\n      - fieldname: columnAccessAudit\n        description: "Yes | No — whether access to sensitive columns is individually audited"\n      - fieldname: columnEncryptionPolicy\n        description: "None | SelectedColumns | AllSensitive | AlwaysEncrypted — column-level encryption approach"\n  tdip-form:\n    fields:\n      - fieldname: tenantIsolationModel\n        description: "SharedDatabase_SharedSchema | SharedDatabase_SeparateSchema | SeparateDatabase — multi-tenancy architecture"\n      - fieldname: tenantIdentifierColumn\n        description: "Column name used for tenant filtering (e.g., tenant_id, org_id)"\n      - fieldname: tenantContextInjection\n        description: "SessionVariable | ConnectionString | MiddlewareFilter | RowPolicy — how tenant context is set"\n      - fieldname: tenantIsolationEnforcement\n        description: "DatabaseLevel | ApplicationLevel | Both — where isolation is enforced"\n      - fieldname: crossTenantQueryPrevention\n        description: "DatabaseRLS | QueryRewriting | GlobalFilter | AllLayers — how cross-tenant queries are blocked"\n      - fieldname: tenantDataBackupIsolation\n        description: "SharedBackup | PerTenantBackup | EncryptedShared — tenant-specific backup strategy"\n      - fieldname: tenantDataDeletion\n        description: "SoftDelete | HardDelete | CryptoShredding — how tenant data is removed on offboarding"\n      - fieldname: tenantDataExport\n        description: "SelfService | AdminAssisted | ApiExport — data portability for tenants"\n      - fieldname: tenantResourceQuotas\n        description: "Yes | No — whether storage/query quotas are enforced per tenant"\n      - fieldname: tenantIsolationTesting\n        description: "AutomatedTests | PenetrationTesting | Both — how tenant isolation is verified"\n      - fieldname: sharedReferenceDataAccess\n        description: "ReadOnly | CachedLocally | Replicated — how tenants access shared/global reference data"\n  dmp-form:\n    fields:\n      - fieldname: dynamicDataMaskingEnabled\n        description: "Yes | No — whether dynamic data masking is implemented in production"\n      - fieldname: dynamicMaskingRules\n        description: "FullMask | PartialMask | Redact | Tokenize — available masking transformations"\n      - fieldname: dynamicMaskingScope\n        description: "RoleBased | QueryBased | ColumnBased — how masking rules are applied"\n      - fieldname: staticMaskingForNonProduction\n        description: "Yes | No — whether production data is statically masked before copying to test/dev"\n      - fieldname: staticMaskingTool\n        description: "BuiltIn | ThirdParty | CustomScript — tool used for static data masking"\n      - fieldname: maskingPreservesFormat\n        description: "Yes | No — whether masked data maintains original format and referential integrity"\n      - fieldname: maskingReversibility\n        description: "Irreversible | Tokenized | Deterministic — whether masking can be reversed"\n      - fieldname: piiMaskingPolicy\n        description: "FullRedact | PartialMask | Pseudonymize — specific masking approach for PII fields"\n      - fieldname: emailMaskingFormat\n        description: "e.g., j***@example.com or completely redacted — how email addresses are masked"\n      - fieldname: phoneMaskingFormat\n        description: "e.g., ***-***-1234 or fully redacted — how phone numbers are masked"\n      - fieldname: addressMaskingFormat\n        description: "CityOnly | ZipCodeOnly | FullRedact — how addresses are masked"\n      - fieldname: financialDataMasking\n        description: "FullRedact | Last4Digits | Tokenized — how financial data (credit cards, bank accounts) is masked"\n      - fieldname: maskingAuditTrail\n        description: "Yes | No — whether masking/unmasking operations are audited"\n      - fieldname: developmentDataStrategy\n        description: "MaskedCopy | SyntheticData | SubsetExtract | SeedData — strategy for development/test environments"\n  daap-form:\n    fields:\n      - fieldname: dataAccessLoggingEnabled\n        description: "Yes | No — whether data access events are logged"\n      - fieldname: dataAccessLoggingScope\n        description: "AllTables | SensitiveTablesOnly | ByClassification — which data access is logged"\n      - fieldname: loggedOperations\n        description: "Read | Write | Delete | SchemaChange | All — which operations are captured"\n      - fieldname: dataAccessLogDetail\n        description: "QueryText | AffectedRows | ColumnAccess | Minimal — what detail is recorded per event"\n      - fieldname: queryTextLogging\n        description: "Full | Sanitized | HashOnly | Disabled — whether executed query text is logged"\n      - fieldname: anomalyDetectionEnabled\n        description: "Yes | No — whether unusual data access patterns trigger alerts"\n      - fieldname: anomalySignals\n        description: "BulkExport | OffHoursAccess | UnusualVolume | NewAccessPattern — signals monitored"\n      - fieldname: dataBreachDetection\n        description: "RealTime | BatchReview | ThirdPartyDLP — how potential data exfiltration is detected"\n      - fieldname: dataAccessReviewCycle\n        description: "Monthly | Quarterly | Annually — how often data access permissions are reviewed"\n      - fieldname: privilegedQueryAlerts\n        description: "Yes | No — whether queries by privileged accounts trigger real-time alerts"\n      - fieldname: complianceReportingEnabled\n        description: "Yes | No — whether automated compliance reports are generated from access logs"\n      - fieldname: dataAccessRetention\n        description: "Duration data access logs are retained (e.g., 90d, 1y, 7y)"\n  aap-form:\n    fields:\n      - fieldname: authenticationMethod\n        required: true\n        description: "OAuth2 | APIKey | JWT | mTLS | HMAC | Basic — primary API authentication mechanism"\n      - fieldname: multipleMethodsSupported\n        description: "Yes | No — whether the API supports multiple authentication methods simultaneously"\n      - fieldname: apiKeyTransmission\n        description: "Header | QueryParam | Cookie — where API keys are transmitted (Header recommended)"\n      - fieldname: apiKeyRotationPolicy\n        description: Automatic periodic rotation interval and overlap/grace period for old keys\n      - fieldname: apiKeyScoping\n        description: "Global | PerEnvironment | PerService — whether keys are scoped to specific environments or services"\n      - fieldname: jwtValidationPolicy\n        description: "iss, aud, exp, nbf — required JWT claims to validate on every request"\n      - fieldname: jwtSigningAlgorithm\n        description: "RS256 | ES256 | EdDSA — required JWT signing algorithm (HS256 discouraged for APIs)"\n      - fieldname: accessTokenLifetime\n        description: "Maximum access token validity duration (e.g. 15 min, 1 hour)"\n      - fieldname: refreshTokenPolicy\n        description: "Rotation | Reuse | None — refresh token handling and lifetime"\n      - fieldname: clientCredentialsFlow\n        description: "Yes | No — whether OAuth2 client credentials flow is supported for service-to-service"\n      - fieldname: authorizationCodeFlow\n        description: "Yes | No — whether OAuth2 authorization code flow with PKCE is supported"\n      - fieldname: tokenRevocationSupport\n        description: "Yes | No — whether explicit token revocation is supported (RFC 7009)"\n      - fieldname: mutualTlsRequired\n        description: "Yes | No — require client certificate authentication for service-to-service communication"\n      - fieldname: serviceAccountPolicy\n        description: How service accounts authenticate and what credential types they use\n      - fieldname: webhookSignatureVerification\n        description: "HMAC-SHA256 | RSA | EdDSA — method used to verify incoming webhook requests"\n      - fieldname: thirdPartyApiConsumption\n        description: Security requirements when consuming external third-party APIs (OWASP API10)\n      - fieldname: credentialTransmission\n        description: "Header | Body — where credentials are transmitted (Header via Authorization recommended)"\n      - fieldname: bearerTokenFormat\n        description: "JWT | Opaque | Reference — format used for bearer tokens"\n      - fieldname: notes\n        description: Additional API authentication notes\n  apaupo-form:\n    fields:\n      - fieldname: objectLevelAuthorization\n        required: true\n        description: How every API endpoint verifies the caller owns or may access the requested object (OWASP API1)\n      - fieldname: functionLevelAuthorization\n        description: How administrative vs. regular functions are separated and access-controlled (OWASP API5)\n      - fieldname: propertyLevelAuthorization\n        description: How field-level exposure is controlled — preventing excessive data exposure and mass assignment (OWASP API3)\n      - fieldname: permissionGranularity\n        description: "Endpoint | Resource | Field — granularity at which permissions are evaluated"\n      - fieldname: scopeDefinitions\n        description: "OAuth2 scopes required for API access (e.g. read:users, write:orders)"\n      - fieldname: scopeEnforcementLevel\n        description: "Gateway | Service | Both — where scope checks are enforced"\n      - fieldname: delegatedAccessPolicy\n        description: How delegation or impersonation is controlled (on-behalf-of flows)\n      - fieldname: bulkOperationAuthorization\n        description: How batch/bulk API operations are authorized — per-item or at collection level\n      - fieldname: contextualAuthorization\n        description: "IP, time-of-day, device, or geolocation-based access decisions"\n      - fieldname: massAssignmentPrevention\n        description: "How mass assignment attacks are prevented — allowlisted fields, DTOs, read-only markers"\n      - fieldname: horizontalPrivilegeEscalation\n        description: Controls preventing a user from accessing another user\'s data via direct object reference\n      - fieldname: verticalPrivilegeEscalation\n        description: Controls preventing regular users from accessing administrative functions\n      - fieldname: sensitiveBusinessFlowProtection\n        description: "How sensitive workflows (checkout, transfer) are protected from automated abuse (OWASP API6)"\n      - fieldname: workflowStateValidation\n        description: How out-of-order API execution is prevented (server-side state machine enforcement)\n      - fieldname: notes\n        description: Additional API authorization notes\n  arvp-form:\n    fields:\n      - fieldname: inputValidationStrategy\n        required: true\n        description: "Allowlist | Blocklist | SchemaValidation — primary validation approach (Allowlist recommended)"\n      - fieldname: schemaValidationEnforced\n        description: "Yes | No — whether JSON Schema or OpenAPI schema validation is enforced on all requests"\n      - fieldname: schemaValidationTool\n        description: Library or framework used for request schema validation\n      - fieldname: contentTypeValidation\n        description: "Yes | No — whether Content-Type header is validated against expected types"\n      - fieldname: acceptedContentTypes\n        description: "application/json | application/xml — comma-separated list of accepted content types"\n      - fieldname: rejectUnexpectedContentType\n        description: "Yes | No — respond with HTTP 415 for unsupported media types"\n      - fieldname: requestSizeLimit\n        description: "Maximum request body size (e.g. 1 MB, 10 MB) — reject with HTTP 413"\n      - fieldname: arrayLengthLimit\n        description: Maximum number of elements allowed in any JSON array in request body\n      - fieldname: nestedObjectDepthLimit\n        description: Maximum nesting depth for JSON objects to prevent DoS via deep nesting\n      - fieldname: stringFieldMaxLength\n        description: Default maximum character length for string fields unless overridden per field\n      - fieldname: parameterTypeEnforcement\n        description: "Yes | No — enforce strong typing (number, boolean, date) on query/path parameters"\n      - fieldname: numericRangeValidation\n        description: "Yes | No — enforce min/max bounds on numeric parameters"\n      - fieldname: dateFormatValidation\n        description: "ISO 8601 | RFC 3339 | Custom — required date/time format for all date fields"\n      - fieldname: encodingValidation\n        description: "UTF-8 | ASCII — accepted character encoding for request bodies"\n      - fieldname: fileUploadValidation\n        description: "Allowed extensions, MIME types, max file size, and content scanning requirements"\n      - fieldname: notes\n        description: Additional request validation notes\n  apcose-form:\n    fields:\n      - fieldname: corsEnabled\n        required: true\n        description: "Yes | No — whether CORS is enabled for the API"\n      - fieldname: allowedOrigins\n        description: "Explicit domain list or pattern — avoid wildcard * with credentials"\n      - fieldname: allowedMethods\n        description: "GET | POST | PUT | DELETE | PATCH — permitted HTTP methods"\n      - fieldname: allowedHeaders\n        description: "Authorization, Content-Type, X-Request-ID — allowed request headers"\n      - fieldname: exposedHeaders\n        description: "X-RateLimit-Remaining, X-Request-ID — response headers visible to client JavaScript"\n      - fieldname: credentialsAllowed\n        description: "Yes | No — Access-Control-Allow-Credentials (mutually exclusive with wildcard origin)"\n      - fieldname: preflightCacheMaxAge\n        description: Maximum time in seconds that preflight responses can be cached (e.g. 3600)\n      - fieldname: wildcardRestriction\n        description: "Yes | No — whether wildcard * origin is explicitly prohibited when credentials are used"\n      - fieldname: contentSecurityPolicy\n        description: "CSP directives for API responses (e.g. default-src none, frame-ancestors none)"\n      - fieldname: strictTransportSecurity\n        description: HSTS max-age and includeSubDomains directive for API endpoints\n      - fieldname: securityHeadersRequired\n        description: "X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff, X-Frame-Options: DENY, Referrer-Policy: no-referrer"\n      - fieldname: privateNetworkAccess\n        description: How CORS private network access requests are handled (Access-Control-Request-Private-Network)\n      - fieldname: notes\n        description: Additional CORS security notes\n  apabpr-form:\n    fields:\n      - fieldname: rateLimitingEnabled\n        required: true\n        description: "Yes | No — whether security-focused rate limiting is enforced"\n      - fieldname: rateLimitScope\n        description: "PerClient | PerEndpoint | PerTenant | Global — at what level limits are applied"\n      - fieldname: authenticationEndpointLimits\n        description: Stricter rate limits for login/token endpoints to prevent brute-force attacks\n      - fieldname: sensitiveEndpointLimits\n        description: "Additional rate limits for password reset, MFA enrolment, payment endpoints"\n      - fieldname: bruteForceProtection\n        description: "Account lockout, progressive delays, CAPTCHA — how brute force authentication attacks are mitigated"\n      - fieldname: botDetectionPolicy\n        description: "CAPTCHA | BehavioralAnalysis | DeviceFingerprint | None — automated request detection"\n      - fieldname: ipReputationFiltering\n        description: "Yes | No — use IP reputation databases to filter known-malicious sources"\n      - fieldname: automaticBlocking\n        description: "Yes | No — automatically block clients exceeding abuse thresholds"\n      - fieldname: blockDuration\n        description: Temporary (minutes/hours) or permanent — duration of automatic blocks\n      - fieldname: geographicRestrictions\n        description: Region or country-based access restrictions for API endpoints\n      - fieldname: requestThrottlingOnFailure\n        description: Progressive delay or backoff on repeated authentication or validation failures\n      - fieldname: businessFlowProtection\n        description: How automated abuse of business-critical flows is detected and prevented (OWASP API6)\n      - fieldname: webhookFloodProtection\n        description: How webhook replay attacks and flood scenarios are prevented\n      - fieldname: notes\n        description: Additional abuse protection notes\n  apsemo-form:\n    fields:\n      - fieldname: apiAccessLogging\n        required: true\n        description: "Yes | No — whether all API access is logged with caller identity and action"\n      - fieldname: loggedAttributes\n        description: "Timestamp, clientId, endpoint, method, statusCode, responseTime, sourceIP — attributes captured per request"\n      - fieldname: sensitiveEndpointMonitoring\n        description: "Yes | No — enhanced logging for authentication, payment, and admin endpoints"\n      - fieldname: sensitiveDataRedaction\n        description: "Yes | No — redact PII, credentials, and tokens from API logs"\n      - fieldname: anomalyDetection\n        description: "Yes | No — detect anomalous API usage patterns (unusual volume, timing, geography)"\n      - fieldname: errorRateMonitoring\n        description: "Threshold and window for error-rate alerting (e.g. >5% 4xx in 5-min window)"\n      - fieldname: authenticationFailureTracking\n        description: "Yes | No — track and alert on authentication failure patterns per client/IP"\n      - fieldname: dataExfiltrationDetection\n        description: "Yes | No — detect unusual data volume patterns that may indicate exfiltration"\n      - fieldname: apiVersionInventory\n        description: "Yes | No — maintain a current inventory of all API versions and endpoints (OWASP API9)"\n      - fieldname: deprecatedEndpointMonitoring\n        description: "Yes | No — monitor and alert on usage of deprecated API endpoints or versions"\n      - fieldname: realTimeAlerts\n        description: "Yes | No — trigger real-time security alerts on threshold breaches"\n      - fieldname: securityResponseAutomation\n        description: "Automated actions on security events — block, throttle, escalate, notify"\n      - fieldname: complianceReporting\n        description: Frequency and format of API security compliance reports\n      - fieldname: notes\n        description: Additional API security monitoring notes\n  fuvp-form:\n    fields:\n      - fieldname: extensionValidationStrategy\n        required: true\n        description: "Allowlist | Blocklist | Both — approach to file extension validation (Allowlist recommended)"\n      - fieldname: allowedFileExtensions\n        description: "Comma-separated list of permitted extensions (e.g. jpg, png, pdf, docx)"\n      - fieldname: blockedFileExtensions\n        description: "Comma-separated list of explicitly blocked extensions (e.g. exe, bat, sh, php, js)"\n      - fieldname: doubleExtensionPrevention\n        description: "Yes | No — prevent bypass via double extensions like .jpg.php"\n      - fieldname: contentTypeValidation\n        description: "Yes | No — validate MIME type from Content-Type header against allowed types"\n      - fieldname: fileSignatureValidation\n        description: "Yes | No — validate file magic bytes match the declared content type"\n      - fieldname: signatureMismatchAction\n        description: "Reject | Quarantine | Log — action when file signature does not match extension"\n      - fieldname: filenameStrategy\n        description: "GenerateUUID | SanitizeOriginal | Preserve — how filenames are handled on upload"\n      - fieldname: filenameMaxLength\n        description: Maximum allowed filename length in characters\n      - fieldname: filenameAllowedCharacters\n        description: "Alphanumeric, hyphen, underscore, period — allowed characters in filenames"\n      - fieldname: pathTraversalPrevention\n        description: "Yes | No — strip or reject path components (../, /) in filenames"\n      - fieldname: nullBytePrevention\n        description: "Yes | No — reject filenames containing null bytes (%00)"\n      - fieldname: maxFileSizeBytes\n        description: "Maximum individual file size (e.g. 10 MB, 50 MB, 1 GB)"\n      - fieldname: maxUploadBatchSize\n        description: Maximum total size for multi-file uploads in a single request\n      - fieldname: maxConcurrentUploads\n        description: Maximum number of simultaneous file uploads per user\n      - fieldname: compressedFileSizeLimit\n        description: Maximum decompressed size for ZIP/archive files to prevent ZIP bombs\n      - fieldname: imageRewriting\n        description: "Yes | No — rewrite/re-encode images to strip embedded metadata and malicious payloads"\n      - fieldname: documentSanitization\n        description: "Yes | No — apply Content Disarm & Reconstruct (CDR) to office documents and PDFs"\n      - fieldname: metadataStripping\n        description: "Yes | No — remove EXIF, XMP, and other embedded metadata from uploaded files"\n      - fieldname: notes\n        description: Additional file upload validation notes\n  stenpo-form:\n    fields:\n      - fieldname: encryptionAtRest\n        required: true\n        description: "Yes | No — whether stored files are encrypted at rest"\n      - fieldname: encryptionAlgorithm\n        description: "AES-256-GCM | AES-256-CBC | ChaCha20-Poly1305 — algorithm for file encryption"\n      - fieldname: encryptionScope\n        description: "Volume | Bucket | PerFile | PerTenant — granularity at which encryption keys are applied"\n      - fieldname: serverSideEncryption\n        description: "SSE-S3 | SSE-KMS | SSE-C | ManagedKey — server-side encryption method"\n      - fieldname: clientSideEncryption\n        description: "Yes | No — whether files are encrypted before upload by the client"\n      - fieldname: clientSideEncryptionMethod\n        description: "Envelope encryption, client-managed keys — method for client-side encryption"\n      - fieldname: fileKeyRotation\n        description: Frequency and method of rotating file encryption keys\n      - fieldname: perTenantKeys\n        description: "Yes | No — whether each tenant has its own encryption key for file storage"\n      - fieldname: keyDeletionOnTenantRemoval\n        description: "Yes | No — whether tenant file encryption keys are destroyed when tenant is deleted"\n      - fieldname: encryptionInTransit\n        description: "Yes | No — TLS for file upload/download transport"\n      - fieldname: minimumTlsVersion\n        description: "TLS 1.2 | TLS 1.3 — minimum TLS version for file transfers"\n      - fieldname: backupEncryption\n        description: "Yes | No — whether file storage backups are encrypted with the same or separate keys"\n      - fieldname: notes\n        description: Additional storage encryption notes\n  facp-form:\n    fields:\n      - fieldname: fileAccessModel\n        required: true\n        description: "OwnerBased | RoleBased | ACL | Capability — how file access permissions are determined"\n      - fieldname: authenticationRequired\n        description: "Yes | No — whether authentication is required for all file access"\n      - fieldname: anonymousDownloadAllowed\n        description: "Yes | No — whether any files can be downloaded without authentication (public files)"\n      - fieldname: fileOwnershipModel\n        description: "User | Tenant | SharedOwnership — who owns uploaded files by default"\n      - fieldname: permissionGranularity\n        description: "Read | Write | Delete | Share | Admin — permission types supported on files"\n      - fieldname: folderLevelPermissions\n        description: "Yes | No — whether permissions can be set at folder/directory level with inheritance"\n      - fieldname: permissionInheritance\n        description: "Inherit | Override | None — how folder permissions propagate to contained files"\n      - fieldname: sharingEnabled\n        description: "Yes | No — whether files can be shared with other users or externally"\n      - fieldname: shareableLinkSupport\n        description: "Yes | No — support for time-limited or password-protected shareable URLs"\n      - fieldname: shareableLinkExpiration\n        description: "Default expiration time for shareable links (e.g. 24 hours, 7 days, never)"\n      - fieldname: externalSharingPolicy\n        description: "Allowed | RestrictedDomains | Disabled — whether files can be shared outside the tenant"\n      - fieldname: storageLocationPolicy\n        description: "SeparateServer | OutsideWebroot | CloudBucket — where files are stored relative to application"\n      - fieldname: tenantStorageIsolation\n        description: "SeparateBucket | PrefixPartition | SharedWithACL — how tenant files are isolated in storage"\n      - fieldname: filesystemPermissions\n        description: "Least-privilege file permission policy (read-only for web server, write for upload service)"\n      - fieldname: presignedUrlSupport\n        description: "Yes | No — use pre-signed URLs for time-limited direct file access"\n      - fieldname: presignedUrlMaxExpiry\n        description: "Maximum validity period for pre-signed URLs (e.g. 15 min, 1 hour)"\n      - fieldname: notes\n        description: Additional file access control notes\n  coscpo-form:\n    fields:\n      - fieldname: antivirusScanningEnabled\n        required: true\n        description: "Yes | No — whether uploaded files are scanned by antivirus before acceptance"\n      - fieldname: scanTiming\n        description: "OnUpload | Asynchronous | OnAccess | Periodic — when scanning occurs"\n      - fieldname: scanEngine\n        description: "ClamAV | CloudProvider | ThirdPartyAPI | Multiple — scanning engine or service used"\n      - fieldname: quarantinePolicy\n        description: "Quarantine | Reject | NotifyAndQuarantine — action when malicious content is detected"\n      - fieldname: quarantineRetentionDays\n        description: Number of days quarantined files are retained before permanent deletion\n      - fieldname: signatureUpdateFrequency\n        description: "Hourly | Daily | RealTime — how often antivirus signatures are updated"\n      - fieldname: cdrEnabled\n        description: "Yes | No — whether CDR is applied to office documents, PDFs, and similar file types"\n      - fieldname: cdrApplicableTypes\n        description: "PDF | DOCX | XLSX | Images — file types processed by CDR"\n      - fieldname: dlpScanningEnabled\n        description: "Yes | No — scan file contents for sensitive data (PII, credit cards, health records)"\n      - fieldname: dlpPolicies\n        description: "Regex patterns, trained classifiers, keyword lists — methods for detecting sensitive data in files"\n      - fieldname: dlpAction\n        description: "Block | Redact | Notify | Quarantine — action when DLP detects sensitive content"\n      - fieldname: contentModeration\n        description: "Yes | No — scan for illegal, offensive, or policy-violating content"\n      - fieldname: moderationMethod\n        description: "Automated | ManualReview | Hybrid — approach to content moderation"\n      - fieldname: hashBasedDetection\n        description: "Yes | No — use file hash databases (e.g. VirusTotal) to detect known-malicious files"\n      - fieldname: notes\n        description: Additional content scanning notes\n  fdsp-form:\n    fields:\n      - fieldname: downloadAuthenticationRequired\n        required: true\n        description: "Yes | No — whether authentication is required for file downloads"\n      - fieldname: downloadRateLimiting\n        description: "Yes | No — rate limit file downloads per user/IP to prevent DoS"\n      - fieldname: downloadRateLimit\n        description: Maximum downloads per minute/hour/day per user or IP\n      - fieldname: bandwidthThrottling\n        description: "Yes | No — throttle download bandwidth per user to prevent abuse"\n      - fieldname: contentDispositionPolicy\n        description: "Attachment | Inline | PerType — how Content-Disposition header is set (Attachment recommended for untrusted content)"\n      - fieldname: cdnDelivery\n        description: "Yes | No — serve files through a CDN for performance and DDoS protection"\n      - fieldname: hotlinkPrevention\n        description: "Yes | No — prevent direct linking to files from external sites"\n      - fieldname: cacheControlPolicy\n        description: "NoStore | Private | PublicShortTTL — cache directives for file download responses"\n      - fieldname: downloadAuditLogging\n        description: "Yes | No — log all file download events with user, timestamp, file, and IP"\n      - fieldname: downloadAlerts\n        description: "Yes | No — alert on unusual download patterns (bulk downloads, sensitive files)"\n      - fieldname: watermarking\n        description: "Yes | No — apply invisible watermarks to downloaded files for traceability"\n      - fieldname: notes\n        description: Additional file download security notes\n  stlipo-form:\n    fields:\n      - fieldname: retentionPolicy\n        required: true\n        description: "TimeBased | Indefinite | ComplianceDriven — default file retention strategy"\n      - fieldname: defaultRetentionPeriod\n        description: "Default duration files are kept before eligible for deletion (e.g. 90 days, 7 years)"\n      - fieldname: retentionByFileType\n        description: "Yes | No — different retention periods for different file categories"\n      - fieldname: legalHoldSupport\n        description: "Yes | No — ability to place legal holds preventing deletion regardless of retention policy"\n      - fieldname: archivingEnabled\n        description: "Yes | No — whether files are moved to low-cost archival tiers after a defined period"\n      - fieldname: archivalStorageTier\n        description: "Glacier | ColdStorage | NearlineStorage — target tier for archived files"\n      - fieldname: archivalTransitionDays\n        description: Number of days after last access before files move to archival storage\n      - fieldname: versioningEnabled\n        description: "Yes | No — maintain previous versions of overwritten or modified files"\n      - fieldname: maxVersions\n        description: Maximum number of previous versions to retain per file\n      - fieldname: versionRetentionDays\n        description: Number of days previous versions are retained\n      - fieldname: backupSchedule\n        description: "Daily | Hourly | Continuous — frequency of file storage backups"\n      - fieldname: backupRetentionDays\n        description: Number of days file backups are retained\n      - fieldname: crossRegionReplication\n        description: "Yes | No — replicate file storage to a secondary region for disaster recovery"\n      - fieldname: secureDeletionMethod\n        description: "CryptoShred | Overwrite | StandardDelete — method for permanent file deletion"\n      - fieldname: deletionConfirmation\n        description: "Yes | No — require explicit confirmation or approval for permanent file deletion"\n      - fieldname: deletionAuditLogging\n        description: "Yes | No — log all file deletion events for compliance and forensics"\n      - fieldname: notes\n        description: Additional storage lifecycle notes\n  acms-form:\n    fields:\n      - fieldname: primaryModel\n        required: true\n        description: "RBAC | ABAC | ReBAC | Hybrid-RBAC-ABAC | Hybrid-RBAC-ReBAC | Hybrid-ABAC-ReBAC | Hybrid-All — primary access control paradigm"\n      - fieldname: modelRationale\n        description: Why this model was chosen over alternatives\n      - fieldname: rbacEnabled\n        description: "Yes | No — role-based access control with permissions assigned to roles rather than directly to users"\n      - fieldname: abacEnabled\n        description: "Yes | No — attribute-based access control using subject, resource, action, and environment attributes per NIST SP 800-162"\n      - fieldname: rebacEnabled\n        description: "Yes | No — relationship-based access control granting access based on relationships between resources and users (e.g. Zanzibar model)"\n      - fieldname: policyLanguage\n        description: "XACML | OPA-Rego | CedarPolicy | CustomDSL | None — formal policy language for expressing access control rules"\n      - fieldname: policyDecisionPoint\n        description: "Embedded | ExternalPDP | Sidecar | CloudService — where access control decisions are evaluated"\n      - fieldname: policyEnforcementPoint\n        description: "APIGateway | Middleware | ServiceMesh | InApplication — where access control decisions are enforced"\n      - fieldname: policyAdministrationPoint\n        description: "AdminUI | ConfigFile | PolicyRepository | ExternalService — where policies are managed and maintained"\n      - fieldname: policyInformationPoint\n        description: "UserDirectory | AttributeStore | ExternalIdP | Database — source of attributes used in access decisions"\n      - fieldname: delegationModel\n        description: "None | Administrative | UserInitiated | Hierarchical — whether and how permissions can be delegated between users"\n      - fieldname: notes\n        description: Additional access control model selection notes\n  pegrpo-form:\n    fields:\n      - fieldname: functionLevelControl\n        description: "Yes | No — permissions control access to entire functions, operations, or API endpoints"\n      - fieldname: dataLevelControl\n        description: "Yes | No — permissions control access to specific data records, rows, or resource instances (horizontal access control)"\n      - fieldname: fieldLevelControl\n        description: "Yes | No — permissions control access to individual fields or attributes within a record (column-level security)"\n      - fieldname: uiElementControl\n        description: "Yes | No — permissions control visibility or availability of UI components, menus, or actions"\n      - fieldname: apiOperationControl\n        description: "Yes | No — permissions are specific to individual API operations (GET, POST, PUT, DELETE on specific resources)"\n      - fieldname: objectLevelControl\n        description: "Yes | No — permissions apply to individual business object instances (IDOR prevention through ownership checks)"\n      - fieldname: tenantLevelControl\n        description: "Yes | No — permissions provide isolation between tenants in a multi-tenant system"\n      - fieldname: finestGranularity\n        description: "Function | Data | Field | UIElement | APIOperation | Object — the finest level of permission granularity supported"\n      - fieldname: dynamicPermissions\n        description: "Yes | No — permissions can change dynamically based on runtime context (time, location, device, risk score)"\n      - fieldname: notes\n        description: Additional permission granularity notes\n  pecost-form:\n    fields:\n      - fieldname: compositionModel\n        required: true\n        description: "Additive | Subtractive | MostRestrictive | LeastRestrictive | OrderedPrecedence | WeightedPriority — how permissions compose"\n      - fieldname: defaultPolicy\n        required: true\n        description: "DenyByDefault | AllowByDefault — action when no explicit rule matches (OWASP: always deny by default)"\n      - fieldname: explicitDenyOverride\n        description: "Yes | No — whether explicit deny always overrides any allow (deny-trumps-allow semantics)"\n      - fieldname: rolePermissionInheritance\n        description: "Yes | No — whether child roles inherit permissions from parent roles in a hierarchy"\n      - fieldname: groupPermissionAggregation\n        description: "Union | Intersection | FirstMatch — how permissions from multiple group memberships combine"\n      - fieldname: conflictResolution\n        description: "DenyWins | AllowWins | MostSpecificWins | ExplicitWins | PriorityBased — how conflicting permissions are resolved"\n      - fieldname: permissionBoundary\n        description: "Yes | No — whether a maximum permission boundary constrains effective permissions regardless of assigned roles"\n      - fieldname: scopedPermissions\n        description: "Yes | No — whether permissions can be scoped to specific contexts (e.g. project, department, time window)"\n      - fieldname: temporaryElevation\n        description: "Yes | No — whether time-limited permission elevation is supported (just-in-time access, break-glass procedures)"\n      - fieldname: notes\n        description: Additional permission composition notes\n  accopo-form:\n    fields:\n      - fieldname: separationOfDuties\n        description: "Yes | No — enforce static or dynamic separation of duties to prevent conflicts of interest (e.g. creator cannot approve)"\n      - fieldname: sodEnforcement\n        description: "Static | Dynamic | Both — whether separation of duties is enforced at role-assignment time (static) or at runtime (dynamic)"\n      - fieldname: temporalConstraints\n        description: "Yes | No — time-based access restrictions (business hours, maintenance windows, embargo periods)"\n      - fieldname: locationConstraints\n        description: "Yes | No — geographic or network-based access restrictions (IP range, geofencing, VPN requirement)"\n      - fieldname: deviceConstraints\n        description: "Yes | No — device-based access restrictions (managed devices, compliance status, device type)"\n      - fieldname: riskAdaptiveAccess\n        description: "Yes | No — access decisions consider real-time risk scores (user behavior, threat intelligence, anomaly detection)"\n      - fieldname: contextualAttributes\n        description: "Comma-separated list of contextual attributes used in access decisions (e.g. time, location, device, riskScore, authenticationLevel, networkZone)"\n      - fieldname: maxSessionPermissions\n        description: "Yes | No — limit the maximum number of active permissions per session to reduce exposure from compromised sessions"\n      - fieldname: leastPrivilegeEnforcement\n        description: "Manual | Automated | ContinuousReview — how least privilege principle is enforced and verified over time"\n      - fieldname: privilegeCreepDetection\n        description: "Yes | No — automatically detect users who accumulate excessive permissions over time through role changes"\n      - fieldname: notes\n        description: Additional access constraint notes\n  peevbe-form:\n    fields:\n      - fieldname: evaluationLocation\n        required: true\n        description: "ServerSide | Gateway | ServiceMesh | Serverless — where permission checks are performed (OWASP: never client-side only)"\n      - fieldname: evaluationFrequency\n        required: true\n        description: "EveryRequest | SessionStart | Cached | Lazy — how often permissions are re-evaluated (OWASP: validate on every request)"\n      - fieldname: cachingStrategy\n        description: "None | ShortLived | SessionBound | DistributedCache — permission decision caching approach and TTL"\n      - fieldname: cacheTtlSeconds\n        description: Maximum time in seconds before cached permission decisions expire\n      - fieldname: failureMode\n        required: true\n        description: "DenyOnFailure | LastKnownGood | DegradedAccess — behavior when the authorization service is unavailable (OWASP: exit safely)"\n      - fieldname: authorizationLogging\n        description: "Yes | No — log all access control decisions including grants and denials for audit and incident response"\n      - fieldname: logDeniedRequests\n        description: "Yes | No — log details of all denied access attempts"\n      - fieldname: logSuccessfulAccess\n        description: "Yes | No — log successful access to sensitive resources for forensic analysis"\n      - fieldname: automatedTesting\n        description: "Yes | No — unit and integration tests verify authorization logic (OWASP: catch low-hanging security issues early)"\n      - fieldname: clientSideHints\n        description: "Yes | No — provide permission hints to UI for UX purposes while enforcing all checks server-side"\n      - fieldname: notes\n        description: Additional permission evaluation behavior notes\n  ares-form:\n    fields:\n      - fieldname: roleScope\n        description: "Global | Tenant | Department | Project | Team | Custom — organizational scope where this role is applicable"\n      - fieldname: inheritsFrom\n        description: Parent role name or "none" for top-level roles; child roles inherit all permissions of the parent\n      - fieldname: permissionSet\n        description: "Comma-separated permission keys summarizing the role\'s access (e.g. user.manage, config.read, audit.read)"\n  areg-form:\n    fields:\n      - fieldname: riskLevel\n        description: Privilege risk classification for access review prioritization.\n      - fieldname: maxHolders\n        description: Maximum number of users who can hold this role concurrently; 0 = unlimited\n      - fieldname: activationType\n        description: "AlwaysActive | OnDemand | TimeLimited | Scheduled — whether the role is permanently active or requires activation"\n      - fieldname: activationDuration\n        description: "Maximum duration for on-demand or time-limited activation (e.g. 8h, 24h, 7d)"\n      - fieldname: approvalRequired\n        description: "Yes | No — whether role assignment requires explicit approval"\n      - fieldname: approver\n        description: "Role or person responsible for approving role assignments (e.g. Line Manager, Security Officer, System Owner)"\n  arel-form:\n    fields:\n      - fieldname: provisioningMethod\n        description: "Manual | Automatic | ApprovalBased | SelfService | RuleBased — how the role is assigned to users"\n      - fieldname: reviewFrequency\n        description: "Monthly | Quarterly | SemiAnnual | Annual | OnChange | Never — how often role assignments are reviewed for appropriateness"\n  auroenst-form:\n    fields:\n      - fieldname: dataAccessScope\n        description: "AllData | TenantData | DepartmentData | TeamData | OwnData | None — breadth of data accessible through this role"\n      - fieldname: isDefault\n        description: "Yes | No — automatically assigned to new users upon creation"\n      - fieldname: isSystem\n        description: "Yes | No — system-defined role that cannot be modified or deleted by administrators"\n      - fieldname: notes\n        description: Additional role definition notes\n  rohipo-form:\n    fields:\n      - fieldname: hierarchyModel\n        required: true\n        description: "Tree | DAG | Flat | Layered — structure of the role hierarchy (tree = single parent, DAG = multiple parents, flat = no inheritance, layered = tiered levels)"\n      - fieldname: maxHierarchyDepth\n        description: Maximum number of inheritance levels allowed (e.g. 5); 0 = unlimited depth\n      - fieldname: inheritanceMode\n        description: "Full | Selective | None — whether child roles automatically inherit all parent permissions (full), selected permissions (selective), or none"\n      - fieldname: multipleInheritance\n        description: "Yes | No — whether a role can inherit from more than one parent role (DAG model)"\n      - fieldname: permissionOverride\n        description: "Yes | No — whether child roles can override (restrict or extend) inherited permissions from parent roles"\n      - fieldname: activationConstraints\n        description: "Yes | No — whether role activation is subject to constraints (time-based, prerequisite roles, approval workflows)"\n      - fieldname: maxActiveRolesPerUser\n        description: Maximum number of roles a single user can hold simultaneously; 0 = unlimited\n      - fieldname: rolePriorityScheme\n        description: "HierarchyLevel | ExplicitWeight | None — how conflicts between equal-level roles are resolved"\n      - fieldname: automaticInheritanceRevocation\n        description: "Yes | No — whether removing a parent role automatically revokes inherited child-role permissions"\n      - fieldname: notes\n        description: Additional role hierarchy policy notes\n  rocepo-form:\n    fields:\n      - fieldname: certificationRequired\n        description: "Yes | No — whether periodic role certification (access review) is mandated"\n      - fieldname: certificationFrequency\n        description: "Monthly | Quarterly | SemiAnnual | Annual | OnChange — how often role certifications are conducted"\n      - fieldname: certifier\n        description: "Manager | RoleOwner | SecurityOfficer | Automated — who performs the certification review"\n      - fieldname: nonResponseAction\n        description: "Revoke | Escalate | Extend | NoAction — what happens if the certifier does not respond within the deadline"\n      - fieldname: riskBasedScheduling\n        description: "Yes | No — whether high-risk role assignments are reviewed more frequently than low-risk ones"\n      - fieldname: automatedDetection\n        description: "Yes | No — whether the system automatically detects and flags anomalous or dormant role assignments"\n      - fieldname: dormantRoleThresholdDays\n        description: Number of days after which an unused role assignment is flagged as dormant (e.g. 90)\n      - fieldname: certificationAuditTrail\n        description: "Yes | No — whether certification decisions are logged for compliance and audit purposes"\n      - fieldname: notes\n        description: Additional role certification notes\n  tecopo-form:\n    fields:\n      - fieldname: contextResolutionMethod\n        required: true\n        description: "Token | Header | Domain | Path | Session | IDP-Asserted — how tenant identity is determined from incoming requests"\n      - fieldname: contextPropagation\n        description: "ThreadLocal | RequestScoped | ServiceMesh | TokenBased — how tenant context flows through application layers during authorization evaluation"\n      - fieldname: contextValidation\n        description: "SessionBinding | TokenClaim | DatabaseLookup | IDP-Asserted — how tenant context is validated against the authenticated user"\n      - fieldname: contextImmutability\n        description: "Yes | No — whether the tenant context is immutable once established for a request (prevents mid-request tampering)"\n      - fieldname: crossServicePropagation\n        description: "JwtClaim | Header | gRPC-Metadata | ContextObject — how tenant context propagates across service boundaries in distributed architectures"\n      - fieldname: missingContextBehavior\n        description: "Reject | DefaultTenant | Anonymous — what happens when tenant context cannot be determined (reject = deny access; defaultTenant = use platform default)"\n      - fieldname: notes\n        description: Additional tenant context policy notes\n  ctap-form:\n    fields:\n      - fieldname: crossTenantAccessAllowed\n        required: true\n        description: "Yes | No — whether any form of cross-tenant access is permitted in the system"\n      - fieldname: crossTenantAccessModel\n        description: "GlobalAdmin | ServiceAccount | ExplicitGrant | Federation | None — model governing how cross-tenant access is structured"\n      - fieldname: authorizationMechanism\n        description: "SuperAdminRole | ServiceAccountToken | ExplicitGrant | FederationAgreement — how cross-tenant operations are authorized when allowed"\n      - fieldname: resourceSharingModel\n        description: "None | ReferenceOnly | Copy | SharedOwnership | Linked — how resources can be shared across tenant boundaries"\n      - fieldname: idorPreventionStrategy\n        description: "CompositeKeys | QueryFilter | RLS | ScopedTokens — strategy to prevent insecure direct object references across tenants"\n      - fieldname: crossTenantAuditRequirement\n        description: "All | AdminOnly | None — level of audit logging required for cross-tenant operations"\n      - fieldname: accessReviewFrequency\n        description: "Monthly | Quarterly | SemiAnnual | Annual | OnChange — how often cross-tenant access grants are reviewed"\n      - fieldname: notes\n        description: Additional cross-tenant access policy notes\n  teonpo-form:\n    fields:\n      - fieldname: authorizationProvisioningModel\n        required: true\n        description: "Template | Clone | Custom | Minimal — how authorization resources (roles, permissions, policies) are provisioned for new tenants"\n      - fieldname: defaultRoleTemplate\n        description: "Name or ID of the role template used to bootstrap initial roles for a new tenant (e.g. StandardSaaS, Enterprise, Minimal)"\n      - fieldname: adminRoleProvisioning\n        description: "AutoCreate | ManualAssign | InviteBased — how the initial tenant administrator role is set up"\n      - fieldname: initialPermissionSet\n        description: "Full | Minimal | Custom — what permissions are granted to a new tenant upon creation"\n      - fieldname: offboardingStrategy\n        description: "SoftDelete | HardDelete | Archive | Anonymize — how tenant authorization data is handled on offboarding"\n      - fieldname: resourceCleanupOnOffboarding\n        description: "Immediate | Deferred | Manual | PolicyBased — when authorization resources are cleaned up after tenant removal"\n      - fieldname: dataRetentionDays\n        description: "Number of days tenant authorization data (roles, assignments, audit logs) is retained after offboarding (0 = immediate)"\n      - fieldname: offboardingApproval\n        description: "None | PlatformAdmin | ComplianceOfficer | Both — who must approve tenant offboarding and data deletion"\n      - fieldname: notes\n        description: Additional tenant onboarding/offboarding notes\n  tbep-form:\n    fields:\n      - fieldname: enforcementLayer\n        required: true\n        description: "API | Service | Database | All — at which architectural layer tenant authorization boundaries are enforced"\n      - fieldname: authorizationFilterStrategy\n        description: "QueryFilter | TokenScope | PolicyEngine | Middleware — how tenant boundaries are applied in authorization decisions"\n      - fieldname: implicitTenantFilter\n        description: "Yes | No — whether all authorization queries automatically include a tenant filter (defense-in-depth)"\n      - fieldname: escalationPrevention\n        description: "StrictScoping | RoleSeparation | TokenIsolation | All — how privilege escalation across tenant boundaries is prevented"\n      - fieldname: sharedServiceAuthorization\n        description: "ServiceAccount | PlatformRole | TenantAgnostic | ScopedProxy — how shared platform services authorize operations that span or are independent of tenants"\n      - fieldname: tenantSwitchingPolicy\n        description: "ReAuthenticate | SessionSwitch | TokenExchange | NotAllowed — how users belonging to multiple tenants switch their active tenant context"\n      - fieldname: multiTenantUserSupport\n        description: "Yes | No — whether a single user identity can belong to and operate within multiple tenants"\n      - fieldname: authorizationCaching\n        description: "None | PerTenant | SharedWithValidation | InvalidateOnSwitch — how authorization decisions are cached with respect to tenant context to prevent cross-tenant cache leakage"\n      - fieldname: notes\n        description: Additional tenant boundary enforcement notes\n  earp-form:\n    fields:\n      - fieldname: defaultAlgorithm\n        required: true\n        description: "AES-256 | AES-128 | ChaCha20 | 3DES | Other — symmetric encryption algorithm used as the default for data at rest (AES-256 recommended per OWASP/NIST)"\n      - fieldname: defaultKeyLength\n        required: true\n        description: "128 | 192 | 256 — minimum key length in bits for symmetric encryption (256-bit recommended for sensitive data)"\n      - fieldname: cipherMode\n        description: "GCM | CCM | CTR | CBC | XTS — block cipher mode of operation (GCM or CCM recommended for authenticated encryption; XTS for full-disk encryption)"\n      - fieldname: encryptionLayer\n        description: "Application | Database | Filesystem | Hardware | Multiple — at which architectural layer encryption is primarily applied (multiple = defense-in-depth across layers)"\n      - fieldname: fieldLevelEncryption\n        description: "Yes | No — whether individual sensitive fields (e.g. SSN, credit card) are encrypted at the application level beyond database/disk encryption"\n      - fieldname: transparentDataEncryption\n        description: "Yes | No — whether TDE (Transparent Data Encryption) is used at the database engine level (e.g. SQL Server TDE, Oracle TDE, PostgreSQL pgcrypto)"\n      - fieldname: fullDiskEncryption\n        description: "Yes | No — whether full-disk or volume-level encryption is required (e.g. LUKS, BitLocker, AWS EBS encryption)"\n      - fieldname: minimizeSensitiveStorage\n        description: "Yes | No — whether the system actively minimizes storage of sensitive data (e.g. tokenization, truncation, avoiding unnecessary PII retention)"\n      - fieldname: complianceFramework\n        description: "FIPS-140-2 | PCI-DSS | HIPAA | GDPR | SOC2 | None — regulatory or compliance framework dictating encryption requirements"\n      - fieldname: notes\n        description: Additional encryption at rest policy notes\n  daenpo-form:\n    fields:\n      - fieldname: databaseEncryptionMethod\n        required: true\n        description: "TDE | ColumnLevel | CellLevel | ApplicationLayer | None — method of encrypting data within the database"\n      - fieldname: encryptedColumnStrategy\n        description: "Deterministic | Randomized | Homomorphic | Envelope — how individual columns are encrypted (deterministic allows equality search; randomized provides stronger security)"\n      - fieldname: indexOnEncryptedColumns\n        description: "Yes | No — whether indexes are maintained on encrypted columns (requires deterministic encryption or specialized schemes)"\n      - fieldname: searchOnEncryptedData\n        description: "None | DeterministicMatch | BlindIndex | Searchable Encryption | DecryptThenSearch — strategy for querying encrypted data without full decryption"\n      - fieldname: connectionEncryption\n        description: "Yes | No — whether database connections use TLS/SSL for data in transit to/from the database"\n      - fieldname: databaseEngine\n        description: "PostgreSQL | MySQL | SQLServer | Oracle | MongoDB | Other — target database engine (encryption capabilities vary by engine)"\n      - fieldname: notes\n        description: Additional database encryption notes\n  fsep-form:\n    fields:\n      - fieldname: fileEncryptionMethod\n        required: true\n        description: "FileLevel | VolumeLevel | ObjectLevel | ClientSide | ServerSide | None — how files and blobs are encrypted at rest"\n      - fieldname: cloudStorageEncryption\n        description: "SSE-S3 | SSE-KMS | SSE-C | AzureSSE | GCS-CMEK | None — cloud provider server-side encryption method if applicable"\n      - fieldname: clientSideEncryption\n        description: "Yes | No — whether files are encrypted before upload (client-side encryption for defense-in-depth)"\n      - fieldname: encryptedFileFormats\n        description: "Comma-separated list of file types that must be encrypted (e.g. PDF, XLSX, CSV, backup dumps, log archives)"\n      - fieldname: localDeviceEncryption\n        description: "Yes | No — whether local device storage (mobile, desktop) must be encrypted for cached or offline data"\n      - fieldname: temporaryFileEncryption\n        description: "Yes | No — whether temporary files and caches must be encrypted (prevents data leakage through temp files)"\n      - fieldname: notes\n        description: Additional file and storage encryption notes\n  baenpo-form:\n    fields:\n      - fieldname: backupEncryptionRequired\n        required: true\n        description: "Yes | No — whether all backups (database, file, system) must be encrypted"\n      - fieldname: backupEncryptionMethod\n        description: "SameAsSource | SeparateKey | EnvelopeEncryption | CloudProviderManaged — how backup data is encrypted (SameAsSource = same keys as live data)"\n      - fieldname: separateBackupKeys\n        description: "Yes | No — whether backups use separate encryption keys from production data (recommended for key rotation independence)"\n      - fieldname: backupKeyRotation\n        description: "OnEveryBackup | Monthly | Quarterly | Annual | OnKeyChange — how often backup encryption keys are rotated"\n      - fieldname: encryptedBackupVerification\n        description: "Yes | No — whether backup integrity and encryption are periodically verified through test restores"\n      - fieldname: offSiteBackupEncryption\n        description: "Yes | No — whether off-site or disaster recovery backups have additional encryption requirements"\n      - fieldname: notes\n        description: Additional backup encryption notes\n  tlprpo-form:\n    fields:\n      - fieldname: minimumTlsVersion\n        required: true\n        description: "TLS1.2 | TLS1.3 — minimum acceptable TLS version (TLS 1.3 recommended; TLS 1.0/1.1 are deprecated and should not be used; PCI DSS forbids TLS 1.0)"\n      - fieldname: preferredTlsVersion\n        description: "TLS1.3 | TLS1.2 — preferred TLS version for new connections (TLS 1.3 provides improved security and performance)"\n      - fieldname: allowedCipherSuites\n        description: "Comma-separated cipher suite names or categories (e.g. TLS_AES_256_GCM_SHA384, TLS_CHACHA20_POLY1305_SHA256; disable NULL, Anonymous, EXPORT, DES, RC4 ciphers)"\n      - fieldname: preferAuthenticatedEncryption\n        description: "Yes | No — whether GCM/CCM authenticated cipher modes are preferred over CBC (recommended: Yes)"\n      - fieldname: dhGroups\n        description: "Comma-separated DH groups for key exchange (e.g. x25519, prime256v1, ffdhe3072; per RFC 7919)"\n      - fieldname: tlsCompressionDisabled\n        description: "Yes | No — whether TLS compression is disabled to prevent CRIME/BREACH attacks (recommended: Yes)"\n      - fieldname: sessionResumption\n        description: "Tickets | SessionID | None — TLS session resumption mechanism (tickets recommended for TLS 1.3; session IDs for TLS 1.2)"\n      - fieldname: complianceFramework\n        description: "FIPS-140-2 | PCI-DSS | HIPAA | NIST-800-52 | None — regulatory framework dictating TLS requirements"\n      - fieldname: notes\n        description: Additional TLS protocol policy notes\n  cemapo-form:\n    fields:\n      - fieldname: certificateAuthority\n        required: true\n        description: "LetsEncrypt | DigiCert | GlobalSign | InternalCA | Other — certificate authority used for issuing TLS certificates"\n      - fieldname: validationType\n        description: "DV | OV | EV — Domain Validated, Organization Validated, or Extended Validation (DV is sufficient for most applications; EV provides no additional browser security benefits)"\n      - fieldname: minimumKeyLength\n        description: "2048 | 3072 | 4096 — minimum RSA key length in bits for certificates (2048 minimum per NIST; 3072+ recommended)"\n      - fieldname: keyType\n        description: "RSA | ECDSA | Ed25519 — certificate key type (ECDSA with P-256/P-384 or Ed25519 preferred for performance; RSA for broadest compatibility)"\n      - fieldname: hashingAlgorithm\n        description: "SHA-256 | SHA-384 | SHA-512 — certificate hashing algorithm (SHA-256 minimum; MD5 and SHA-1 must not be used)"\n      - fieldname: wildcardCertificatePolicy\n        description: "Allowed | Restricted | Prohibited — policy on wildcard certificates (* certs; use with caution per OWASP — violates least privilege principle)"\n      - fieldname: certificateLifetimeDays\n        description: "Maximum certificate validity in days (e.g. 90 for LetsEncrypt auto-renewal, 365 for annual, 730 for 2-year)"\n      - fieldname: automatedRenewal\n        description: "Yes | No — whether certificates are automatically renewed via ACME or similar protocol before expiration"\n      - fieldname: certificateTransparency\n        description: "Yes | No — whether certificates are logged in Certificate Transparency logs for public auditability"\n      - fieldname: caaRecords\n        description: "Yes | No — whether CAA DNS records restrict which CAs can issue certificates for the domain"\n      - fieldname: notes\n        description: Additional certificate management notes\n  mutlpo-form:\n    fields:\n      - fieldname: mtlsEnabled\n        required: true\n        description: "Yes | No — whether mutual TLS is used anywhere in the system (client certificates for authentication)"\n      - fieldname: mtlsScope\n        description: "AllServices | InternalOnly | HighValueAPIs | SpecificEndpoints — which communication paths require mTLS"\n      - fieldname: clientCertificateIssuance\n        description: "InternalCA | ExternalCA | SelfSigned | Automated — how client certificates are issued and distributed"\n      - fieldname: revocationChecking\n        description: "CRL | OCSP | OCSPStapling | None — how certificate revocation status is verified"\n      - fieldname: fallbackOnMtlsFailure\n        description: "Reject | FallbackToTLS | DegradeWithWarning — behavior when mTLS handshake fails (Reject recommended for high-security channels)"\n      - fieldname: clientCertificateRotation\n        description: "Automated | Manual | OnExpiry — how client certificates are rotated"\n      - fieldname: notes\n        description: Additional mutual TLS policy notes\n  trsepo-form:\n    fields:\n      - fieldname: hstsEnabled\n        required: true\n        description: "Yes | No — whether HTTP Strict Transport Security header is sent to force browsers to use HTTPS"\n      - fieldname: hstsMaxAgeDays\n        description: HSTS max-age value in days (e.g. 365 = 1 year; 730 = 2 years; must be sufficiently long to prevent downgrade)\n      - fieldname: hstsIncludeSubdomains\n        description: "Yes | No — whether HSTS applies to all subdomains (recommended: Yes when all subdomains support HTTPS)"\n      - fieldname: hstsPreload\n        description: "Yes | No — whether the domain is submitted to the HSTS preload list (hardcoded into browsers; requires includeSubDomains and long max-age)"\n      - fieldname: httpToHttpsRedirect\n        description: "Yes | No — whether HTTP requests are permanently redirected (301) to HTTPS"\n      - fieldname: secureCookieFlag\n        description: "Yes | No — whether all cookies are marked with Secure flag (browsers only send them over HTTPS)"\n      - fieldname: preventMixedContent\n        description: "Yes | No — whether loading of non-TLS resources from TLS pages is blocked"\n      - fieldname: sensitiveDataCaching\n        description: "NoCache | NoStore | Private | Default — cache-control headers for responses containing sensitive data (NoStore recommended per OWASP)"\n      - fieldname: notes\n        description: Additional transport security policy notes\n  reid-form:\n    fields:\n      - fieldname: description\n        description: Business purpose and summary of the report\n      - fieldname: reportCategory\n        description: Operational / Analytical / Compliance / Financial / Audit\n      - fieldname: relatedUseCases\n        description: ISC references this report serves\n      - fieldname: relatedBusinessProcesses\n        description: TOM references where this report is used\n      - fieldname: relatedDataEntities\n        description: IFM entity references used as data sources\n  redaso-form:\n    fields:\n      - fieldname: dataSource\n        description: Primary data source or query reference\n      - fieldname: dataScope\n        description: "What data is included, e.g. All orders for current fiscal year"\n      - fieldname: dataCurrency\n        description: Real-time / Near-real-time / Daily-snapshot / As-of-date\n      - fieldname: generationTrigger\n        description: On-demand / Scheduled / Event-triggered / Batch\n  refo-form:\n    fields:\n      - fieldname: format\n        description: PDF / Excel / CSV / HTML / Word / Print / Multi-format\n      - fieldname: interactivity\n        description: Static / Interactive / Drill-down / Parameterized\n      - fieldname: pageSize\n        description: "Override: A4 / Letter / Legal / A3 / Custom"\n      - fieldname: orientation\n        description: "Override: Portrait / Landscape / Auto"\n  rela-form:\n    fields:\n      - fieldname: marginTop\n        description: Override top margin\n      - fieldname: marginBottom\n        description: Override bottom margin\n      - fieldname: marginLeft\n        description: Override left margin\n      - fieldname: marginRight\n        description: Override right margin\n  rehefo-form:\n    fields:\n      - fieldname: headerTemplate\n        description: "Page header override, e.g. {logo} {reportTitle}"\n      - fieldname: footerTemplate\n        description: Page footer override\n      - fieldname: coverPage\n        description: Yes / No — include a cover page\n      - fieldname: coverPageTemplate\n        description: Cover page content template\n      - fieldname: tableOfContents\n        description: Yes / No — include TOC for multi-section reports\n  regr-form:\n    fields:\n      - fieldname: defaultSortField\n        description: Default sort column or field\n      - fieldname: defaultSortDirection\n        description: Ascending / Descending\n      - fieldname: defaultGroupBy\n        description: Default grouping field\n      - fieldname: groupSummary\n        description: Yes / No — show subtotals per group\n      - fieldname: grandTotal\n        description: Yes / No — show grand total row\n  rf-form:\n    fields:\n      - fieldname: conditionalFormatting\n        description: Description of conditional formatting rules\n      - fieldname: highlightRules\n        description: "Row/cell highlight rules, e.g. overdue items in red"\n  rein-form:\n    fields:\n      - fieldname: drillDownTarget\n        description: Report or screen navigated to on row click\n      - fieldname: drillThroughReports\n        description: "Reports reachable from this report — report section ids (REPENT-REPO-…), comma-separated"\n      - fieldname: parameterForm\n        description: Description of user input form shown before generation\n      - fieldname: emptyDataMessage\n        description: Message to display when report has no data\n  repa-form:\n    fields:\n      - fieldname: maxRows\n        description: Row limit for performance; 0 = unlimited\n      - fieldname: paginationStyle\n        description: Page-break / Continuous / Scrollable\n      - fieldname: rowsPerPage\n        description: For paginated tabular reports\n  rese-form:\n    fields:\n      - fieldname: localization\n        description: "Locales supported, e.g. de-DE, en-US, fr-FR"\n      - fieldname: brandingOverride\n        description: Override branding for this report\n      - fieldname: dataLevelSecurity\n        description: Row/column level security rules narrowing what the report shows a caller who is already permitted to generate it\n  azreq-role-form:\n    fields:\n      - fieldname: roles\n        required: true\n        description: Comma-separated role names from the role catalogue; the caller must hold at least one\n  azreq-grup-form:\n    fields:\n      - fieldname: groups\n        required: true\n        description: "Comma-separated group names the caller must belong to (at least one). Groups are runtime principal data, so these are not checked against a catalogue."\n  azreq-entl-form:\n    fields:\n      - fieldname: patterns\n        required: true\n        description: Comma-separated entitlement match patterns; the caller must match at least one\n  azreq-rkey-form:\n    fields:\n      - fieldname: resourceKey\n        required: true\n        description: The resource key from the resource-key catalogue the caller must hold a grant on\n  azreq-cust-form:\n    fields:\n      - fieldname: handler\n        required: true\n        description: The registered access handler that decides\n      - fieldname: resourceId\n        description: "The resource id passed to the handler, where it needs one"\n      - fieldname: decisionRule\n        required: true\n        description: "What the handler must decide, in business terms — this is the specification the handler is implemented against"\n  azlvl-role-form:\n    fields:\n      - fieldname: roles\n        required: true\n        description: Comma-separated role names from the role catalogue; the caller must hold at least one\n  azlvl-grup-form:\n    fields:\n      - fieldname: groups\n        required: true\n        description: Comma-separated group names the caller must belong to (at least one)\n  azlvl-entl-form:\n    fields:\n      - fieldname: patterns\n        required: true\n        description: Comma-separated entitlement match patterns; the caller must match at least one\n  azlvl-rkey-form:\n    fields:\n      - fieldname: resourceKey\n        required: true\n        description: The resource key from the resource-key catalogue the caller must hold a grant on\n  azlvl-cust-form:\n    fields:\n      - fieldname: handler\n        required: true\n        description: The registered access handler that decides\n      - fieldname: resourceId\n        description: "The resource id passed to the handler, where it needs one"\n      - fieldname: decisionRule\n        required: true\n        description: "What the handler must decide, in business terms"\n  reli-form:\n    fields:\n      - fieldname: archiveRetention\n        description: "Retention policy for generated instances, e.g. 90 days"\n      - fieldname: signatureRequired\n        description: Yes / No — does the report require a digital signature\n      - fieldname: approvalWorkflow\n        description: "Approval steps before distribution, if any"\n      - fieldname: notes\n        description: Additional design notes or open questions\n  reseda-form:\n    fields:\n      - fieldname: purpose\n        description: What this section communicates\n      - fieldname: dataSource\n        description: Data source or query for this section\n      - fieldname: dataScope\n        description: Scope filter applied to the section data\n      - fieldname: textContent\n        description: Static text or template for text-type sections\n      - fieldname: notes\n        description: Design notes\n  resela-form:\n    fields:\n      - fieldname: displayOrder\n        description: Position within the report\n      - fieldname: pageBreakBefore\n        description: Yes / No — force page break before this section\n      - fieldname: pageBreakAfter\n        description: Yes / No — force page break after this section\n      - fieldname: repeatOnNewPage\n        description: Yes / No — repeat section header on each new page\n      - fieldname: orientation\n        description: "Override: Portrait / Landscape"\n      - fieldname: conditionalVisibility\n        description: Condition when section is shown\n      - fieldname: backgroundColor\n        description: Background color or shading\n      - fieldname: borderStyle\n        description: None / Thin / Medium / Thick / Custom\n  reseso-form:\n    fields:\n      - fieldname: sortField\n        description: Default sort for this section data\n      - fieldname: sortDirection\n        description: Ascending / Descending\n      - fieldname: groupByField\n        description: Field used for grouping rows\n      - fieldname: showGroupSubtotals\n        description: Yes / No\n  reseag-form:\n    fields:\n      - fieldname: showSectionTotal\n        description: Yes / No — show totals row at section end\n      - fieldname: aggregationFields\n        description: Comma-separated fields with