:\n    prefix: WOTREN_TRIG_LST\n    subsection-types:\n      wotren-trig:\n        max-count: infinite\n    min-text-length: 0\n    max-text-length: 0\n    description: "Add one entry per trigger, with its type (event, schedule, manual, system), source, condition, and frequency."\n  carch-inte-lst:\n    prefix: CARCH_INTE_LST\n    subsection-types:\n      carch-inte:\n        max-count: infinite\n    min-text-length: 0\n    max-text-length: 0\n    description: "Add one entry per integration pattern in use (e.g. point-to-point, hub-and-spoke, pub/sub, ESB, API gateway). Note where each pattern is applied and why."\n  carch-shar-lst:\n    prefix: CARCH_SHAR_LST\n    subsection-types:\n      carch-shar:\n        max-count: infinite\n    min-text-length: 0\n    max-text-length: 0\n    description: "Add one entry per shared service used by more than one system (e.g. authentication, logging, notifications). Capture which systems consume it."\n  esent-syst-lst:\n    prefix: ESENT_SYST_LST\n    subsection-types:\n      esent-syst:\n        max-count: infinite\n        min-count: 1\n    min-text-length: 0\n    max-text-length: 0\n    description: "Add one entry per existing system that is relevant to the project scope. Include all systems that will be replaced, integrated with, or affected by the new system."\n  exsde-item-lst:\n    prefix: EXSDE_ITEM_LST\n    subsection-types:\n      exsde-item:\n        max-count: infinite\n    min-text-length: 0\n    max-text-length: 0\n    description: "Add one entry per external service or third-party provider the current systems rely on. Capture vendor, SLA, risk, and fallback for each."\n  exsde-prim-ref:\n    prefix: EXSDE_PRIM_REF\n    subsection-types:\n      estec:\n        max-count: 1\n      esbct:\n        max-count: 1\n      esusg:\n        max-count: 1\n      eslcy:\n        max-count: 1\n      esint:\n        max-count: 1\n      esinf:\n        max-count: 1\n      limet-know-lst:\n        max-count: 1\n      esqua:\n        max-count: 1\n    description: "The in-house system that stops working when this external service does,"\n  limet-know-lst:\n    prefix: LIMET_KNOW_LST\n    subsection-types:\n      limet-know:\n        max-count: infinite\n    min-text-length: 0\n    max-text-length: 0\n    description: Document each known limitation with its impact on current operations and any workarounds in place.\n  mgmls-mile-lst:\n    prefix: MGMLS_MILE_LST\n    subsection-types:\n      mgmls-mile:\n        max-count: infinite\n    min-text-length: 0\n    max-text-length: 0\n    description: "Add one entry per program milestone, with its target date, systems included, and the success/gate criteria that must be met."\n  mgrsk-item-lst:\n    prefix: MGRSK_ITEM_LST\n    subsection-types:\n      mgrsk-item:\n        max-count: infinite\n    min-text-length: 0\n    max-text-length: 0\n    description: "Add one entry per identified migration risk, each capturing its full lifecycle from identification through resolution."\n  msddo-mast-lst:\n    prefix: MSDDO_MAST_LST\n    subsection-types:\n      msddo-mast:\n        max-count: infinite\n        min-count: 1\n    min-text-length: 0\n    max-text-length: 0\n    description: "Add one entry per master data domain (e.g. Customer, Product, Vendor). Capture its golden-record source, quality and volume, consuming systems and cadence, and ownership and improvement plans."\n  ppgce-corr-lst:\n    prefix: PPGCE_CORR_LST\n    subsection-types:\n      ppgce-corr:\n        max-count: infinite\n        min-count: 1\n    min-text-length: 0\n    max-text-length: 0\n    description: "Add one entry per pain-point-to-gap relationship, naming both IDs and describing how they are linked (cause, contribution, or indication) and how strong the link is."\n  repol-rete-lst:\n    prefix: REPOL_RETE_LST\n    subsection-types:\n      repol-rete:\n        max-count: infinite\n        min-count: 1\n    min-text-length: 0\n    max-text-length: 0\n    description: "Add one entry per data category with a retention policy. Capture its retention period and trigger, legal basis, archival and deletion methods, and compliance/implementation status."\n  shien-item-lst:\n    prefix: SHIEN_ITEM_LST\n    subsection-types:\n      shien-item:\n        max-count: infinite\n    min-text-length: 0\n    max-text-length: 0\n    description: "Add one entry per shared infrastructure component (e.g. a database cluster, message broker, identity provider). Capture its criticality, resilience, and the systems that depend on it."\n  cpie-impr-lst:\n    prefix: CPIE_IMPR_LST\n    subsection-types:\n      cpie-impr:\n        max-count: infinite\n    min-text-length: 0\n    max-text-length: 0\n    description: "Add one entry per improvement opportunity, contrasting the current and desired state with its benefit, effort, and priority."\n  cuwf-work-lst:\n    prefix: CUWF_WORK_LST\n    subsection-types:\n      cuwf-work:\n        max-count: infinite\n        min-count: 1\n    min-text-length: 0\n    max-text-length: 0\n    description: "Add one entry per workflow within this process, documenting its triggers, steps, actors, inputs, outputs, and timing."\n  dadu-dupl-lst:\n    prefix: DADU_DUPL_LST\n    subsection-types:\n      dadu-dupl:\n        max-count: infinite\n    min-text-length: 0\n    max-text-length: 0\n    description: "Add one entry per documented duplication case. Capture the data element, its primary and duplicate sources, how copies are synchronized, the business reason, and the recommended action."\n  dain-inte-lst:\n    prefix: DAIN_INTE_LST\n    subsection-types:\n      dain-inte:\n        max-count: infinite\n        min-count: 1\n    min-text-length: 0\n    max-text-length: 0\n    description: "Add one entry per data integration point. Capture its source and target systems, integration type, volume and transport, reliability and monitoring, and its owners."\n  dasr-data-lst:\n    prefix: DASR_DATA_LST\n    subsection-types:\n      dasr-data:\n        max-count: infinite\n    min-text-length: 0\n    max-text-length: 0\n    description: "Add one entry per data source/store in the environment (databases, warehouses, lakes, file systems, SaaS, APIs). Capture each source\'s technology, volume, quality, ownership, and key entities."\n  dcle-clas-lst:\n    prefix: DCLE_CLAS_LST\n    subsection-types:\n      dcle-clas:\n        max-count: infinite\n        min-count: 1\n    min-text-length: 0\n    max-text-length: 0\n    description: "Add one entry per classification level (e.g. Public, Internal, Confidential, Restricted). Capture its order, meaning, examples, and the handling, access, storage, transmission, and disposal requirements."\n  dcse-clas-lst:\n    prefix: DCSE_CLAS_LST\n    subsection-types:\n      dcse-clas:\n        max-count: infinite\n    min-text-length: 0\n    max-text-length: 0\n    description: "Add one entry per data domain. Capture its classification status, percentage classified, highest sensitivity level present, the classification owner, and when it was last reviewed."\n  dgpe-gove-lst:\n    prefix: DGPE_GOVE_LST\n    subsection-types:\n      dgpe-gove:\n        max-count: infinite\n        min-count: 1\n    min-text-length: 0\n    max-text-length: 0\n    description: "Add one entry per data governance policy (quality, security, privacy, access, MDM). Capture its area, scope, status, owner, enforcement mechanism, and current compliance level."\n  dqie-impr-lst:\n    prefix: DQIE_IMPR_LST\n    subsection-types:\n      dqie-impr:\n        max-count: infinite\n    min-text-length: 0\n    max-text-length: 0\n    description: "Add one entry per active or planned data-quality improvement initiative. Capture the issues it targets, its status, expected completion, and the improvement it should deliver."\n  dsee-keye-lst:\n    prefix: DSEE_KEYE_LST\n    subsection-types:\n      dsee-keye:\n        max-count: infinite\n        min-count: 1\n    min-text-length: 0\n    max-text-length: 0\n    description: "Add one entry per key entity in this source. Capture its name, what it represents, record count, primary key, relationships, and any sensitive fields."\n  gape-item-lst:\n    prefix: GAPE_ITEM_LST\n    subsection-types:\n      gape-item:\n        max-count: infinite\n    min-text-length: 0\n    max-text-length: 0\n    description: "Add one entry per identified gap between current capabilities and business needs, each with its category, severity, cost, drivers, and proposed resolution."\n  miri-moni-lst:\n    prefix: MIRI_MONI_LST\n    subsection-types:\n      miri-moni:\n        max-count: infinite\n    min-text-length: 0\n    max-text-length: 0\n    description: "Add one entry per monitoring procedure, describing what is tracked, how often, and the control action taken."\n  miri-rbde-lst:\n    prefix: MIRI_RBDE_LST\n    subsection-types:\n      miri-rbde:\n        max-count: infinite\n    min-text-length: 0\n    max-text-length: 0\n    description: "Add one entry per risk-based decision rule, describing the threshold or criterion and the decision it triggers."\n  miri-resp-lst:\n    prefix: MIRI_RESP_LST\n    subsection-types:\n      miri-resp:\n        max-count: infinite\n    min-text-length: 0\n    max-text-length: 0\n    description: "Add one entry per response strategy, mapping a risk category to its chosen response approach and rationale."\n  miri-risk-lst:\n    prefix: MIRI_RISK_LST\n    subsection-types:\n      miri-risk:\n        max-count: infinite\n    min-text-length: 0\n    max-text-length: 0\n    description: "Add one entry per risk category, naming the category and the kinds of migration risks it groups."\n  pape-item-lst:\n    prefix: PAPE_ITEM_LST\n    subsection-types:\n      pape-item:\n        max-count: infinite\n    min-text-length: 0\n    max-text-length: 0\n    description: "Add one entry per distinct technical problem, each with its own root cause, impact, and resolution outlook. Scope entries to technology, architecture, security, and maintainability concerns."\n  syde-item-lst:\n    prefix: SYDE_ITEM_LST\n    subsection-types:\n      syde-item:\n        max-count: infinite\n    min-text-length: 0\n    max-text-length: 0\n    description: "Add one entry per dependency between internal systems. Capture the mechanism, coupling strength, data flow, and failure impact of each."\n  syde-sour-ref:\n    prefix: SYDE_SOUR_REF\n    subsection-types:\n      estec:\n        max-count: 1\n      esbct:\n        max-count: 1\n      esusg:\n        max-count: 1\n      eslcy:\n        max-count: 1\n      esint:\n        max-count: 1\n      esinf:\n        max-count: 1\n      limet-know-lst:\n        max-count: 1\n      esqua:\n        max-count: 1\n    description: The depending end — the system that stops working if the dependency\n  syde-targ-ref:\n    prefix: SYDE_TARG_REF\n    subsection-types:\n      estec:\n        max-count: 1\n      esbct:\n        max-count: 1\n      esusg:\n        max-count: 1\n      eslcy:\n        max-count: 1\n      esint:\n        max-count: 1\n      esinf:\n        max-count: 1\n      limet-know-lst:\n        max-count: 1\n      esqua:\n        max-count: 1\n    description: The depended-upon end — the system that owes the availability and the SLA\n  syin-item-lst:\n    prefix: SYIN_ITEM_LST\n    subsection-types:\n      syin-item:\n        max-count: infinite\n    min-text-length: 0\n    max-text-length: 0\n    description: "Add one entry per active integration between systems. Capture its type, pattern, protocol, data format, throughput, and monitoring."\n  syin-sour-ref:\n    prefix: SYIN_SOUR_REF\n    subsection-types:\n      estec:\n        max-count: 1\n      esbct:\n        max-count: 1\n      esusg:\n        max-count: 1\n      eslcy:\n        max-count: 1\n      esint:\n        max-count: 1\n      esinf:\n        max-count: 1\n      limet-know-lst:\n        max-count: 1\n      esqua:\n        max-count: 1\n    description: "The system data flows out of, named by section id."\n  syin-targ-ref:\n    prefix: SYIN_TARG_REF\n    subsection-types:\n      estec:\n        max-count: 1\n      esbct:\n        max-count: 1\n      esusg:\n        max-count: 1\n      eslcy:\n        max-count: 1\n      esint:\n        max-count: 1\n      esinf:\n        max-count: 1\n      limet-know-lst:\n        max-count: 1\n      esqua:\n        max-count: 1\n    description: "The system data flows into, named by section id."\n  cubipr-proc:\n    prefix: CUBIPR_PROC_\n    subsection-types:\n      pc:\n        max-count: 1\n      wode:\n        max-count: 1\n      pm:\n        max-count: 1\n      prpapo:\n        max-count: 1\n    pattern-check-id:\n      pattern: ^CUBIPR-PROC-.+\$\n      error-message: IDs of this section must match CUBIPR-PROC-xxx\n    description: "Document each business process that the project will impact. Include process maps (BPMN recommended), actor descriptions, and quantitative metrics. Identify manual steps and error-prone areas."\n  cudala-datal:\n    prefix: CUDALA_DATAL\n    format: mermaid-flowchart\n    description: Visual representation of the data landscape.\n  cuopme-oper:\n    prefix: CUOPME_OPER_\n    pattern-check-id:\n      pattern: ^CUOPME-OPER-.+\$\n      error-message: IDs of this section must match CUOPME-OPER-xxx\n    description: 1.5. Operational Metrics.\n  daenmi-enti:\n    prefix: DAENMI_ENTI_\n    pattern-check-id:\n      pattern: ^DAENMI-ENTI-.+\$\n      error-message: IDs of this section must match DAENMI-ENTI-xxx\n    description: "Add one entry per data entity to migrate; capture record count, target mapping, and transformation rules."\n  daowen-owne:\n    prefix: DAOWEN_OWNE_\n    subsection-types:\n      daowenst:\n        max-count: 1\n      doeg:\n        max-count: 1\n    pattern-check-id:\n      pattern: ^DAOWEN-OWNE-.+\$\n      error-message: IDs of this section must match DAOWEN-OWNE-xxx\n    description: "Add one entry per data domain or asset. Capture its business owner, data steward and technical custodian, who approves access, and the current ownership coverage status."\n  daqlis-qual:\n    prefix: DAQLIS_QUAL_\n    subsection-types:\n      dqiec:\n        max-count: 1\n      dqiei:\n        max-count: 1\n      dqier:\n        max-count: 1\n    pattern-check-id:\n      pattern: ^DAQLIS-QUAL-.+\$\n      error-message: IDs of this section must match DAQLIS-QUAL-xxx\n    description: "Add one entry per known data quality issue. Capture its severity, affected sources/entities, business impact, root cause, and proposed resolution."\n  davoen-volu:\n    prefix: DAVOEN_VOLU_\n    pattern-check-id:\n      pattern: ^DAVOEN-VOLU-.+\$\n      error-message: IDs of this section must match DAVOEN-VOLU-xxx\n    description: "Add one entry per data source. Capture its current volume, record count, average record size, historical and projected growth, growth drivers, and archival/purge rates."\n  inhesu-frag:\n    prefix: INHESU_FRAG_\n    pattern-check-id:\n      pattern: ^INHESU-FRAG-.+\$\n      error-message: IDs of this section must match INHESU-FRAG-xxx\n    description: "Add one entry per fragile or high-risk integration point — brittle interfaces, undocumented links, or single points of failure that threaten operations or the new system implementation."\n  mebaen-entr:\n    prefix: MEBAEN_ENTR_\n    pattern-check-id:\n      pattern: ^MEBAEN-ENTR-.+\$\n      error-message: IDs of this section must match MEBAEN-ENTR-xxx\n    description: "Add one entry per metric to be tracked, with its baseline value, target value, and improvement target."\n  migcon-esca:\n    prefix: MIGCON_ESCA_\n    pattern-check-id:\n      pattern: ^MIGCON-ESCA-.+\$\n      error-message: IDs of this section must match MIGCON-ESCA-xxx\n    description: "Add one entry per escalation procedure, describing the trigger condition, the escalation path, and the responsible decision authority."\n  miriin-indi:\n    prefix: MIRIIN_INDI_\n    pattern-check-id:\n      pattern: ^MIRIIN-INDI-.+\$\n      error-message: IDs of this section must match MIRIIN-INDI-xxx\n    description: "Add one entry per indicator set, describing the metrics, thresholds, and monitoring frequency that signal the risk."\n  papor1-rela:\n    prefix: PAPOR1_RELA_\n    pattern-check-id:\n      pattern: ^PAPOR1-RELA-.+\$\n      error-message: IDs of this section must match PAPOR1-RELA-xxx\n    description: "Add one entry per relationship this pain point has — related pain points, originating gaps, or other pain points it depends on."\n  pme-item-lst:\n    prefix: PME_ITEM_LST\n    subsection-types:\n      pme-item:\n        max-count: infinite\n    min-text-length: 0\n    max-text-length: 0\n    description: Add any individual metrics that do not fit a specific category above.\n  pme-keym-lst:\n    prefix: PME_KEYM_LST\n    subsection-types:\n      pme-keym:\n        max-count: infinite\n    min-text-length: 0\n    max-text-length: 0\n    description: Add the most important metrics that characterize overall process performance at a glance.\n  pme-metr-lst:\n    prefix: PME_METR_LST\n    subsection-types:\n      pme-metr:\n        max-count: infinite\n    min-text-length: 0\n    max-text-length: 0\n    description: "Add one entry per metric in this category, with its current value, unit, and measurement details."\n  pme-proc-ref:\n    prefix: PME_PROC_REF\n    subsection-types:\n      pc:\n        max-count: 1\n      wode:\n        max-count: 1\n      pm:\n        max-count: 1\n      prpapo:\n        max-count: 1\n    description: "Document each business process that the project will impact. Include process maps (BPMN recommended), actor descriptions, and quantitative metrics. Identify manual steps and error-prone areas."\n  prdeen-depe:\n    prefix: PRDEEN_DEPE_\n    pattern-check-id:\n      pattern: ^PRDEEN-DEPE-.+\$\n      error-message: IDs of this section must match PRDEEN-DEPE-xxx\n    description: "Add one entry per source→target process dependency, capturing the artifact exchanged, coupling, timing, and failure impact."\n  prmeca-cost:\n    prefix: PRMECA_COST_\n    subsection-types:\n      pme-metr-lst:\n        max-count: 1\n    pattern-check-id:\n      pattern: ^PRMECA-COST-.+\$\n      error-message: IDs of this section must match PRMECA-COST-xxx\n    description: Group related metrics under this category and add one entry per metric it contains.\n  prmeca-effi:\n    prefix: PRMECA_EFFI_\n    subsection-types:\n      pme-metr-lst:\n        max-count: 1\n    pattern-check-id:\n      pattern: ^PRMECA-EFFI-.+\$\n      error-message: IDs of this section must match PRMECA-EFFI-xxx\n    description: Group related metrics under this category and add one entry per metric it contains.\n  prmeca-manu:\n    prefix: PRMECA_MANU_\n    subsection-types:\n      pme-metr-lst:\n        max-count: 1\n    pattern-check-id:\n      pattern: ^PRMECA-MANU-.+\$\n      error-message: IDs of this section must match PRMECA-MANU-xxx\n    description: Group related metrics under this category and add one entry per metric it contains.\n  prmeca-qual:\n    prefix: PRMECA_QUAL_\n    subsection-types:\n      pme-metr-lst:\n        max-count: 1\n    pattern-check-id:\n      pattern: ^PRMECA-QUAL-.+\$\n      error-message: IDs of this section must match PRMECA-QUAL-xxx\n    description: Group related metrics under this category and add one entry per metric it contains.\n  prmeca-volu:\n    prefix: PRMECA_VOLU_\n    subsection-types:\n      pme-metr-lst:\n        max-count: 1\n    pattern-check-id:\n      pattern: ^PRMECA-VOLU-.+\$\n      error-message: IDs of this section must match PRMECA-VOLU-xxx\n    description: Group related metrics under this category and add one entry per metric it contains.\n  prscen-insc:\n    prefix: PRSCEN_INSC_\n    pattern-check-id:\n      pattern: ^PRSCEN-INSC-.+\$\n      error-message: IDs of this section must match PRSCEN-INSC-xxx\n    description: "Add one entry per process that is in scope for analysis, with the rationale for its inclusion."\n  prscen-outo:\n    prefix: PRSCEN_OUTO_\n    pattern-check-id:\n      pattern: ^PRSCEN-OUTO-.+\$\n      error-message: IDs of this section must match PRSCEN-OUTO-xxx\n    description: "Add one entry per process excluded from analysis, noting why and the impact of leaving it out."\n  repphs-phas:\n    prefix: REPPHS_PHAS_\n    pattern-check-id:\n      pattern: ^REPPHS-PHAS-.+\$\n      error-message: IDs of this section must match REPPHS-PHAS-xxx\n    description: "Add one entry per replacement phase; capture scope, dates, and exit criteria for each."\n  resyde-depe:\n    prefix: RESYDE_DEPE_\n    pattern-check-id:\n      pattern: ^RESYDE-DEPE-.+\$\n      error-message: IDs of this section must match RESYDE-DEPE-xxx\n    description: "Add one entry per integration or dependency; capture direction, criticality, and how the link will be rebuilt or eliminated."\n  sybupr-supp:\n    prefix: SYBUPR_SUPP_\n    pattern-check-id:\n      pattern: ^SYBUPR-SUPP-.+\$\n      error-message: IDs of this section must match SYBUPR-SUPP-xxx\n    description: Add one entry per business process the system supports; note its role and execution frequency.\n  sybuun-busi:\n    prefix: SYBUUN_BUSI_\n    pattern-check-id:\n      pattern: ^SYBUUN-BUSI-.+\$\n      error-message: IDs of this section must match SYBUUN-BUSI-xxx\n    description: Add one entry per business unit using the system; note user count and dependency level.\n  sycoan-nonf:\n    prefix: SYCOAN_NONF_\n    pattern-check-id:\n      pattern: ^SYCOAN-NONF-.+\$\n      error-message: IDs of this section must match SYCOAN-NONF-xxx\n    description: "Add one entry per non-financial benefit (e.g. risk reduction, agility) to weigh in the ROI case."\n  sydasc-know:\n    prefix: SYDASC_KNOW_\n    pattern-check-id:\n      pattern: ^SYDASC-KNOW-.+\$\n      error-message: IDs of this section must match SYDASC-KNOW-xxx\n    description: Add one entry per data-quality issue to address; note severity and remediation approach.\n  sykntr-crit:\n    prefix: SYKNTR_CRIT_\n    pattern-check-id:\n      pattern: ^SYKNTR-CRIT-.+\$\n      error-message: IDs of this section must match SYKNTR-CRIT-xxx\n    description: Add one entry per critical knowledge area at risk of being lost when the system is retired.\n  symiri-risk:\n    prefix: SYMIRI_RISK_\n    pattern-check-id:\n      pattern: ^SYMIRI-RISK-.+\$\n      error-message: IDs of this section must match SYMIRI-RISK-xxx\n    description: "Add one entry per migration risk; capture probability, impact, mitigation, and contingency."\n  syrest-pred:\n    prefix: SYREST_PRED_\n    pattern-check-id:\n      pattern: ^SYREST-PRED-.+\$\n      error-message: IDs of this section must match SYREST-PRED-xxx\n    description: Add one entry per predecessor system that must be replaced or addressed before this system can proceed.\n  syteas-know:\n    prefix: SYTEAS_KNOW_\n    pattern-check-id:\n      pattern: ^SYTEAS-KNOW-.+\$\n      error-message: IDs of this section must match SYTEAS-KNOW-xxx\n    description: "Add one entry per significant known technical issue, defect, or deficiency affecting the system."\n  syteas-secu:\n    prefix: SYTEAS_SECU_\n    pattern-check-id:\n      pattern: ^SYTEAS-SECU-.+\$\n      error-message: IDs of this section must match SYTEAS-SECU-xxx\n    description: Add one entry per security vulnerability or compliance gap; note severity and remediation status.\n  sytore-syst:\n    prefix: SYTORE_SYST_\n    subsection-types:\n      sytore-iden:\n        max-count: 1\n      strep:\n        max-count: 1\n      strev:\n        max-count: 1\n      syteas:\n        max-count: 1\n      sybucr:\n        max-count: 1\n      syrest:\n        max-count: 1\n      sydasc:\n        max-count: 1\n      resyde-depe-lst:\n        max-count: 1\n      syusim:\n        max-count: 1\n      sycoan:\n        max-count: 1\n      symipl:\n        max-count: 1\n      sykntr:\n        max-count: 1\n    pattern-check-id:\n      pattern: ^SYTORE-SYST-.+\$\n      error-message: IDs of this section must match SYTORE-SYST-xxx\n    description: "Add one entry per legacy system targeted for replacement; each entry captures its full technical, business, and migration assessment."\n  usgrim-user:\n    prefix: USGRIM_USER_\n    pattern-check-id:\n      pattern: ^USGRIM-USER-.+\$\n      error-message: IDs of this section must match USGRIM-USER-xxx\n    description: Add one entry per user group needing special handling; note impact level and special considerations.\n  wae-acto-lst:\n    prefix: WAE_ACTO_LST\n    subsection-types:\n      wae-acto:\n        max-count: infinite\n    min-text-length: 0\n    max-text-length: 0\n    description: "Add one entry per actor (role, system, department, external) taking part in this workflow, with their responsibilities and authorization level."\n  wae-part-ref:\n    prefix: WAE_PART_REF\n    subsection-types:\n      wse:\n        max-count: infinite\n    min-text-length: 0\n    max-text-length: 0\n    description: Steps this actor participates in.\n  woburu-busi:\n    prefix: WOBURU_BUSI_\n    pattern-check-id:\n      pattern: ^WOBURU-BUSI-.+\$\n      error-message: IDs of this section must match WOBURU-BUSI-xxx\n    description: "Add one entry per business rule constraining this workflow, with its logic, source, and exceptions."\n  wodepo-deci:\n    prefix: WODEPO_DECI_\n    pattern-check-id:\n      pattern: ^WODEPO-DECI-.+\$\n      error-message: IDs of this section must match WODEPO-DECI-xxx\n    description: "Add one entry per decision point, with its criteria, decision maker, possible outcomes, and escalation path."\n  woexen-exce:\n    prefix: WOEXEN_EXCE_\n    pattern-check-id:\n      pattern: ^WOEXEN-EXCE-.+\$\n      error-message: IDs of this section must match WOEXEN-EXCE-xxx\n    description: "Add one entry per exception type, with its frequency, handling procedure, escalation path, and recovery time."\n  woinen-inpu:\n    prefix: WOINEN_INPU_\n    pattern-check-id:\n      pattern: ^WOINEN-INPU-.+\$\n