s are listed here once: mark a step that needs human judgment or that fails often with the corresponding flag rather than repeating it in a second list."\n  carch-inte:\n    prefix: CARCH_INTE_\n    pattern-check-id:\n      pattern: ^CARCH-INTE-.+\$\n      error-message: IDs of this section must match CARCH-INTE-xxx\n    description: "Add one entry per integration pattern in use (e.g. point-to-point, hub-and-spoke, pub/sub, ESB, API gateway). Note where each pattern is applied and why."\n  carch-shar:\n    prefix: CARCH_SHAR_\n    pattern-check-id:\n      pattern: ^CARCH-SHAR-.+\$\n      error-message: IDs of this section must match CARCH-SHAR-xxx\n    description: "Add one entry per shared service used by more than one system (e.g. authentication, logging, notifications). Capture which systems consume it."\n  cubupr-proc:\n    prefix: CUBUPR_PROC\n    format: mermaid-flowchart\n    description: "Create a Mermaid flowchart showing the process landscape. Group processes by category (Core, Support, Management). Show handoffs and data flows between processes."\n  cudala-data:\n    prefix: CUDALA_DATA\n    format: mermaid\n    description: Data architecture summary diagram.\n  daduan-dupl:\n    prefix: DADUAN_DUPL\n    format: mermaid\n    description: Visual representation of data redundancy.\n  dainpo-data:\n    prefix: DAINPO_DATA\n    format: mermaid-flowchart\n    description: Data flow diagram.\n  daquas-qual:\n    prefix: DAQUAS_QUAL\n    format: mermaid\n    description: Quality issues by severity.\n  dasoin-data:\n    prefix: DASOIN_DATA\n    format: mermaid\n    description: Visual map of data sources by domain/category.\n  esent-syst:\n    prefix: ESENT_SYST_\n    subsection-types:\n      estec:\n        max-count: 1\n      esbct:\n        max-count: 1\n      esusg:\n        max-count: 1\n      eslcy:\n        max-count: 1\n      esint:\n        max-count: 1\n      esinf:\n        max-count: 1\n      limet-know-lst:\n        max-count: 1\n      esqua:\n      