f` case."\n  biru-busi:\n    prefix: BIRU_BUSI_\n    subsection-types:\n      biru-iden:\n        max-count: 1\n      biru-clas:\n        max-count: 1\n      biru-rule:\n        max-count: 1\n      biru-impl:\n        max-count: 1\n      biru-exce:\n        max-count: 1\n      biru-gove:\n        max-count: 1\n      afob-affe-lst:\n        max-count: 1\n      affn-affe-lst:\n        max-count: 1\n      rulexm-exam-lst:\n        max-count: 1\n    pattern-check-id:\n      pattern: ^BIRU-BUSI-.+\$\n      error-message: IDs of this section must match BIRU-BUSI-xxx\n    description: A business rule entry (form).\n  bjoen-doma:\n    prefix: BJOEN_DOMA\n    format: bjoen-doma-form\n    description: "Which part of the business this object belongs to, and who speaks for it."\n  bjoen-iden:\n    prefix: BJOEN_IDEN\n    format: bjoen-iden-form\n    description: "What this business object is called in the business, and which pattern it"\n  bjoen-life:\n    prefix: BJOEN_LIFE\n    format: bjoen-life-form\n    description: "The object\'s states at a glance — the digest, not the authority."\n  bjoen-owne:\n    prefix: BJOEN_OWNE\n    format: bjoen-owne-form\n    description: "Who is accountable for the object\'s data, and how concurrent change is"\n  daatt-data:\n    prefix: DAATT_DATA\n    format: daatt-data-form\n    description: "The logical type of the attribute, and the physical form it is realised"\n  daatt-deri:\n    prefix: DAATT_DERI\n    format: daatt-deri-form\n    description: "Whether the attribute holds an authored value at all, or one produced from"\n  daatt-dtbi:\n    prefix: DAATT_DTBI\n    format: daatt-dtbi-form\n    description: "Binary-kind type options — a promoted `@OneOf` case (csra4)."\n  daatt-dten:\n    prefix: DAATT_DTEN\n    format: daatt-dten-form\n    description: "Enumeration-kind type options — a promoted `@OneOf` case."\n  daatt-dtfr:\n    prefix: DAATT_DTFR\n    format: daatt-dtfr-form\n    description: "File-reference type options — a promoted `@OneOf` case (csra10)."\n  daatt-dtnu:\n    prefix: DAATT_DTNU\n    format: daatt-dtnu-form\n    description: "Numeric-kind type options — a promoted `@OneOf` case (csra4)."\n  daatt-dttm:\n    prefix: DAATT_DTTM\n    format: daatt-dttm-form\n    description: "Temporal-kind type options — a promoted `@OneOf` case (csra4)."\n  daatt-dttx:\n    prefix: DAATT_DTTX\n    format: daatt-dttx-form\n    description: "Text-kind type options — a promoted `@OneOf` case (csra4)."\n  daatt-iden:\n    prefix: DAATT_IDEN\n    format: daatt-iden-form\n    description: "What this attribute is called and what it means, in business terms."\n  daatt-migr:\n    prefix: DAATT_MIGR\n    format: daatt-migr-form\n    description: "Where this attribute\'s values come from — upstream system, source field"\n  daatt-secu:\n    prefix: DAATT_SECU\n    format: daatt-secu-form\n    description: "How exposed this single attribute is, independently of its entity."\n  daent-clas:\n    prefix: DAENT_CLAS\n    format: daent-clas-form\n    description: "Where this entity sits in the domain, and who answers for it."\n  daent-iden:\n    prefix: DAENT_IDEN\n    format: daent-iden-form\n    description: "What this entity is called, in each vocabulary that needs a name for it."\n  daent-life:\n    prefix: DAENT_LIFE\n    format: daent-life-form\n    description: "What becomes of this entity\'s rows over time: how long they are kept,"\n  daent-rela:\n    prefix: DAENT_RELA\n    format: daent-rela-form\n    description: "The entity\'s relationships as seen from this entity — a digest, not the"\n  datcl-over:\n    prefix: DATCL_OVER\n    format: datcl-over-form\n    description: "The framework the classification levels are drawn from, and who maintains"\n  dclse-acce:\n    prefix: DCLSE_ACCE\n    format: dclse-acce-form\n    description: "Who may reach data at this level, how they prove who they are, and what is"\n  dclse-comp:\n    prefix: DCLSE_COMP\n    format: dclse-comp-form\n    description: "The named regulations that impose this level, and the duties that come"\n  dclse-iden:\n    prefix: DCLSE_IDEN\n    format: dclse-iden-form\n    description: What this level means and what belongs in it.\n  dclse-rete:\n    prefix: DCLSE_RETE\n    format: dclse-rete-form\n    description: "How long data at this level is kept, and how it is destroyed."\n  dclse-stor:\n    prefix: DCLSE_STOR\n    format: dclse-stor-form\n    description: "Where data at this level may physically live, and how it is protected on"\n  enrle-card:\n    prefix: ENRLE_CARD\n    format: enrle-card-form\n    description: "How many instances may stand at each end, and whether either end may stand"\n  enrle-iden:\n    prefix: ENRLE_IDEN\n    format: enrle-iden-form\n    description: "What kind of relationship this is, and why it exists."\n  enrle-navi:\n    prefix: ENRLE_NAVI\n    format: enrle-navi-form\n    description: "How the relationship is traversed in code, and where the key physically"\n  enrle-refe:\n    prefix: ENRLE_REFE\n    format: enrle-refe-form\n    description: "What happens to the far end when a row is deleted or its key changes, and"\n  obop-oper:\n    prefix: OBOP_OPER_\n    subsection-types:\n      ooee:\n        max-count: 1\n      ooel:\n        max-count: 1\n      ooeg:\n        max-count: 1\n    pattern-check-id:\n      pattern: ^OBOP-OPER-.+\$\n      error-message: IDs of this section must match OBOP-OPER-xxx\n    description: Add one entry per object operation.\n  obst-keys:\n    prefix: OBST_KEYS_\n    pattern-check-id:\n      pattern: ^OBST-KEYS-.+\$\n      error-message: IDs of this section must match OBST-KEYS-xxx\n    description: Add one entry per object state.\n  scmst-base:\n    prefix: SCMST_BASE\n    format: scmst-base-form\n    description: "Baseline schema definition — a promoted `@OneOf` case."\n  scmst-chng:\n    prefix: SCMST_CHNG\n    format: scmst-chng-form\n    description: "Schema change — a promoted `@OneOf` case."\n  scmst-refd:\n    prefix: SCMST_REFD\n    format: scmst-refd-form\n    description: "Reference-data definition — a promoted `@OneOf` case."\n  sufn-subf:\n    prefix: SUFN_SUBF_\n    pattern-check-id:\n      pattern: ^SUFN-SUBF-.+\$\n      error-message: IDs of this section must match SUFN-SUBF-xxx\n    description: Add one entry per sub-function.\n  biru-clas:\n    prefix: BIRU_CLAS\n    format: biru-clas-form\n    description: "What kind of rule this is, how binding it is, and where it came from."\n  biru-exce:\n    prefix: BIRU_EXCE\n    format: biru-exce-form\n    description: "What happens when the rule is violated, and whether it may be waived."\n  biru-gove:\n    prefix: BIRU_GOVE\n    format: biru-gove-form\n    description: "Who owns the rule, and for how long it holds."\n  biru-iden:\n    prefix: BIRU_IDEN\n    format: biru-iden-form\n    description: "The rule\'s own statement, in the words of the business, and its version."\n  biru-impl:\n    prefix: BIRU_IMPL\n    format: biru-impl-form\n    description: "Where and how the rule is actually enforced, and whether that can be"\n  biru-rule:\n    prefix: BIRU_RULE\n    format: biru-rule-form\n    description: "The rule as a condition and its consequences — IF, THEN, and otherwise."\n  fuencl:\n    prefix: FUENCL\n    format: fuencl-form\n    description: Decomposition position and classification.\n  fuenim:\n    prefix: FUENIM\n    format: fuenim-form\n    description: Automation and data handling summary.\n  fuenop:\n    prefix: FUENOP\n    format: fuenop-form\n    description: Execution profile and criticality.\n  azgrd:\n    prefix: AZGRD\n    subsection-types:\n      azlvl-leve-lst:\n        max-count: 1\n        min-count: 1\n    description: "Graded requirement payload — a promoted `@OneOf` case."\n  azreq:\n    prefix: AZREQ\n    subsection-types:\n      azreq-role:\n        max-count: 1\n      azreq-grup:\n        max-count: 1\n      azreq-entl:\n        max-count: 1\n      azreq-rkey:\n        max-count: 1\n      azreq-cust:\n        max-count: 1\n      azgrd:\n        max-count: 1\n    description: 7.9.x. Authorization — what a caller must satisfy to invoke this\n  boaed:\n    prefix: BOAED\n    format: boaed-form\n    description: Format and requirement details.\n  boaeg:\n    prefix: BOAEG\n    format: boaeg-form\n    description: Sensitivity and presentation guidance.\n  boaev:\n    prefix: BOAEV\n    format: boaev-form\n    description: Validation and derivation rules.\n  datcl:\n    prefix: DATCL\n    subsection-types:\n      datcl-over:\n        max-count: 1\n      dclse-item-lst:\n        max-count: 1\n    description: Data classification.\n  dochd:\n    prefix: DOCHD\n    description: Standard TomSpecs document header.\n  domen:\n    prefix: DOMEN\n    subsection-types:\n      dmene-enum-lst:\n        max-count: 1\n    description: Domain enum registry — the closed value sets the data model relies on\n  enrel:\n    prefix: ENREL\n    subsection-types:\n      enrle-item-lst:\n        max-count: 1\n    description: Entity relationships.\n  ercrg:\n    prefix: ERCRG\n    subsection-types:\n      ercen-code-lst:\n        max-count: 1\n    description: Error code registry — the shared application error-code vocabulary\n  keagn:\n    prefix: KEAGN\n    format: keagn-form\n    description: Key generation settings.\n  keagv:\n    prefix: KEAGV\n    format: keagv-form\n    description: Constraint semantics and business meaning.\n  kearf:\n    prefix: KEARF\n    format: kearf-form\n    description: Foreign-key reference and cascade behavior.\n  msgkr:\n    prefix: MSGKR\n    subsection-types:\n      msgke-mkey-lst:\n        max-count: 1\n    description: Message key registry — the single author-copy-once home for user-facing\n  rslte:\n    prefix: RSLTE\n    subsection-types:\n      rsfde-fldd-lst:\n        max-count: 1\n    description: "Result envelope — the canonical CE-ER `codespecs_mapping.md` §7 contract."\n  schmg:\n    prefix: SCHMG\n    subsection-types:\n      migtg-targ-lst:\n        max-count: 1\n      scmst-step-lst:\n        max-count: 1\n    description: "Schema versioning and migration — the CE-MG home: the versioning policy,"\n  svopr:\n    prefix: SVOPR\n    subsection-types:\n      svope-oper-lst:\n        max-count: 1\n    description: "Server operation registry — the system\'s own operation surface (CE-API):"\n  dadi:\n    prefix: DADI\n    description: Data dictionary.\n  inco:\n    prefix: INCO\n    description: Integrity constraints.\n  ltec:\n    prefix: LTEC\n    format: ltec-form\n    description: Transition conditions and guarantees.\n  ltee:\n    prefix: LTEE\n    format: ltee-form\n    description: "Actions, actors, and rollback handling."\n  ltet:\n    prefix: LTET\n    format: ltet-form\n    description: Triggering event details.\n  ooee:\n    prefix: OOEE\n    format: ooee-form\n    description: Execution contract for this operation.\n  ooeg:\n    prefix: OOEG\n    format: ooeg-form\n    description: Authorization and usage boundaries.\n  ooel:\n    prefix: OOEL\n    format: ooel-form\n    description: State and event lifecycle details.\n  vaco:\n    prefix: VACO\n    description: Validation constraints.\nform-types:\n  daent-iden-form:\n    fields:\n      - fieldname: entityName\n        required: true\n        description: "Singular noun or noun phrase (e.g., Customer, OrderItem)"\n      - fieldname: tableName\n        description: Database table name if different from logical name\n      - fieldname: entityAlias\n        description: "Short alias for diagrams and references (e.g., CUST, ORD)"\n      - fieldname: description\n        description: Clear definition of what this entity represents\n      - fieldname: entityStereoType\n        description: "Entity pattern: Entity | ValueObject | Event | View | Bridge. Aggregate-root-ness is not a stereotype here — it is read from aggregateRoot below, which is the only field that states it"\n  daent-clas-form:\n    fields:\n      - fieldname: category\n        description: "Data category: MasterData | TransactionData | ReferenceData | ConfigurationData | AuditData"\n      - fieldname: boundedContext\n        description: "Context Name of the bounded context this entity belongs to. This is the outer bound on service-unit grouping: aggregates in different contexts are never served by one service unit"\n      - fieldname: aggregateRoot\n        required: true\n        description: "Entity Name of the root of the aggregate this entity belongs to — a root names itself, so an entity with no enclosing aggregate names its own Entity Name. This is the ownership key: the service unit that owns the aggregate owns this entity, its repository, and every operation that primarily writes it"\n      - fieldname: serviceUnitAggregate\n        description: "Only when business-process cohesion overrides the default grouping: Entity Name of the aggregate root whose service unit serves this entity. Several aggregates naming one root is a merge; one aggregate whose entities name different roots is a split. Empty means the aggregate named above"\n      - fieldname: owningDomain\n        description: Business domain responsible for this entity\n      - fieldname: dataOwner\n        description: Role or team accountable for data quality\n      - fieldname: dataSteward\n        description: Person or role responsible for data governance\n      - fieldname: sourceSystem\n        description: System of record or originating system for migration\n  daent-life-form:\n    fields:\n      - fieldname: lifecyclePhases\n        description: "Phases: Active → Archived → Purged, or Active → Soft-deleted → Hard-deleted"\n      - fieldname: retentionPolicy\n        description: "How long data is retained and why (e.g., 7 years per tax regulations)"\n      - fieldname: archivalTrigger\n        description: "Condition for moving to archive (e.g., 2 years after last activity)"\n      - fieldname: archivalDestination\n        description: "Where archived data goes: ColdStorage | Archive | DataLake"\n      - fieldname: purgePolicy\n        description: When and how data is permanently deleted\n      - fieldname: anonymizationPolicy\n        description: "PII anonymization rules (e.g., hash email after deletion)"\n      - fieldname: auditRequirements\n        description: "What changes must be tracked: None | KeyFields | AllFields | FullHistory"\n      - fieldname: auditRetention\n        description: How long audit records are kept\n  daent-rela-form:\n    fields:\n      - fieldname: parentEntities\n        description: "Entities this depends on (e.g., Order depends on Customer)"\n      - fieldname: childEntities\n        description: "Entities that depend on this (e.g., OrderItem depends on Order)"\n      - fieldname: referencedEntities\n        description: "Lookup/reference entities used (e.g., OrderStatus, PaymentMethod)"\n      - fieldname: crossDomainRelationships\n        description: Relationships that cross bounded context boundaries\n  daatt-iden-form:\n    fields:\n      - fieldname: columnName\n        description: "Database column name if different (e.g., snake_case)"\n      - fieldname: description\n        description: Clear definition of what this attribute represents\n      - fieldname: businessTerm\n        description: Business glossary term this maps to\n      - fieldname: exampleValues\n        description: "Comma-separated examples (e.g., \\"Draft, Confirmed, Shipped\\")"\n  daatt-data-form:\n    fields:\n      - fieldname: dataType\n        description: The logical type — selects the promoted options subsection.\n      - fieldname: physicalType\n        description: "Database type: VARCHAR(255), BIGINT, DECIMAL(10,2), TIMESTAMP"\n      - fieldname: format\n        description: "Display or storage format (e.g., YYYY-MM-DD, E.164 for phone)"\n  daatt-dttx-form:\n    fields:\n      - fieldname: length\n        description: Maximum character length\n      - fieldname: collation\n        description: "Character collation for text (e.g., utf8_general_ci)"\n  daatt-dtnu-form:\n    fields:\n      - fieldname: precision\n        description: Total digits for numeric types\n      - fieldname: scale\n        description: Decimal places for numeric types\n  daatt-dttm-form:\n    fields:\n      - fieldname: timezone\n        description: "For datetime: UTC | Local | WithOffset"\n  daatt-dtbi-form:\n    fields:\n      - fieldname: maxSizeBytes\n        description: Maximum stored size in bytes\n  daatt-dtfr-form:\n    fields:\n      - fieldname: storageGroup\n        required: true\n        description: Naming group the files are filed under — sets their retention and access partition (e.g. documents/attachment)\n      - fieldname: fileStore\n        description: Name of the configured file store holding the files; empty means the deployment default store\n      - fieldname: deleteWithRecord\n        description: "Yes | No — whether deleting the record also deletes the file (Yes unless the file outlives its reference by design)"\n      - fieldname: acceptedContentKinds\n        description: "Comma-separated content kinds accepted on upload (e.g. PDF, PNG); empty means unrestricted"\n      - fieldname: defaultContentKind\n        description: Content kind recorded when an upload declares none\n      - fieldname: maxFileSizeBytes\n        description: Maximum accepted file size in bytes\n  daatt-dten-form:\n    fields:\n      - fieldname: domainEnum\n        required: true\n        description: "DomainEnumEntry.enumName this attribute is typed by (e.g. OrderStatus) — declared once in the domain enum register, not restated here"\n  daatt-deri-form:\n    fields:\n      - fieldname: isComputed\n        description: "Whether value is computed: Yes | No"\n      - fieldname: computeFormula\n        description: Formula or expression for computed fields\n      - fieldname: isDerived\n        description: "Whether derived from other attributes: Yes | No"\n      - fieldname: derivationLogic\n        description: How derived value is calculated\n  daatt-secu-form:\n    fields:\n      - fieldname: sensitivityLevel\n        description: "Public | Internal | Confidential | Restricted | PII | PHI"\n      - fieldname: isPii\n        description: "Personally identifiable information: Yes | No"\n      - fieldname: maskingRule\n        description: "How to mask in logs/displays: None | Partial | Full | Hash"\n      - fieldname: encryptionLevel\n        description: "Field-level encryption: None | Encrypted | Tokenized"\n      - fieldname: auditLevel\n        description: "Change tracking: None | ValueChanges | FullHistory"\n  daatt-migr-form:\n    fields:\n      - fieldname: sourceSystem\n        description: Originating system for data lineage\n      - fieldname: sourceAttribute\n        description: Source field name for migration mapping\n      - fieldname: transformationRule\n        description: Transformation applied during migration/ETL\n      - fieldname: dataLineage\n        description: Upstream sources that feed this attribute\n      - fieldname: qualityRules\n        description: "Data quality checks (e.g., completeness, accuracy)"\n  keagn-form:\n    fields:\n      - fieldname: generationStrategy\n        description: "Auto | Sequence | UUID | ULID | Custom | Natural"\n      - fieldname: sequenceName\n        description: Database sequence name if applicable\n      - fieldname: isNaturalKey\n        description: "Whether key has business meaning: Yes | No"\n  kearf-form:\n    fields:\n      - fieldname: referencedEntity\n        description: "For foreign keys: target entity name"\n      - fieldname: referencedKey\n        description: "For foreign keys: target key/column name"\n      - fieldname: onDeleteAction\n        description: "Cascade | SetNull | Restrict | NoAction | SetDefault"\n      - fieldname: onUpdateAction\n        description: "Cascade | SetNull | Restrict | NoAction | SetDefault"\n  keagv-form:\n    fields:\n      - fieldname: deferrable\n        description: "Whether constraint check can be deferred: Yes | No"\n  enrle-iden-form:\n    fields:\n      - fieldname: relationshipType\n        description: "Association | Aggregation | Composition | Generalization | Dependency"\n      - fieldname: description\n        description: Business meaning of this relationship\n      - fieldname: businessJustification\n        description: Why this relationship exists from business perspective\n      - fieldname: implementationType\n        description: "ForeignKey | JunctionTable | Embedded | Reference"\n  enrle-card-form:\n    fields:\n      - fieldname: sourceCardinality\n        description: "Source side: 1 | 0..1 | 0..* | 1..* | n..m"\n      - fieldname: targetCardinality\n        description: "Target side: 1 | 0..1 | 0..* | 1..* | n..m"\n      - fieldname: sourceParticipation\n        description: "Mandatory | Optional (whether source must participate)"\n      - fieldname: targetParticipation\n        description: "Mandatory | Optional (whether target must participate)"\n      - fieldname: minSourceInstances\n        description: Minimum number of source entity instances\n      - fieldname: maxTargetInstances\n        description: Maximum number of related target instances\n  enrle-refe-form:\n    fields:\n      - fieldname: onDeleteAction\n        description: "Cascade | SetNull | Restrict | NoAction | SetDefault | Archive"\n      - fieldname: onUpdateAction\n        description: "Cascade | SetNull | Restrict | NoAction"\n      - fieldname: enforcementLevel\n        description: "Database | Application | Both | None"\n      - fieldname: isDeferrable\n        description: "Whether constraint check can be deferred: Yes | No"\n      - fieldname: cascadeScope\n        description: "For cascading: DirectOnly | AllDescendants | Custom"\n      - fieldname: orphanHandling\n        description: "How orphaned records are handled: Prevent | Allow | AssignDefault"\n  enrle-navi-form:\n    fields:\n      - fieldname: navigability\n    