s may shadow it. Never write the value: it is supplied per deployment, and a secret-bearing setting declares only its presence and shape, never its content. Typical keys: server.host, server.port, server.isolateCount, log.level, database.migrationsDirectory, tls.privateKey, jwt.rsaPrivateKey. This list is the only place a secret may be declared: the security, encryption, key-management and audit-sink policy sections name their own settings and carry values only, so a credential they need — a remote log sink password, a KMS access key — is authored here as its own entry."\n  se-slos-lst:\n    prefix: SE_SLOS_LST\n    subsection-types:\n      se-slos:\n        max-count: infinite\n    min-text-length: 0\n    max-text-length: 0\n    description: Add one entry per SLO.\n  secrq-requ:\n    prefix: SECRQ_REQU_\n    subsection-types:\n      sereencl:\n        max-count: 1\n      sereenco:\n        max-count: 1\n      srev:\n        max-count: 1\n      sereenst:\n        max-count: 1\n      rac:\n        max-count: 1\n      seco:\n        max-count: 1\n      reqdep:\n        max-count: 1\n      rt:\n        max-count: 1\n    pattern-check-id:\n      pattern: ^SECRQ-REQU-.+\$\n      error-message: IDs of this section must match SECRQ-REQU-xxx\n    description: Add one entry per security requirement.\n  shien-item:\n    prefix: SHIEN_ITEM_\n    subsection-types:\n      sier:\n        max-count: 1\n      siec:\n        max-count: 1\n      sieo:\n        max-count: 1\n    pattern-check-id:\n      pattern: ^SHIEN-ITEM-.+\$\n      error-message: IDs of this section must match SHIEN-ITEM-xxx\n    description: "Add one entry per shared infrastructure component (e.g. a database cluster, message broker, identity provider). Capture its criticality, resilience, and the systems that depend on it."\n  shlcp-shar:\n    prefix: SHLCP_SHAR_\n    subsection-types:\n      slced:\n        max-count: 1\n      slcet:\n        max-count: 1\n      slceq:\n        max-count: 1\n      slceo:\n      