t of Work, CQRS, Event Sourcing\n      - **Concurrency**: Thread Pool, Producer-Consumer, Async/Await patterns\n      - **Integration**: API Gateway, Circuit Breaker, Retry, Bulkhead\n      **Coding Standards**:\n      - Language-specific style guides (PEP 8, Google Style, Airbnb)\n      - Naming conventions and code organization\n      - Documentation requirements (doc comments, README standards)\n      - Testing requirements (unit, integration, e2e coverage targets)\n      - Code review checklist and approval criteria\n      **Industry Standards**:\n      - **Security**: OWASP Top 10, OWASP ASVS, CWE\n      - **Quality**: ISO/IEC 25010, CMMI\n      - **Documentation**: IEEE 830, ISO/IEC 26514\n      - **Process**: ISO 27001, SOC 2, GDPR, HIPAA\n      **Enforcement**: Linters, static analysis, automated checks in CI/CD.\n  dpch:\n    prefix: DPCH\n    format: dpch-form\n    description: Handling rules.\n  dpci:\n    prefix: DPCI\n    format: dpci-form\n    description: Incident handling.\n  dpcm:\n    prefix: DPCM\n    format: dpcm-form\n    description: Masking and de-identification rules.\n  dpcr:\n    prefix: DPCR\n    format: dpcr-form\n    description: Retention and disposal rules.\n  dpea:\n    prefix: DPEA\n    format: dpea-form\n    description: Applicability guidance.\n  dpec:\n    prefix: DPEC\n    format: dpec-form\n    description: Context and timing information.\n  dpee:\n    prefix: DPEE\n    format: dpee-form\n    description: Enforcement and notes.\n  dpef:\n    prefix: DPEF\n    format: dpef-form\n    description: "Inputs, outputs, and participant flow."\n  dpei:\n    prefix: DPEI\n    format: dpei-form\n    description: Implementation guidance.\n  dpeo:\n    prefix: DPEO\n    format: dpeo-form\n    description: Operating cadence and coordination details.\n  dper:\n    prefix: DPER\n    subsection-types:\n      doe-opti-lst:\n        max-count: 1\n    description: Resolution details (filled when decided).\n  dpes:\n    prefix: DPES\n    format: dpe