 **Monitoring and Alerting**: Release/DevOps deployment-pipeline\n        observability — build/deploy health, pipeline alerts, release gates,\n        rollback triggers\n      - **Maintenance Windows**: Scheduled maintenance, emergency procedures,\n        change management, user communication\n      **Ownership boundary**: This section owns *release/DevOps* concerns. The\n      *runtime* operational monitoring (health checks, runtime metrics, SLA/SLO\n      tracking, dashboards, on-call, incident management) is owned by SBP.8.7\n      `SystemOperationAndMonitoring` (runtime SRE) — reference it, do not\n      restate it here.\n      **DevOps/SRE Principles**:\n      - Automation over manual processes\n      - Immutable infrastructure\n      - Everything as code (IaC, GitOps)\n      - Blameless postmortems\n      - Continuous improvement\n      **Operational Metrics**:\n      - MTTR (Mean Time To Recovery)\n      - MTBF (Mean Time Between Failures)\n      - Change failure rate\n      - Deployment frequency\n      - Lead time for changes\n      **Reference**: Google SRE book, DORA metrics, ITIL practices.\n  orec:\n    prefix: OREC\n    format: orec-form\n    description: Requirement classification and source.\n  orei:\n    prefix: OREI\n    format: orei-form\n    description: Impact and change profile.\n  oren:\n    prefix: OREN\n    subsection-types:\n      oren-orga:\n        max-count: 1\n      orenma:\n        max-count: 1\n      oedm:\n        max-count: 1\n      ade-affe-lst:\n        max-count: 1\n      dme-deci-lst:\n        max-count: 1\n      oren-cult-lst:\n        max-count: 1\n      oren-comm-lst:\n        max-count: 1\n      oren-chan-lst:\n        max-count: 1\n    description: 4.6.1. Organizational Environment.\n  orep:\n    prefix: OREP\n    format: orep-form\n    description: "Planning, ownership, and success tracking."\n  orgf:\n    prefix: ORGF\n    subsection-types:\n      norgs:\n        max-count: 1\n      jdas:\n        max-count: 1\n      wpde-work-lst:\n        max-count: 1\n        min-count: 1\n    description: Target organizational structure and roles.\n  orip:\n    prefix: ORIP\n    subsection-types:\n      orip-plan:\n        max-count: 1\n      orgim-acti-lst:\n        max-count: 1\n    description: Define the implementation approach for this organizational change requirement.\n  otec:\n    prefix: OTEC\n    format: otec-form\n    description: Content maintenance.\n  otes:\n    prefix: OTES\n    format: otes-form\n    description: Scheduling and delivery.\n  pacp:\n    prefix: PACP\n    subsection-types:\n      prp:\n        max-count: 1\n      psp:\n        max-count: 1\n      plp:\n        max-count: 1\n      alp:\n        max-count: 1\n      crp:\n        max-count: 1\n      ccdp:\n        max-count: 1\n      sacp:\n        max-count: 1\n      mfacrq-mfac-lst:\n        max-count: 1\n    description: 9.2.3. Password and Credential Policy.\n  paor:\n    prefix: PAOR\n    subsection-types:\n      paorst:\n        max-count: 1\n      paorty:\n        max-count: 1\n      paorde:\n        max-count: 1\n      paordo:\n        max-count: 1\n    description: Package organization and structure.\n  pass:\n    prefix: PASS\n    subsection-types:\n      pe-prot-lst:\n        max-count: 1\n      tlre:\n        max-count: 1\n      cema:\n        max-count: 1\n      apvest:\n        max-count: 1\n      mefost:\n        max-count: 1\n      ralipo:\n        max-count: 1\n      prcore:\n        max-count: 1\n    description: |\n      Specify communication protocols, security standards, and API conventions.\n      Standardized protocols ensure interoperability and security.\n      **Network Protocols**:\n      - **Application Layer**: HTTP/1.1, HTTP/2, HTTP/3 (QUIC), gRPC, WebSocket\n      - **Transport**: TCP, UDP, QUIC\n      - **Security**: TLS 1.2/1.3, DTLS, SSH\n      **API Protocols**:\n      - **REST**: Resource-based, HTTP verbs, JSON/XML\n      - **GraphQL**: Query language, single endpoint, flexible queries\n      - **gRPC**: Binary protocol, Protocol Buffers, streaming support\n      - **WebSocket**: Full-duplex, real-time, persistent connection\n      **TLS/SSL Requirements**:\n      - Minimum TLS version (TLS 1.2 or 1.3)\n      - Cipher suites (AEAD, perfect forward secrecy)\n      - Certificate requirements (CA-signed, validity period)\n      - Certificate pinning considerations\n      **Certificate Management**:\n      - Certificate lifecycle (issuance, renewal, revocation)\n      - Automated certificate management (cert-manager, Let\'s Encrypt)\n      - Certificate monitoring and alerting\n      - Key rotation procedures\n      **API Versioning Strategy**:\n      - URL versioning (/v1/, /v2/)\n      - Header versioning (Accept-Version)\n      - Content negotiation (media type)\n      - Deprecation and sunset policies\n  pceo:\n    prefix: PCEO\n    format: pceo-form\n    description: Control operation and ownership.\n  pcev:\n    prefix: PCEV\n    format: pcev-form\n    description: "Evidence, testing, and failure handling."\n  pcrc:\n    prefix: PCRC\n    format: pcrc-form\n    description: Caching requirements.\n  pcre:\n    prefix: PCRE\n    format: pcre-form\n    description: "Webhook, event, and health endpoint standards."\n  pcro:\n    prefix: PCRO\n    format: pcro-form\n    description: Request logging and trace propagation rules.\n  peea:\n    prefix: PEEA\n    format: peea-form\n    description: "Likelihood, impact, and detection."\n  peef:\n    prefix: PEEF\n    subsection-types:\n      peef-perf:\n        max-count: 1\n      efqu:\n        max-count: 1\n    description: 11.3. Performance Efficiency (ISO/IEC 25010:2023).\n  peer:\n    prefix: PEER\n    format: peer-form\n    description: Resolution and prevention approach.\n  pfsf:\n    prefix: PFSF\n    format: pfsf-form\n    description: Fidelity expectations for the prototype.\n  pfss:\n    prefix: PFSS\n    format: pfss-form\n    description: Included and excluded feature scope.\n  pgro:\n   