icError — response to invalid credentials (generic preferred)"\n      - fieldname: accountLockoutThreshold\n        description: "Number of failed attempts before lockout (e.g., 5, 10, configurable)"\n      - fieldname: lockoutDuration\n        description: "Duration of lockout (e.g., 15min, 30min, progressive, permanent)"\n      - fieldname: lockoutEscalation\n        description: "Fixed | Progressive | Exponential — whether lockout duration increases"\n      - fieldname: bruteForceProtection\n        description: "RateLimiting | CAPTCHA | IPBlock | AccountLock — brute-force mitigation"\n      - fieldname: credentialStuffingProtection\n        description: "BreachDatabase | DeviceFingerprint | BehaviorAnalysis | None"\n      - fieldname: userNotificationOnFailure\n        description: "Yes | No — whether users are notified of failed login attempts"\n      - fieldname: adminAlertThreshold\n        description: "Number of failures before admin alert (e.g., 10, 50, per-minute rate)"\n      - fieldname: failedLoginAuditLogging\n        description: "Yes | No — whether failed login attempts are logged for audit"\n      - fieldname: suspiciousActivityResponse\n        description: "RequireMFA | TemporaryBlock | CAPTCHA | ManualReview — response to anomalies"\n      - fieldname: gracefulDegradation\n        description: "Behavior when authentication service is partially unavailable (queue, fallback, deny)"\n  suap-form:\n    fields:\n      - fieldname: stepUpEnabled\n        description: "Yes | No — whether step-up authentication is implemented"\n      - fieldname: stepUpTriggers\n        description: "HighRiskOperation | SensitiveDataAccess | AdminAction | PaymentApproval | SettingsChange"\n      - fieldname: stepUpTargetAal\n        description: "AAL2 | AAL3 — target assurance level for step-up authentication"\n      - fieldname: stepUpTimeout\n        description: "Duration the elevated session lasts (e.g., 5min, 15min, transaction-scoped)"\n      - fieldname: riskBasedAuthEnabled\n        description: "Yes | No — whether risk signals influence authentication requirements"\n      - fieldname: riskSignals\n        description: "GeoLocation | IPReputation | DeviceFingerprint | BehaviorPattern | TimeOfDay"\n      - fieldname: riskScoringMethod\n        description: "RuleBased | MachineLearning | Hybrid — how risk scores are computed"\n      - fieldname: lowRiskAction\n        description: "AllowSilently | NormalAuth — response to low-risk signals"\n      - fieldname: mediumRiskAction\n        description: "RequireMFA | AdditionalVerification — response to medium-risk signals"\n      - fieldname: highRiskAction\n        description: "Block | RequirePhishingResistant | ManualReview — response to high-risk signals"\n      - fieldname: adaptiveAuthProvider\n        description: "Built-in | Third-party service name — provider of adaptive authentication"\n      - fieldname: continuousAuthEnabled\n        description: "Yes | No — whether session is continuously monitored for risk changes"\n  lfsev-form:\n    fields:\n      - fieldname: inputRequired\n        description: "Username | Password | OTP | BiometricSample | ConsentApproval | None"\n      - fieldname: validationAction\n        description: "CredentialVerification | TokenValidation | RiskAssessment | MfaVerification | None"\n      - fieldname: timeoutSeconds\n        description: "Maximum time allowed for this step (e.g., 300, 600)"\n  lfseb-form:\n    fields:\n      - fieldname: successOutcome\n        description: "NextStep | TokenIssued | SessionCreated | RedirectToApp — outcome on success"\n      - fieldname: failureOutcome\n        description: "RetryWithError | Lockout | RedirectToError | AbortFlow — outcome on failure"\n      - fieldname: conditionalTrigger\n        description: "The condition under which this step runs, if it is not unconditional (e.g. MFA required, new device). Leave empty for a step that always runs; a step that states a trigger is by that fact the one that can be skipped."\n  lfsep-form:\n    fields:\n      - fieldname: protocolMessage\n        description: "OAuth2 AuthZ Request | Token Request | SAML AuthnRequest | OIDC Userinfo — protocol-level message"\n      - fieldname: description\n        description: Detailed description of what happens in this step\n  prp-form:\n    fields:\n      - fieldname: minimumLengthSingleFactor\n        description: "Minimum password length when used as single factor (NIST: 15 characters)"\n      - fieldname: minimumLengthMultiFactor\n        description: "Minimum password length when used as part of MFA (NIST: 8 characters)"\n      - fieldname: maximumLength\n        description: "Maximum allowed password length (NIST: at least 64 characters)"\n      - fieldname: allowedCharacterSets\n        description: "ASCII | Unicode | ASCIIPlusSpace — character sets accepted in passwords"\n      - fieldname: compositionRulesEnforced\n        description: "Yes | No — whether mixed-case/digit/symbol rules are enforced (NIST: No)"\n      - fieldname: passphraseSupported\n        description: "Yes | No — whether multi-word passphrases with spaces are supported"\n      - fieldname: unicodeNormalization\n        description: "NFC | NFD | None — Unicode normalization form applied before hashing"\n      - fieldname: passwordBlocklistEnabled\n        description: "Yes | No — whether passwords are compared against a blocklist"\n      - fieldname: blocklistSources\n        description: "BreachCorpus | DictionaryWords | ContextSpecific | HaveIBeenPwned — sources for blocklist"\n      - fieldname: passwordStrengthMeter\n        description: "Yes | No — whether a real-time strength indicator is displayed during creation"\n      - fieldname: passwordHintsAllowed\n        description: "Yes | No — whether password hints are stored (NIST: No)"\n      - fieldname: securityQuestionsAllowed\n        description: "Yes | No — whether KBA/security questions are used (NIST: No)"\n      - fieldname: showPasswordOption\n        description: "Yes | No — whether users can toggle password visibility during entry"\n      - fieldname: passwordManagerSupport\n        description: "Yes | No — whether autofill and paste are supported for password entry"\n      - fieldname: truncationPolicy\n        description: "None | Trim — whether leading/trailing whitespace is trimmed (NIST: verify entire password)"\n      - fieldname: typoTolerancePolicy\n        description: "None | CaseFirstChar | TrimWhitespace — whether minor typo corrections are attempted"\n  psp-form:\n    fields:\n      - fieldname: hashingAlgorithm\n        description: "Argon2id | bcrypt | scrypt | PBKDF2 — password hashing algorithm"\n      - fieldname: hashingCostFactor\n        description: "Work factor/iteration count for the hashing algorithm (e.g., bcrypt cost 12)"\n      - fieldname: costFactorReviewSchedule\n        description: "Annual | Biannual | OnHardwareUpgrade — when cost factor is re-evaluated"\n      - fieldname: saltLength\n        description: "Minimum salt length in bits (NIST: at least 32 bits)"\n      - fieldname: saltGeneration\n        description: "CryptoRandom | CSPRNG — method for generating salt values"\n      - fieldname: pepperEnabled\n        description: "Yes | No — whether a server-side secret key (pepper) is used for additional hashing"\n      - fieldname: pepperStorage\n        description: "HSM | TEE | EncryptedConfig | SecretManager — where the pepper key is stored"\n      - fieldname: hashVersioning\n        description: "Yes | No — whether the hash algorithm and cost factor are stored per password for migration"\n      - fieldname: transmissionEncryption\n        description: "TLS1.3 | TLS1.2 — encryption for password transmission"\n      - fieldname: clientSideHashing\n        description: "Yes | No — whether passwords are pre-hashed on the client before transmission"\n      - fieldname: memoryHardFunction\n        description: "Yes | No — whether the hashing function is memory-hard to resist GPU attacks"\n      - fieldname: outputLength\n        description: Hash output length in bits (should match underlying scheme output length)\n  plp-form:\n    fields:\n      - fieldname: periodicRotationRequired\n        description: "Yes | No — whether periodic password changes are required (NIST: No)"\n      - fieldname: rotationPeriod\n        description: "If rotation is required: period in days (e.g., 90, 180, 365)"\n      - fieldname: forceChangeOnCompromise\n        description: "Yes | No — whether password change is forced on evidence of compromise"\n      - fieldname: passwordHistoryDepth\n        description: "Number of previous passwords stored to prevent reuse (e.g., 0, 5, 12, 24)"\n      - fieldname: minimumPasswordAge\n        description: "Minimum time before a password can be changed again (e.g., 0, 1d) to prevent rapid cycling"\n      - fieldname: initialPasswordPolicy\n        description: "SystemGenerated | UserChosen | TemporaryWithForceChange — policy for initial passwords"\n      - fieldname: temporaryPasswordExpiry\n        description: "Duration before a temporary/initial password expires (e.g., 24h, 72h)"\n      - fieldname: passwordExpiryWarning\n        description: "Number of days before expiry that users are warned (e.g., 14, 30)"\n      - fieldname: passwordChangeNotification\n        description: "Yes | No — whether users are notified when their password is changed"\n      - fieldname: passwordChangeRequiresCurrent\n        description: "Yes | No — whether current password must be verified before setting a new one"\n      - fieldname: administratorResetPolicy\n        description: "TemporaryPassword | ResetLink | MfaVerification — how admins reset user passwords"\n      - fieldname: passwordInactivityDisable\n        description: "Duration of inactivity before account is disabled (e.g., 90d, 180d, Never)"\n  alp-form:\n    fields:\n      - fieldname: lockoutThreshold\n        description: "Number of consecutive failed attempts before lockout (NIST max: 100, typical: 5-10)"\n      - fieldname: lockoutDuration\n        description: "Duration of lockout (e.g., 15min, 30min, UntilAdminUnlock, Progressive)"\n      - fieldname: lockoutEscalation\n        description: "Fixed | Progressive | Exponential — whether lockout duration increases"\n      - fieldname: rateLimitingMethod\n        description: "Delay | CAPTCHA | Lockout | IPBlock | Combination — rate-limiting strategy"\n      - fieldname: delayProgression\n        description: "Delay schedule for progressive throttling (e.g., 30s after 3rd, 1min after 5th)"\n      - fieldname: captchaTriggerThreshold\n        description: Number of failed attempts before CAPTCHA is required\n      - fieldname: ipBasedRateLimiting\n        description: "Yes | No — whether rate limiting also applies per IP address"\n      - fieldname: distributedAttackProtection\n        description: "Yes | No — whether protection against credential stuffing across IPs is implemented"\n      - fieldname: unlockMechanism\n        description: "TimeBasedAutoUnlock | AdminUnlock | SelfServiceWithMFA | EmailVerification"\n      - fieldname: failedAttemptResetOnSuccess\n        description: "Yes | No — whether the failed attempt counter resets after successful login"\n      - fieldname: lockoutNotification\n        description: "User | Admin | Both | None — who is notified when lockout occurs"\n      - fieldname: permanentLockoutEnabled\n        description: "Yes | No — whether accounts are permanently locked after extreme abuse"\n      - fieldname: permanentLockoutThreshold\n        description: "Number of lockout cycles before permanent lock (e.g., 5, 10)"\n  crp-form:\n    fields:\n      - fieldname: passwordResetMethod\n        description: "EmailLink | SMSCode | SecurityQuestions | MfaVerification | AdminAssisted — how users reset passwords"\n      - fieldname: resetLinkExpiry\n        description: "Duration before a password reset link expires (e.g., 15min, 1h, 24h)"\n      - fieldname: resetLinkSingleUse\n        description: "Yes | No — whether reset links can only be used once"\n      - fieldname: resetRateLimiting\n        description: "Requests per period allowed (e.g., 3 per hour, 5 per day)"\n      - fieldname: savedRecoveryCodesEnabled\n        description: "Yes | No — whether one-time recovery codes are provided at enrollment"\n      - fieldname: recoveryCodeCount\n        description: "Number of recovery codes generated (e.g., 8, 10, 16)"\n      - fieldname: recoveryCodeFormat\n        description: "AlphaNumeric | NumericOnly | Words — format of recovery codes"\n      - fieldname: issuedRecoveryCodeChannels\n        description: "Email | SMS | PostalMail | InPerson — channels for sending issued recovery codes"\n      - fieldname: recoveryCodeExpiry\n        description: "Duration before issued recovery codes expire (NIST: 10min SMS, 24h email)"\n      - fieldname: identityReverificationRequired\n        description: "Yes | No — whether identity re-verification is required for recovery at higher AALs"\n      - fieldname: recoveryContactEnabled\n        description: "Yes | No — whether a trusted contact can initiate recovery"\n      - fieldname: multipleRecoveryAddresses\n        description: "Yes | No — whether subscribers can register multiple recovery addresses (NIST: at least 2)"\n      - fieldname: recoveryAuditLogging\n        description: "Yes | No — whether all recovery attempts are logged for audit"\n  ccdp-form:\n    fields:\n      - fieldname: breachDatabaseMonitoring\n        description: "Yes | No — whether passwords are checked against known breach databases"\n      - fieldname: breachDatabaseSource\n        description: "HaveIBeenPwned | Internal | CommercialFeed | Multiple — source of breach data"\n      - fieldname: breachCheckFrequency\n        description: "AtCreation | AtLogin | Periodic | RealTime — when breach checks are performed"\n      - fieldname: compromisedCredentialAction\n        description: "